        'bible-character-quest-l17-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        17,
        4,
        'Which royal title and name belonged to the queen of the Ethiopians whose chief court treasurer was baptized by Philip on the desert road?',
        '"Athaliah","Vashti","Tahpenes","Candace"'::text[],
        'Candace',
        'Philip met an Ethiopian eunuch of great authority under Candace, queen of the Ethiopians, who had charge of all her royal treasury.',
        'Acts 8:27',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Thrones and Bloodlines","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"thrones-bloodlines","mechanic":"thrones-bloodlines","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was sovereign queen over an ancient African empire.","My royal official traveled thousands of miles to worship in Jerusalem.","My chief treasurer was converted through Isaiah''s prophecy on the road to Gaza."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l17-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        17,
        5,
        'Which queen mother (Gebirah) of Judah was stripped of her royal dignity by King Asa because she had erected an abominable image for Asherah?',
        '"Athaliah","Maakah","Naamah","Azubah"'::text[],
        'Maakah',
        'King Asa removed his grandmother Maakah from being queen mother because she had made an abominable image for Asherah, which Asa cut down and burned.',
        '1 Kings 15:13',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Thrones and Bloodlines","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"thrones-bloodlines","mechanic":"thrones-bloodlines","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I held the prestigious court title of Queen Mother in Judah.","I worshipped pagan idols and set up an Asherah image.","My grandson Asa dethroned me and crushed my idolatrous pole."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l18-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        18,
        1,
        'Which military commander seized the throne of the northern kingdom of Israel and reigned for only seven days in Tirzah before setting fire to the palace over himself?',
        '"Tibni","Elah","Zimri","Shallum"'::text[],
        'Zimri',
        'Zimri reigned seven days in Tirzah; when Omri''s army besieged the city, Zimri went into the royal palace citadel and burned it down around himself.',
        '1 Kings 16:15-18',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Divided Kingdom","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"divided-kingdom","mechanic":"divided-kingdom","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I assassinated King Elah while he was drinking himself drunk.","My reign was the shortest in Israel''s history—just one week.","When the capital fell to Omri, I perished in my own burning palace."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l18-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        18,
        2,
        'Which son of Herod the Great ruled over Judea after Herod''s death, whose cruel reputation caused Joseph to avoid Judea and take Jesus to Galilee?',
        '"Archelaus","Herod Antipas","Herod Philip","Lysanias"'::text[],
        'Archelaus',
        'When Joseph heard that Archelaus was reigning over Judea in place of his father Herod, he was afraid to go there and settled in Nazareth.',
        'Matthew 2:22',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Divided Kingdom","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"divided-kingdom","mechanic":"divided-kingdom","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was designated ethnarch of Judea, Samaria, and Idumea.","My brutality at Passover resulted in thousands of deaths.","Joseph steered the holy family away from my territory to Galilee."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l18-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        18,
        3,
        'Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch?',
        '"Tibni son of Ginath","Elah","Nadab","Pekah"'::text[],
        'Tibni son of Ginath',
        'Half the people of Israel followed Tibni son of Ginath to make him king, and half followed Omri; Omri prevailed and Tibni died.',
        '1 Kings 16:21-22',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Divided Kingdom","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"divided-kingdom","mechanic":"divided-kingdom","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["Half the northern tribes chose me as their monarch.","I waged civil war against General Omri for control of the kingdom.","After four years of struggle I died, leaving Omri undisputed king."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l18-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        18,
        4,
        'Which king of Judah ruled for 52 years and prospered greatly, but was struck with leprosy in the temple after arrogantly trying to burn incense?',
        '"Jotham","Asa","Amaziah","Uzziah (Azariah)"'::text[],
        'Uzziah (Azariah)',
        'Uzziah grew proud and entered the sanctuary to burn incense; 80 brave priests opposed him, and leprosy broke out on his forehead.',
        '2 Chronicles 26:16-21',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Divided Kingdom","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"divided-kingdom","mechanic":"divided-kingdom","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a military innovator and builder who reigned for 52 years.","I intruded into the holy sanctuary to perform the duty of Aaron''s sons.","God struck my forehead with leprosy, forcing me into quarantine until death."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l18-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        18,
        5,
        'Which regional ruler was tetrarch of Abilene during the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, as recorded in Luke''s historical synchronization?',
        '"Quirinius","Lysanias","Festus","Archelaus"'::text[],
        'Lysanias',
        'Luke 3:1 identifies Lysanias as tetrarch of Abilene alongside Pontius Pilate of Judea and Herod Antipas of Galilee.',
        'Luke 3:1',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Divided Kingdom","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"divided-kingdom","mechanic":"divided-kingdom","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an imperial governor in the Syrian-Lebanon border region.","My territory was the district of Abilene.","Luke specifically dated the start of John the Baptist''s ministry by my rule."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l19-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        19,
        1,
        'Which royal supervisor of forced labor was dispatched by King Rehoboam to negotiate with the rebellious northern tribes, only to be stoned to death by all Israel?',
        '"Adoniram (Hadoram)","Shemaiah","Ahijah","Benaiah"'::text[],
        'Adoniram (Hadoram)',
        'Rehoboam foolishly sent Adoniram, taskmaster over forced labor, to the rebellious northern tribes, and all Israel stoned him to death.',
        '1 Kings 12:18',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Royal Mistakes","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"royal-mistakes","mechanic":"royal-mistakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the chief minister over royal conscript labor under David, Solomon, and Rehoboam.","My presence infuriated the already overtaxed northern tribes.","My mission ended instantly when the crowd stoned me to death."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l19-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        19,
        2,
        'Which ruler foolishly bound himself with an oath before banquet guests to grant a dancing girl anything, resulting in the beheading of John the Baptist?',
        '"Herod the Great","Herod Philip","Herod Antipas","Herod Agrippa I"'::text[],
        'Herod Antipas',
        'Herod Antipas the tetrarch made a rash oath to Salome and, because of his dinner guests, ordered John the Baptist beheaded in prison.',
        'Matthew 14:6-10',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Royal Mistakes","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"royal-mistakes","mechanic":"royal-mistakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I ruled Galilee and Perea as tetrarch.","I married my brother''s former wife Herodias.","A reckless birthday pledge compelled me to execute God''s greatest prophet."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l19-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        19,
        3,
        'Which king of Judah made the disastrous mistake of showing every treasure, storehouse, and weapon to envoys from Merodach-baladan king of Babylon?',
        '"Hezekiah","Josiah","Manasseh","Jehoshaphat"'::text[],
        'Hezekiah',
        'Hezekiah showed the Babylonian ambassadors all his royal armory and gold; Isaiah rebuked him and prophesied everything would be carried to Babylon.',
        '2 Kings 20:12-17',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Royal Mistakes","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"royal-mistakes","mechanic":"royal-mistakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I had just been miraculously healed from a fatal illness.","I received a friendly delegation from the prince of Babylon.","My prideful tour of the royal treasury sealed Judah''s future exile."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l19-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        19,
        4,
        'Which king donned magnificent royal robes, delivered an oration to the people of Tyre and Sidon, and was struck down and eaten by worms for not giving God the glory?',
        '"Herod the Great","Herod Agrippa I","Herod Agrippa II","Herod Antipas"'::text[],
        'Herod Agrippa I',
        'Herod Agrippa I accepted the crowd''s shout ''The voice of a god, not of a man!'' and an angel struck him down; he was eaten by worms and died.',
        'Acts 12:21-23',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Royal Mistakes","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"royal-mistakes","mechanic":"royal-mistakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I had earlier martyred James the apostle and imprisoned Peter.","The crowd flattered me shouting that my voice was divine.","I was immediately struck down by an angel and perished in agony."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l19-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        19,
        5,
        'Which Babylonian co-regent monarch held a blasphemous feast using sacred golden goblets plundered from Jerusalem, during which a detached hand wrote his doom on the wall?',
        '"Belshazzar","Darius the Mede","Evil-Merodach","Nebuchadnezzar"'::text[],
        'Belshazzar',
        'Belshazzar toasted idols using sacred temple cups; divine fingers wrote on the plaster wall, and he was slain that very night when Babylon fell.',
        'Daniel 5:1-5, 30',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"Royal Mistakes","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"royal-mistakes","mechanic":"royal-mistakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I hosted a lavish banquet for a thousand of my royal lords.","We drank wine from the sacred vessels stolen from the Lord''s house.","A mysterious hand wrote MENE, MENE, TEKEL, PARSIN, and my kingdom fell that night."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l20-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        20,
        1,
        'Which courageous high priest engineered the temple coup that overthrew Queen Athaliah, guarded the child Joash, and crowned him king at age seven?',
        '"Abiathar","Zadok","Hilkiah","Jehoiada"'::text[],
        'Jehoiada',
        'Jehoiada the high priest formed an armed alliance with the royal guards, brought out young Joash, crowned him, and gave him the testimony.',
        '2 Kings 11:4-12',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Kingmaker''s Trial","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"kingmakers-trial","mechanic":"kingmakers-trial","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the highest spiritual authority in Jerusalem.","I secretly raised the rightful Davidic heir in the temple courts.","I staged a synchronized military coup to place the crown on seven-year-old Joash."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l20-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        20,
        2,
        'Which monarch sat with Roman Governor Festus to hear Paul''s legal defense and famously interrupted: ''In a short time would you persuade me to be a Christian?''',
        '"Felix","Herod Agrippa I","Herod Agrippa II","Herod Antipas"'::text[],
        'Herod Agrippa II',
        'King Agrippa II (Marcus Julius Agrippa), great-grandson of Herod the Great, told Paul: ''Almost thou persuadest me to be a Christian.''',
        'Acts 26:28',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Kingmaker''s Trial","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"kingmakers-trial","mechanic":"kingmakers-trial","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the last king of the Herodian line.","I inspected Paul''s case alongside my sister Bernice and Festus.","I admitted Paul could have been freed had he not appealed to Caesar."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l20-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        20,
        3,
        'Which Shilonite prophet met Jeroboam outside Jerusalem, ripped his new garment into twelve pieces, and handed Jeroboam ten pieces to symbolize ten divided tribes?',
        '"Micaiah","Ahijah the Shilonite","Iddo the Seer","Shemaiah"'::text[],
        'Ahijah the Shilonite',
        'Ahijah tore his new cloak into twelve pieces and gave ten to Jeroboam, announcing that God was rending the kingdom out of Solomon''s hand.',
        '1 Kings 11:29-31',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Kingmaker''s Trial","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"kingmakers-trial","mechanic":"kingmakers-trial","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I came from the ancient sanctuary town of Shiloh.","I ambushed Solomon''s officer Jeroboam in an open field.","I tore my brand-new cloak into twelve pieces as a royal prophecy."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l20-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        20,
        4,
        'Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth?',
        '"Chuza","Blastus","Theophilus","Manaen"'::text[],
        'Chuza',
        'Luke 8:3 records that Joanna, the wife of Chuza, Herod''s household manager, along with Susanna and others, provided for Jesus out of their resources.',
        'Luke 8:3',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Kingmaker''s Trial","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"kingmakers-trial","mechanic":"kingmakers-trial","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I managed the royal estate and finances for the tetrarch of Galilee.","My wife was a devoted follower of Jesus Christ.","Our household funds helped finance the ministry of the Son of God."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l20-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        20,
        5,
        'Which Babylonian monarch, upon succeeding Nebuchadnezzar, showed gracious kindness to exiled King Jehoiachin of Judah, releasing him from prison to eat at the royal table?',
        '"Neriglissar","Evil-Merodach (Amel-Marduk)","Belshazzar","Nabonidus"'::text[],
        'Evil-Merodach (Amel-Marduk)',
        'Evil-Merodach king of Babylon in the year he began to reign pardoned Jehoiachin king of Judah after 37 years of imprisonment and gave him a regular allowance.',
        '2 Kings 25:27-30',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Kings and Royal Families","level_theme":"The Kingmaker''s Trial","category":"Kings and Royal Families","challengeType":"kingmakers-trial","mechanic":"kingmakers-trial","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the royal successor to King Nebuchadnezzar in Babylon.","In my coronation year I opened the imperial dungeons.","I seated the captive King of Judah at my own dinner table for life."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l21-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        21,
        1,
        '• I stood before King Ahab and King Jehoshaphat.
• Ahab hated me because I never prophesied good concerning him, only disaster.
• I foretold Ahab''s death at Ramoth-gilead while Zedekiah struck my cheek.
Who am I?',
        '"Ahijah the Shilonite","Jehu son of Hanani","Hanani the Seer","Micaiah son of Imlah"'::text[],
        'Micaiah son of Imlah',
        'Micaiah son of Imlah told Ahab that a lying spirit had filled the mouths of his 400 prophets and that Ahab would not return alive from Ramoth-gilead.',
        '1 Kings 22:7-28',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Name That Prophet","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"name-that-prophet","mechanic":"name-that-prophet","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was summoned only after Jehoshaphat insisted on an authentic prophet of the Lord.","Ahab kept me imprisoned with scant rations of bread and water.","I saw Israel scattered on the hills like sheep without a shepherd."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l21-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        21,
        2,
        '• I was a prophet who came down from Judea to Antioch and Caesarea.
• I predicted by the Holy Spirit a severe famine across the entire Roman empire under Emperor Claudius.
• I tied my own hands and feet with Paul''s belt to foretell his Jerusalem arrest.
Who am I?',
        '"Barnabas","Silas","Judas Barsabbas","Agabus"'::text[],
        'Agabus',
        'Agabus foretold the great famine in the days of Claudius and later took Paul''s belt to demonstrate how the Jews in Jerusalem would bind its owner.',
        'Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Name That Prophet","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"name-that-prophet","mechanic":"name-that-prophet","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a recognized New Testament prophet in the apostolic church.","I predicted an empire-wide food shortage that prompted relief to Judea.","I performed an acted prophecy with Paul''s waist belt in Philip''s home."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l21-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        21,
        3,
        '• The Spirit of the Lord came upon me in the middle of a national assembly in Jerusalem.
• I was a Levite descended from Asaph.
• I declared to King Jehoshaphat: ''Do not be afraid... for the battle is not yours, but God''s.''
Who am I?',
        '"Asaph","Eliezer son of Dodavahu","Jahaziel son of Zechariah","Benaiah"'::text[],
        'Jahaziel son of Zechariah',
        'Jahaziel, a Levite of the sons of Asaph, prophesied victory over Moab and Ammon without lifting a weapon, because God Himself would fight for Judah.',
        '2 Chronicles 20:14-17',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Name That Prophet","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"name-that-prophet","mechanic":"name-that-prophet","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a temple musician and Levite from the guild of Asaph.","A massive three-nation invasion threatened to annihilate Judah.","God used my voice to instruct the king to stand still and see the Lord''s deliverance."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l21-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        21,
        4,
        '• I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.
• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.
• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.
Who am I?',
        '"Anna","Elizabeth","Deborah","Huldah"'::text[],
        'Anna',
        'Anna, daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Asher, was an 84-year-old widow prophetess who spoke of the infant Jesus to all waiting for Jerusalem''s redemption.',
        'Luke 2:36-38',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Name That Prophet","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"name-that-prophet","mechanic":"name-that-prophet","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["My father was Phanuel and I belonged to the northern tribe of Asher.","I spent over eight decades serving God night and day with prayers and fastings.","I recognized the 40-day-old infant in the arms of Mary as the Redeemer of Israel."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l21-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        21,
        5,
        '• I was a prophetess who lived in the Second Quarter (Mishneh) of Jerusalem.
• My husband Shallum was keeper of the king''s wardrobe.
• King Josiah''s royal delegation consulted me after finding the lost Book of the Law.
Who am I?',
        '"Deborah","Huldah","Miriam","Noadiah"'::text[],
        'Huldah',
        'Hilkiah the high priest and royal scribes consulted Huldah the prophetess, who confirmed God''s judgment on Judah but promised peace during Josiah''s lifetime.',
        '2 Kings 22:14-20',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Name That Prophet","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"name-that-prophet","mechanic":"name-that-prophet","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I resided in the prestigious Mishneh district of Jerusalem.","My husband held the title Keeper of the Wardrobe.","The highest spiritual and political officials sought my prophetic counsel for King Josiah."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l22-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        22,
        1,
        'Which person was NOT a prophet, but the faithful personal scribe and amanuensis who wrote down Jeremiah''s dictated scrolls and read them aloud in the temple?',
        '"Zephaniah","Baruch son of Neriah","Hananiah","Uriah son of Shemaiah"'::text[],
        'Baruch son of Neriah',
        'Baruch son of Neriah was Jeremiah''s scribe who recorded the prophecies on a scroll and read them boldly in the Lord''s house.',
        'Jeremiah 36:4-10; Jeremiah 45:1',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet or Someone Else?","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-or-other","mechanic":"prophet-or-other","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an educated scribe from a distinguished noble family.","I dipped ink on parchment while a weeping prophet spoke God''s warnings.","God addressed me personally in Jeremiah 45: ''Seekest thou great things for thyself? Seek them not.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l22-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        22,
        2,
        'In Acts 15:32, which two leaders sent from Jerusalem to Antioch are explicitly described by Luke as ''being prophets themselves'' who encouraged and strengthened the church?',
        '"Paul and Timothy","Judas Barsabbas and Silas","Peter and John","Barnabas and John Mark"'::text[],
        'Judas Barsabbas and Silas',
        'Acts 15:32 states: ''And Judas and Silas, who were themselves prophets, encouraged and strengthened the brothers with many words.''',
        'Acts 15:32',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet or Someone Else?","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-or-other","mechanic":"prophet-or-other","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["We were chosen by the Jerusalem council to deliver the apostolic decree.","Luke specifically identifies both of us by the title of prophet.","One of us subsequently became Paul''s main companion on his second missionary journey."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l22-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        22,
        3,
        'Which false prophet from Gibeon opposed Jeremiah in the temple, broke the wooden yoke from Jeremiah''s neck, and died within seven months as God foretold?',
        '"Zedekiah son of Chenaanah","Hananiah son of Azzur","Shemaiah the Nehelamite","Pashhur son of Immer"'::text[],
        'Hananiah son of Azzur',
        'Hananiah falsely promised deliverance from Babylon within two years; Jeremiah told him God would remove him from the earth, and he died that seventh month.',
        'Jeremiah 28:1-17',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet or Someone Else?","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-or-other","mechanic":"prophet-or-other","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I came from the priestly town of Gibeon.","I publicly smashed Jeremiah''s wooden ox yoke in front of the priests and people.","Jeremiah declared I had taught rebellion against the Lord, and I died before the year ended."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l22-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        22,
        4,
        'In Acts 21:8-9, who was the evangelist living in Caesarea who had four unmarried daughters who possessed the gift of prophecy?',
        '"Philip the Evangelist","Agabus","Stephen the Martyr","Barnabas"'::text[],
        'Philip the Evangelist',
        'Paul stayed at Caesarea in the house of Philip the evangelist, one of the seven, who had four virgin daughters who prophesied.',
        'Acts 21:8-9',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet or Someone Else?","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-or-other","mechanic":"prophet-or-other","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was one of the seven men appointed to distribute food to widows in Jerusalem.","I spearheaded a massive revival in Samaria and baptized the Ethiopian.","My household in Caesarea included four daughters gifted with prophecy."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l22-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        22,
        5,
        'Which seer rebuked King Asa of Judah for relying on the Syrian army instead of the Lord, declaring ''the eyes of the Lord run to and fro'', for which Asa threw him in prison?',
        '"Jehu son of Hanani","Hanani the Seer","Jahaziel","Iddo the Seer"'::text[],
        'Hanani the Seer',
        'Hanani the seer confronted Asa for bribing Ben-Hadad of Syria; an enraged Asa locked Hanani in the stocks.',
        '2 Chronicles 16:7-10',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet or Someone Else?","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-or-other","mechanic":"prophet-or-other","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I uttered one of Scripture''s most famous declarations of God''s watchful eyes.","I condemned the king for relying on foreign military treaties.","Instead of repenting, the king put me into prison stocks in a rage."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l23-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        23,
        1,
        'Which Cushite palace official in Jerusalem bravely rescued the prophet Jeremiah from a muddy cistern using worn rags and cords under his armpits?',
        '"Seraiah","Gedaliah","Ebed-Melech","Baruch"'::text[],
        'Ebed-Melech',
        'Ebed-Melech the Ethiopian appealed directly to King Zedekiah, took thirty men, and cushioned ropes with old rags to lift Jeremiah out of the mire.',
        'Jeremiah 38:7-13',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophetic Encounters","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophetic-encounters","mechanic":"prophetic-encounters","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an official from Cush serving in the royal court of Judah.","I stood before the king to plead for a dying prophet sinking in deep mud.","God specifically promised my life would be spared as a prize of war because I trusted Him."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l23-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        23,
        2,
        'Which righteous priest of the division of Abijah was burning incense in the Holy Place when the angel Gabriel announced his wife would bear a prophetic forerunner?',
        '"Nicodemus","Caiaphas","Simeon","Zechariah"'::text[],
        'Zechariah',
        'Zechariah, husband of Elizabeth and father of John the Baptist, was chosen by lot to burn incense in the temple sanctuary where Gabriel visited him.',
        'Luke 1:5-22',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophetic Encounters","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophetic-encounters","mechanic":"prophetic-encounters","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["My wife and I were blameless in all the commandments of the Lord.","I was serving in the temple during my priestly order''s turn.","I was rendered completely speechless for nine months due to questioning an angelic message."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l23-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        23,
        3,
        'Which servant of Elisha chased after Naaman the Syrian commander to fraudulently demand silver and garments, resulting in Naaman''s leprosy falling on him?',
        '"Baruch","Gehazi","Ziba","Ebed-Melech"'::text[],
        'Gehazi',
        'Gehazi ran after Naaman claiming Elisha requested money and garments; Elisha discerned his deceit and cursed Gehazi with Naaman''s leprosy.',
        '2 Kings 5:20-27',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophetic Encounters","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophetic-encounters","mechanic":"prophetic-encounters","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the personal attendant and companion to prophet Elisha.","Greed prompted me to lie and profit from a miraculous healing.","I left my master''s presence a leper, white as snow."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l23-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        23,
        4,
        'Which Roman proconsul of Cyprus desired to hear the word of God and believed after seeing the false prophet and sorcerer Elymas struck blind by Paul?',
        '"Cornelius","Sergius Paulus","Claudius Lysias","Gallio"'::text[],
        'Sergius Paulus',
        'Sergius Paulus, an intelligent proconsul at Paphos, believed when he saw Elymas (Bar-Jesus) blinded for opposing Paul and Barnabas.',
        'Acts 13:6-12',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophetic Encounters","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophetic-encounters","mechanic":"prophetic-encounters","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the highest Roman imperial governor over the island of Cyprus.","I had an intelligent mind and summoned Christian missionaries to investigate their message.","I converted to faith in Christ after watching my resident court sorcerer struck blind."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l23-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        23,
        5,
        'Which prominent woman in Shunem constructed and furnished a dedicated upper room for Elisha, and later had her deceased son resurrected by the prophet?',
        '"The Shunammite woman","Jehosheba","Rizpah","The widow of Zarephath"'::text[],
        'The Shunammite woman',
        'A wealthy woman of Shunem prepared a furnished roof chamber for Elisha; when her promised son died, Elisha stretched himself over the boy and revived him.',
        '2 Kings 4:8-37',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophetic Encounters","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophetic-encounters","mechanic":"prophetic-encounters","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I recognized Elisha as a holy man of God passing by our town.","My husband and I built a brick room on the roof with a bed, table, chair, and lamp.","When my son died suddenly of a head affliction, I rode urgently to Mount Carmel to find the prophet."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l24-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        24,
        1,
        'Which prophet was commanded by the Lord to marry Gomer, a promiscuous woman, to vividly portray Israel''s unfaithfulness to God?',
        '"Hosea","Micah","Habakkuk","Amos"'::text[],
        'Hosea',
        'God told Hosea son of Beeri to take a wife of whoredom; his marriage and children''s names symbolized Israel''s spiritual adultery and ultimate restoration.',
        'Hosea 1:2-9; Hosea 3:1-3',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"The Strange Assignment","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"strange-assignment","mechanic":"strange-assignment","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I prophesied during the reigns of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Jeroboam II.","God ordered my domestic life to become a living parable of covenant heartbreak.","I had to buy back my runaway wife from the slave block."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l24-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        24,
        2,
        'Which prophet lived in the Judean wilderness clothed in camel''s hair with a leather belt, ate locusts and wild honey, and baptized crowds in the Jordan?',
        '"Stephen","Silas","Agabus","John the Baptist"'::text[],
        'John the Baptist',
        'John the Baptist came in the spirit and power of Elijah, living in the wilderness with rugged clothing and diet, heralding the arrival of the Lamb of God.',
        'Matthew 3:1-4; Mark 1:4-6',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"The Strange Assignment","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"strange-assignment","mechanic":"strange-assignment","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was filled with the Holy Spirit while still in my mother''s womb.","I did no miraculous signs, but everything I said about Jesus was true.","My garment was woven camel''s hair and my food was locusts and wild honey."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l24-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        24,
        3,
        'Which prophet was ordered to lie on his left side for 390 days and his right side for 40 days, eating bread baked over dung, to depict Jerusalem''s siege and guilt?',
        '"Jeremiah","Zechariah","Ezekiel","Daniel"'::text[],
        'Ezekiel',
        'Ezekiel lay bound by ropes on his side, drawing Jerusalem on a clay brick and eating rationed multigrain bread to depict the coming siege.',
        'Ezekiel 4:1-17',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"The Strange Assignment","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"strange-assignment","mechanic":"strange-assignment","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a priest living among the Jewish exiles by the river Chebar.","God instructed me to draw a siege on a clay brick and lie on my sides for over a year.","My mouth was repeatedly closed and opened as a dramatic sign to a rebellious house."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l24-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        24,
        4,
        'Which major prophet walked stripped and barefoot through Jerusalem for three years as an enacted sign of the coming humiliation of Egypt and Cush by Assyria?',
        '"Amos","Ezekiel","Isaiah","Jeremiah"'::text[],
        'Isaiah',
        'The Lord commanded Isaiah son of Amoz to take off his sackcloth and sandals, walking stripped and barefoot for three years as a portent against Egypt.',
        'Isaiah 20:1-4',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"The Strange Assignment","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"strange-assignment","mechanic":"strange-assignment","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I ministered in Jerusalem during the reigns of four kings of Judah.","God instructed me to shed my sackcloth outer garment and walk barefoot.","My strange three-year attire warned Judah against trusting military alliances with Egypt."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l24-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        24,
        5,
        'In Revelation 10, which apostle on the island of Patmos was commanded by a mighty angel to take an open little scroll and eat it, making his belly bitter but tasting sweet as honey?',
        '"Paul","Peter","Jude","John"'::text[],
        'John',
        'John took the little scroll from the angel''s hand and ate it; it tasted sweet as honey in his mouth, but when he had eaten it, his stomach was made bitter.',
        'Revelation 10:8-10',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"The Strange Assignment","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"strange-assignment","mechanic":"strange-assignment","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was exiled on a lonely Aegean island for the word of God and testimony of Jesus.","A massive angel with a rainbow on his head handed me a celestial booklet.","Eating God''s prophetic message was sweet to my taste but bitter in my stomach."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l25-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        25,
        1,
        'Which prophet from Mareshah rebuked King Jehoshaphat: ''Because you have allied yourself with Ahaziah, the Lord has destroyed what you made,'' causing his fleet to wreck?',
        '"Jahaziel son of Zechariah","Micaiah son of Imlah","Eliezer son of Dodavahu","Hanani the Seer"'::text[],
        'Eliezer son of Dodavahu',
        'Eliezer son of Dodavahu prophesied against Jehoshaphat''s commercial shipping venture with wicked King Ahaziah of Israel, and the ships were wrecked at Ezion-geber.',
        '2 Chronicles 20:37',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet Boss Round","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-boss","mechanic":"prophet-boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I hailed from the town of Mareshah in the foothills of Judah.","I delivered a scathing divine critique of a royal shipping enterprise.","Because of my prophecy, the commercial fleet at Ezion-geber was wrecked without sailing."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l25-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        25,
        2,
        'In 1 Corinthians 14:32, what vital spiritual principle does the Apostle Paul declare concerning the exercise of prophetic utterance in Christian gatherings?',
        '"The spirits of prophets are subject to the control of prophets","Prophetic utterance must always be shouted","Prophecy can only be given by apostles","Prophets are exempt from all human evaluation"'::text[],
        'The spirits of prophets are subject to the control of prophets',
        'Paul established orderly worship by teaching that true prophetic inspiration does not involve uncontrollable ecstasy: ''The spirits of prophets are subject to prophets.''',
        '1 Corinthians 14:32',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet Boss Round","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-boss","mechanic":"prophet-boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["This is a cornerstone rule for orderly charismatic worship in the New Testament.","It demonstrates that prophets maintain moral responsibility and self-control.","Paul wrote this to correct chaotic, ecstatic shouting in the church at Corinth."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l25-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        25,
        3,
        'Which unnamed man of God from Judah cried out against Jeroboam''s altar at Bethel, had his word confirmed by a lion that killed him without mauling the donkey, after an old prophet misled him?',
        '"Ahijah the Shilonite","Iddo the Seer","The unnamed Man of God from Judah","Shemaiah"'::text[],
        'The unnamed Man of God from Judah',
        'A man of God came from Judah and foretold Josiah by name; though Jeroboam''s hand withered and was restored, the prophet disobeyed God''s dietary command and was slain by a lion.',
        '1 Kings 13:1-24',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet Boss Round","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-boss","mechanic":"prophet-boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I accurately predicted King Josiah''s desecration of Bethel''s altar three centuries in advance.","King Jeroboam''s outstretched hand shriveled when he tried to arrest me.","I was seduced into breaking my divine travel orders by an old local prophet."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l25-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        25,
        4,
        'Which Old Testament prophet''s scroll was the Ethiopian royal treasurer reading aloud when Philip approached his chariot and asked: ''Do you understand what you are reading?''',
        '"Zechariah","Jeremiah","Isaiah","Daniel"'::text[],
        'Isaiah',
        'The Ethiopian eunuch was reading Isaiah 53:7-8 (''As a sheep led to the slaughter...''); Philip began with that Scripture and told him the good news about Jesus.',
        'Acts 8:30-35',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet Boss Round","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-boss","mechanic":"prophet-boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I wrote the extensive ''Suffering Servant'' prophecies in the Old Testament.","My text depicted a sheep led silently to slaughter before its shearers.","Philip used my 53rd chapter to bring the gospel to Africa."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l25-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        25,
        5,
        'When King Jehoash (Joash) of Israel visited the dying prophet Elisha, why did the prophet become furious with the young king over his arrow-shooting assignment?',
        '"The king broke the bow of cedar in frustration","The king struck the ground only three times instead of five or six","The king refused to touch the sacred bow","The king shot the arrow toward Jerusalem instead of Aram"'::text[],
        'The king struck the ground only three times instead of five or six',
        'Elisha was angry because Joash struck the ground only three times, signifying he would defeat Syria only three times instead of totally destroying them.',
        '2 Kings 13:14-19',
        '{"stage":5,"stage_title":"Prophets and Their Encounters","level_theme":"Prophet Boss Round","category":"Prophets and Their Encounters","challengeType":"prophet-boss","mechanic":"prophet-boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["The dying prophet laid his trembling hands upon the young king''s hands on the bow.","The king shot the ''arrow of the Lord''s deliverance'' through an eastern window.","The king''s lack of zeal and faith limited Israel''s future military victories."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l26-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        26,
        1,
        'Which devout and righteous man in Jerusalem was promised by the Holy Spirit that he would not die before seeing the Lord''s Messiah, and held Jesus in his arms proclaiming peace?',
        '"Zechariah","Simeon","Joseph of Arimathea","Nicodemus"'::text[],
        'Simeon',
        'Simeon took the infant Jesus into his arms and praised God with the Nunc Dimittis, declaring Christ a light of revelation to the Gentiles and glory to Israel.',
        'Luke 2:25-32',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Birth Story","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"birth-story","mechanic":"birth-story","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an elderly saint waiting expectantly for the consolation of Israel.","The Holy Spirit rested upon me and promised I would gaze upon the Christ.","I warned Mary that a sword would pierce her own soul also."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l26-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        26,
        2,
        'When the angel Gabriel announced the virgin birth of Jesus to Mary in Nazareth, he stated that God would give Him the royal throne of which Old Testament king?',
        '"Abraham","David","Judah","Solomon"'::text[],
        'David',
        'Gabriel announced: ''He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High. The Lord God will give him the throne of his father David.''',
        'Luke 1:32',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Birth Story","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"birth-story","mechanic":"birth-story","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the shepherd boy who became Israel''s greatest king.","God made an everlasting covenant with my house and royal throne.","Gabriel cited my ancient lineage when announcing Christ''s eternal kingdom."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l26-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        26,
        3,
        'Which Roman imperial administrator was serving as governor of Syria during the historic census that required Joseph and Mary to register in Bethlehem?',
        '"Pontius Pilate","Felix","Quirinius","Gallio"'::text[],
        'Quirinius',
        'Luke 2:2 explicitly notes: ''This was the first registration when Quirinius was governor of Syria.''',
        'Luke 2:2',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Birth Story","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"birth-story","mechanic":"birth-story","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an experienced Roman military commander and senator.","I oversaw the imperial province of Syria bordering Judea.","Luke recorded my name to anchor the Savior''s birth to secular world history."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l26-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        26,
        4,
        'Which elderly relative of Mary, belonging to the priestly daughters of Aaron, conceived John the Baptist in her old age and exclaimed ''Blessed are you among women''?',
        '"Anna","Joanna","Salome","Elizabeth"'::text[],
        'Elizabeth',
        'Elizabeth, wife of Zechariah, was filled with the Holy Spirit when Mary greeted her, and the baby leaped in her womb for joy.',
        'Luke 1:36-42',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Birth Story","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"birth-story","mechanic":"birth-story","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I had been barren for decades and was advanced in years.","My unborn child leaped within my womb at the sound of Mary''s voice.","I was mother to the greatest prophet born of women."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l26-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        26,
        5,
        'In Matthew 2:17-18, the horrific slaughter of infant boys in Bethlehem by Herod the Great is identified as fulfilling Jeremiah''s prophecy of which biblical mother weeping?',
        '"Leah","Rachel","Rebekah","Sarah"'::text[],
        'Rachel',
        'Matthew cites Jeremiah 31:15: ''A voice was heard in Ramah, weeping and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children and refusing to be comforted.''',
        'Matthew 2:17-18; Jeremiah 31:15',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Birth Story","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"birth-story","mechanic":"birth-story","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was Jacob''s dearly loved wife who died giving birth near Bethlehem.","My tomb stood along the ancient road to Ephrath (Bethlehem).","Jeremiah portrayed me weeping for my children as they marched into captivity."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l27-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        27,
        1,
        'Which of the twelve apostles is called ''the Cananite'' in Matthew and Mark, and ''the Zealot'' in Luke, to distinguish him from Simon Peter?',
        '"Simon the Zealot","Simon of Cyrene","Simon Magus","Simon the Leper"'::text[],
        'Simon the Zealot',
        'Simon the Zealot (or Cananite, from Hebrew qanna meaning ''zealous'') was one of the Twelve, distinguished from Simon Peter.',
        'Matthew 10:4; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Twelve","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"the-twelve","mechanic":"the-twelve","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was one of the twelve chosen apostles.","My surname designated my fervent Jewish patriotic zeal or former faction.","I sat beside tax collector Matthew as a fellow disciple of the Prince of Peace."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l27-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        27,
        2,
        'Which apostle from Bethsaida found Nathanael under a fig tree and declared: ''We have found Him of whom Moses in the law, and also the prophets, wrote''?',
        '"Philip","Andrew","James son of Alphaeus","Thomas"'::text[],
        'Philip',
        'Jesus found Philip and said ''Follow me''; Philip then found Nathanael and invited him saying, ''Come and see.''',
        'John 1:43-45',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Twelve","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"the-twelve","mechanic":"the-twelve","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I hailed from the Galilean fishing town of Bethsaida.","I invited a skeptical friend saying ''Come and see.''","At the feeding of the 5,000, Jesus tested my faith regarding bread for the crowd."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l27-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        27,
        3,
        'Which apostle was named Didymus (the Twin), famously offered to die with Jesus in Judea, and later proclaimed ''My Lord and my God!'' after touching His wounds?',
        '"Thaddaeus","Thomas","Bartholomew","James son of Alphaeus"'::text[],
        'Thomas',
        'Thomas called Didymus showed fierce courage when Lazarus died and later uttered the highest confession of Christ''s divinity upon seeing His risen scars.',
        'John 11:16; John 20:24-28',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Twelve","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"the-twelve","mechanic":"the-twelve","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["My Greek surname means ''the Twin.''","I was not present on Easter Sunday evening when Jesus first appeared.","I fell on my knees confessing ''My Lord and my God!'' when examining the nail prints."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l27-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        27,
        4,
        'Which apostle is identified in Luke 6:16 and Acts 1:13 as ''Judas son of James'', also known in Matthew and Mark as Thaddaeus (or Lebbaeus)?',
        '"Judas Barsabbas","Jude the brother of Jesus","Judas Iscariot","Judas son of James (Thaddaeus)"'::text[],
        'Judas son of James (Thaddaeus)',
        'Judas (not Iscariot) asked Jesus at the Last Supper: ''Lord, how is it that you will manifest yourself to us, and not to the world?''',
        'Luke 6:16; John 14:22',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Twelve","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"the-twelve","mechanic":"the-twelve","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was one of the Twelve, often referred to by my alternate name Thaddaeus.","Scripture specifically clarifies ''Judas, not Iscariot'' when quoting me.","I questioned Jesus in the upper room regarding how He would reveal Himself."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l27-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        27,
        5,
        'In Matthew 19:28, what supreme eschatological reward did Jesus promise the Twelve when the Son of Man sits on His glorious throne?',
        '"Ruling over twelve Roman provinces","Sitting on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel","Receiving twelve golden crowns of martyrdom","Commanding twelve legions of archangels"'::text[],
        'Sitting on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel',
        'Jesus promised the twelve apostles that in the regeneration when the Son of Man sits on His glorious throne, they also will sit on twelve thrones judging Israel''s twelve tribes.',
        'Matthew 19:28',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Twelve","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"the-twelve","mechanic":"the-twelve","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["This promise links the twelve New Testament apostles with Old Testament tribal heritage.","It speaks of royal authority in the renewal and regeneration of all things.","It promises judicial and governing seats over God''s redeemed people."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l28-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        28,
        1,
        'Which blind beggar sat by the road outside Jericho crying persistently: ''Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!'', throwing off his cloak when summoned?',
        '"Malchus","Zacchaeus","Cleopas","Bartimaeus son of Timaeus"'::text[],
        'Bartimaeus son of Timaeus',
        'Bartimaeus, son of Timaeus, shouted for mercy; Jesus restored his sight, and he immediately followed Jesus on the road.',
        'Mark 10:46-52',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"Around the Master","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"around-the-master","mechanic":"around-the-master","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["Mark preserves both my personal name and my father''s patronymic.","The crowd rebuked me and told me to be quiet, but I shouted louder.","I sprang up, cast aside my beggar''s cloak, and received my sight."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l28-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        28,
        2,
        'Alongside Mary Magdalene and Joanna, which other woman is explicitly mentioned by name in Luke 8:3 as providing for Jesus out of her personal financial means?',
        '"Salome","Rhoda","Martha","Susanna"'::text[],
        'Susanna',
        'Luke 8:2-3 names Mary Magdalene, Joanna wife of Chuza, and Susanna, and many others, who were ministering to Jesus and His disciples from their substance.',
        'Luke 8:3',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"Around the Master","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"around-the-master","mechanic":"around-the-master","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an eyewitness disciple during Jesus'' Galilean travels.","I am honored by name in Luke''s Gospel as a financial benefactor.","My financial support sustained the traveling company of the Messiah."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l28-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        28,
        3,
        'Which disciple was walking with an unnamed companion toward a village seven miles from Jerusalem on resurrection day when Jesus joined them unnoticed?',
        '"Nicodemus","Cleopas","Joseph of Arimathea","Barnabas"'::text[],
        'Cleopas',
        'Cleopas and his companion walked to Emmaus; their eyes were restrained until Jesus took bread, blessed it, broke it, and gave it to them.',
        'Luke 24:18',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"Around the Master","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"around-the-master","mechanic":"around-the-master","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was walking to Emmaus, deeply dejected after the crucifixion.","I asked the stranger: ''Are you the only visitor to Jerusalem unaware of these things?''","My heart burned within me as He opened the Scriptures along the road."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
