        'bible-character-quest',
        28,
        4,
        'In whose house in Bethany was Jesus reclining at table when a woman poured a costly alabaster flask of pure nard over His head?',
        '"Simon the Pharisee","Simon the Tanner","Simon the Leper","Lazarus"'::text[],
        'Simon the Leper',
        'In Bethany, in the house of Simon the Leper, Mary poured precious ointment on Jesus, preparing His body beforehand for burial.',
        'Matthew 26:6; Mark 14:3',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"Around the Master","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"around-the-master","mechanic":"around-the-master","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I lived in the quiet village of Bethany near the Mount of Olives.","My surname preserves the memory of a dreadful skin disease Jesus likely healed.","My dining table became the setting for the fragrant anointing of the Messiah."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l28-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        28,
        5,
        'When Jesus rested beside Jacob''s well at Sychar in Samaria, John notes this plot of land had originally been given by patriarch Jacob to which beloved son?',
        '"Judah","Joseph","Levi","Benjamin"'::text[],
        'Joseph',
        'John 4:5 notes Sychar was near the parcel of ground Jacob gave to his son Joseph, where Joseph''s bones were buried.',
        'John 4:5; Genesis 48:22; Joshua 24:32',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"Around the Master","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"around-the-master","mechanic":"around-the-master","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the favored son with the coat of many colors.","My bones were carried out of Egypt by Moses during the Exodus.","I was buried in Shechem, near where Jesus spoke with the Samaritan woman."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l29-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        29,
        1,
        'Which ruler of the Capernaum synagogue fell at Jesus'' feet pleading for his dying twelve-year-old daughter, whom Jesus raised saying ''Talitha cumi''?',
        '"Jairus","Sosthenes","Crispus","Nicodemus"'::text[],
        'Jairus',
        'Jairus, a synagogue leader, trusted Jesus even after hearing his daughter had died; Jesus took the girl by the hand and raised her to life.',
        'Mark 5:22-43; Luke 8:41',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Miracle Witnesses","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"miracle-witnesses","mechanic":"miracle-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I held the prominent local office of synagogue president.","My only twelve-year-old daughter was at the point of death.","Jesus told me: ''Do not fear, only believe,'' and raised my child from death."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l29-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        29,
        2,
        'What was the exact personal name of the high priest''s servant whose right ear was sliced off by Peter in Gethsemane and miraculously healed by Jesus?',
        '"Alexander","Malchus","Rufus","Chuza"'::text[],
        'Malchus',
        'John 18:10 identifies the servant of the high priest as Malchus; Luke 22:51 records that Jesus touched his ear and healed him.',
        'John 18:10; Luke 22:51',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Miracle Witnesses","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"miracle-witnesses","mechanic":"miracle-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the personal slave and agent of High Priest Caiaphas.","I accompanied the armed mob into the dark Garden of Gethsemane.","Jesus performed His final recorded healing miracle upon my severed right ear."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l29-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        29,
        3,
        'At the city gates of which Galilean town did Jesus encounter a funeral bier, pity a weeping widow, and command her deceased only son: ''Young man, arise''?',
        '"Chorazin","Capernaum","Nain","Bethsaida"'::text[],
        'Nain',
        'At the town of Nain, Jesus had compassion on a widow whose only son was dead; He touched the coffin and the young man sat up and began to speak.',
        'Luke 7:11-15',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Miracle Witnesses","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"miracle-witnesses","mechanic":"miracle-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a small agricultural town in southern Galilee near Mount Moreh.","A funeral procession carried a young man out toward the cemetery.","Jesus stopped the open coffin and restored the son alive to his mother."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l29-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        29,
        4,
        'Near which pool in Jerusalem, surrounded by five covered porticoes, did Jesus heal a man who had suffered from an infirmity for thirty-eight years?',
        '"En-rogel","Siloam","Bethesda","Gihon"'::text[],
        'Bethesda',
        'At the pool of Bethesda near the Sheep Gate, Jesus found an invalid who had been sick 38 years, commanded him to take up his mat, and healed him.',
        'John 5:2-9',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Miracle Witnesses","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"miracle-witnesses","mechanic":"miracle-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I was located near the historic Sheep Gate in Jerusalem.","My perimeter featured five covered colonnades packed with invalids.","Jesus bypassed the superstitions of stirred waters and healed a man paralyzed 38 years."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l29-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        29,
        5,
        'After witnessing Jesus feed the five thousand with five loaves and two fish, the astonished crowd proclaimed Him to be ''The Prophet'', fulfilling the prophecy of which leader in Deuteronomy 18?',
        '"Elijah","Joshua","Samuel","Moses"'::text[],
        'Moses',
        'Seeing the bread miracle in the wilderness, the people recognized Jesus as the prophet like unto Moses promised in Deuteronomy 18:15.',
        'John 6:14; Deuteronomy 18:15',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Miracle Witnesses","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"miracle-witnesses","mechanic":"miracle-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true,"clues":["I led Israel through the wilderness where bread fell from heaven.","I foretold: ''The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from your brothers.''","The crowds recognized the bread miracle as the arrival of my promised successor."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l30-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        30,
        1,
        'Which prominent Sanhedrin member from Arimathea, who had not consented to the council''s condemnation, boldly requested Jesus'' body from Pilate and laid Him in his own new tomb?',
        '"Joseph the carpenter","Joseph called Barsabbas","Joseph a Levite of Cyprus","Joseph of Arimathea"'::text[],
        'Joseph of Arimathea',
        'Joseph of Arimathea, a rich and honorable council member waiting for God''s kingdom, took down Jesus'' body, wrapped it in linen, and laid it in his personal rock tomb.',
        'Matthew 27:57-60; Mark 15:43; Luke 23:50-53',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Gospel Identity Test","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"gospel-identity","mechanic":"gospel-identity","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a wealthy and respected member of the Jewish supreme council.","I was secretly a disciple of Jesus for fear of the Jewish authorities.","I went boldly before Pontius Pilate to claim and bury the Lord''s crucified body."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
