        'bible-character-quest',
        30,
        2,
        'Distinguish these biblical Marys: Which Mary was the sister of Martha and Lazarus who sat at Jesus'' feet listening to His words and later anointed His feet with costly spikenard?',
        '"Mary Magdalene","Mary of Clopas","Mary of Bethany","Mary mother of John Mark"'::text[],
        'Mary of Bethany',
        'Mary of Bethany chose the good portion by sitting at Jesus'' feet; she later wiped His feet with her hair after pouring a pound of costly nard on Him.',
        'Luke 10:38-42; John 11:1-2; John 12:1-3',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Gospel Identity Test","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"gospel-identity","mechanic":"gospel-identity","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I lived with my brother and sister just east of Jerusalem.","Jesus commended my spiritual priority over domestic hospitality busyness.","I poured an entire alabaster container of nard worth a year''s wages on my Lord."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l30-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        30,
        3,
        'Distinguish these biblical Lazaruses: Which Lazarus was the beloved friend whom Jesus wept over and raised to life after being dead in a rock tomb for four days?',
        '"Eleazar the high priest","Lazarus of Bethany","Eliezer of Damascus","Lazarus the beggar at the rich man's gate"'::text[],
        'Lazarus of Bethany',
        'Lazarus of Bethany, brother of Martha and Mary, had been in the tomb four days until Jesus shouted: ''Lazarus, come out!''',
        'John 11:1-44',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Gospel Identity Test","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"gospel-identity","mechanic":"gospel-identity","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the subject of the shortest verse in Scripture: ''Jesus wept.''","I was wrapped in graveclothes and decomposing in a limestone tomb for four days.","The chief priests plotted to murder me because many believed in Jesus on my account."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l30-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        30,
        4,
        'Distinguish these biblical Simons: Which Simon from North Africa was compelled by Roman soldiers to carry Jesus'' heavy wooden cross-beam, whose sons were Alexander and Rufus?',
        '"Simon Peter","Simon of Cyrene","Simon the Zealot","Simon the Leper"'::text[],
        'Simon of Cyrene',
        'A passerby coming in from the country, Simon of Cyrene, was conscripted by the Roman soldiers to bear Christ''s cross behind Him.',
        'Matthew 27:32; Mark 15:21',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Gospel Identity Test","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"gospel-identity","mechanic":"gospel-identity","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a pilgrim traveling thousands of miles from North Africa for Passover.","Roman soldiers pressed me into compulsory cross-bearing service.","My sons Alexander and Rufus became well-known believers in the early church."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l30-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        30,
        5,
        'In John 3:14, Jesus told the inquiring Pharisee Nicodemus that just as which Old Testament leader lifted up the bronze serpent on a pole in the wilderness, so must the Son of Man be lifted up?',
        '"Aaron","Moses","Eleazar","Joshua"'::text[],
        'Moses',
        'Jesus linked His coming crucifixion to Moses lifting the bronze serpent in Numbers 21, so that whoever looks upon Him in faith will have eternal life.',
        'John 3:14; Numbers 21:8-9',
        '{"stage":6,"stage_title":"The People Around Jesus","level_theme":"The Gospel Identity Test","category":"The People Around Jesus","challengeType":"gospel-identity","mechanic":"gospel-identity","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I crafted a serpent of bronze and fastened it to a high pole.","Those bitten by venomous vipers looked upon it in faith and were healed.","Jesus used my wilderness action as the ultimate typological picture of the cross."]}'::jsonb
