(
        'bible-character-quest-l31-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        31,
        1,
        'In the Parable of the Good Samaritan, which two religious officials walked past the beaten traveler on the road from Jerusalem to Jericho before the Samaritan stopped?',
        '"A Priest and a Levite","A Centurion and a Tax Collector","A Pharisee and a Sadducee","A Scribe and an Elder"'::text[],
        'A Priest and a Levite',
        'Jesus described a priest and then a Levite who both came down that road, saw the wounded traveler, and crossed to pass by on the other side.',
        'Luke 10:31-32',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Parable Characters","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"parable-characters","mechanic":"parable-characters","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We held sacred hereditary offices in the Jerusalem temple system.","We both observed a stripped and half-dead countryman in a ditch.","We both crossed over to the opposite side of the road and kept walking."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l31-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        31,
        2,
        'In the Parable of the Rich Man and Lazarus, what was the specific name of the poor beggar who lay at the rich man''s gate covered with sores, longing for scraps?',
        '"Zacchaeus","Lazarus","Bartimaeus","Eleazar"'::text[],
        'Lazarus',
        'This is the only character given an individual personal name in any of Jesus'' parables: Lazarus, meaning ''God is my helper''.',
        'Luke 16:20',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Parable Characters","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"parable-characters","mechanic":"parable-characters","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an impoverished, disabled outcast covered with ulcerated sores.","The domestic dogs of the estate came and licked my wounds.","I was carried away by the angels to Abraham''s bosom."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l31-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        31,
        3,
        'In the Parable of the Two Sons, which Old Testament prophet-like figure did Jesus say came showing the way of righteousness, whom tax collectors and prostitutes believed?',
        '"Malachi","Jeremiah","Elijah","John the Baptist"'::text[],
        'John the Baptist',
        'Jesus told the chief priests: ''John came to you in the way of righteousness, and you did not believe him, but the tax collectors and the prostitutes believed him.''',
        'Matthew 21:31-32',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Parable Characters","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"parable-characters","mechanic":"parable-characters","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I preached in the Judean wilderness heralding the kingdom.","Outcasts repented at my preaching while the religious elite rejected me.","Jesus cited my ministry when teaching the parable of the two sons."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l31-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        31,
        4,
        'In the Parable of the Unjust Judge, who persistently came to him pleading: ''Give me justice against my adversary'', causing the judge to finally grant her legal relief?',
        '"A destitute orphan","A persistent widow","A grieving mother","A runaway servant"'::text[],
        'A persistent widow',
        'Jesus told this parable that disciples ought always to pray and not lose heart: a widow wore down an uncaring judge by her continual coming.',
        'Luke 18:2-5',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Parable Characters","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"parable-characters","mechanic":"parable-characters","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I had neither social influence nor financial leverage in the municipal court.","My relentless knocking and petitioning exhausted an unrighteous magistrate.","Jesus used my tenacity to illustrate unwavering perseverance in prayer."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l31-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        31,
        5,
        'In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, who became furiously angry, refused to enter the celebration banquet, and complained that a young goat was never given to him?',
        '"The father's head steward","The older brother","The village elder","The younger brother's creditor"'::text[],
        'The older brother',
        'The older brother became angry and refused to go inside; when his father came out to plead with him, he complained about his years of dutiful slaving.',
        'Luke 15:28-30',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Parable Characters","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"parable-characters","mechanic":"parable-characters","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I remained at home working the fields faithfully for years.","I grew bitterly resentful when the fatted calf was killed for my wandering sibling.","My father reminded me: ''You are always with me, and all that is mine is yours.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l32-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        32,
        1,
        'Which religious group in Jerusalem, who denied the resurrection of the dead, challenged Jesus with the hypothetical problem of a woman married to seven brothers?',
        '"The Pharisees","The Sadducees","The Herodians","The Essenes"'::text[],
        'The Sadducees',
        'The Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, posed the riddle of Levirate marriage; Jesus replied they knew neither the Scriptures nor the power of God.',
        'Matthew 22:23-28; Luke 20:27-33',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Questioners","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"the-questioners","mechanic":"the-questioners","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We were the wealthy aristocratic and high-priestly establishment.","We rejected belief in angels, spirits, and the bodily resurrection.","Jesus refuted our theological riddle using God''s words to Moses at the burning bush."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l32-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        32,
        2,
        'Which Jewish lawyer stood up to test Jesus by asking ''Teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?'' and subsequently asked ''And who is my neighbor?''',
        '"An expert in the Mosaic Law","Tertullus the orator","Gamaliel the doctor of law","Nicodemus the Pharisee"'::text[],
        'An expert in the Mosaic Law',
        'A certain lawyer (an expert in Torah) stood up to put Jesus to the test, prompting Jesus to tell the timeless Parable of the Good Samaritan.',
        'Luke 10:25-29',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Questioners","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"the-questioners","mechanic":"the-questioners","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was professionally trained in the rabbinic interpretation of Torah jurisprudence.","I sought to justify my own limited definition of communal charity.","Jesus answered my second legal query with a piercing story about a traveling Samaritan."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l32-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        32,
        3,
        'In John 12:20-22, which group of Gentile worshipers came up to Philip at the Passover festival with the earnest request: ''Sir, we wish to see Jesus''?',
        '"Syrians","Greeks","Romans","Ethiopians"'::text[],
        'Greeks',
        'Some Greeks who went up to worship at the feast came to Philip and said ''Sir, we wish to see Jesus.'' Philip told Andrew, and together they told Jesus.',
        'John 12:20-22',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Questioners","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"the-questioners","mechanic":"the-questioners","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We were Hellenistic pilgrims traveling to Jerusalem for the Feast of Unleavened Bread.","We approached Philip from Bethsaida because of his Greek name.","Our inquiry signaled to Jesus that the hour had arrived for the Son of Man to be glorified."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l32-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        32,
        4,
        'Which Roman procurator interrogated Jesus during His civil trial, asking ''Are you the King of the Jews?'' and the cynical question ''What is truth?''',
        '"Pontius Pilate","Porcius Festus","Antonius Felix","Claudius Lysias"'::text[],
        'Pontius Pilate',
        'Pontius Pilate, prefect of Judea, repeatedly declared he found no guilt in Jesus, but delivered Him to be crucified to appease the mob.',
        'John 18:33-38',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Questioners","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"the-questioners","mechanic":"the-questioners","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I held the military and judicial authority of the Roman empire in Judea.","I washed my hands in water before the crowd claiming innocence of His blood.","I wrote the official trilingual title on the cross: ''Jesus of Nazareth, King of the Jews.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l32-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        32,
        5,
        'When Pharisees asked Jesus if it was lawful to divorce for any cause, Jesus countered by citing God''s original creation design of which first couple in Genesis?',
        '"Jacob and Rachel","Abraham and Sarah","Isaac and Rebekah","Adam and Eve"'::text[],
        'Adam and Eve',
        'Jesus answered: ''He who made them at the beginning made them male and female... what therefore God has joined together, let not man separate.''',
        'Matthew 19:4-6; Genesis 1:27; Genesis 2:24',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Questioners","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"the-questioners","mechanic":"the-questioners","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We were created directly by God in the pristine Garden of Eden.","Scripture records that the two of us became one flesh before the fall.","Jesus cited our original union to nullify easy divorce concessions."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l33-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        33,
        1,
        'Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane?',
        '"Annas","Caiaphas","Ananias son of Nedebaeus","Theophilus"'::text[],
        'Annas',
        'The detachment bound Jesus and led Him first to Annas, who was the father-in-law of Caiaphas, the high priest that year.',
        'John 18:13',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Final Week","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"final-week","mechanic":"final-week","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I had previously held the high priesthood and retained enormous patriarchal control.","Five of my sons and my son-in-law held the high priestly office.","The temple police brought Jesus to my palace first for initial questioning."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l33-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        33,
        2,
        'Which infamous prisoner and insurrectionist, who had committed murder in the uprising in Jerusalem, was released by Pilate instead of Jesus?',
        '"Barabbas","Gestas","Simon of Cyrene","Dismas"'::text[],
        'Barabbas',
        'Barabbas was in prison with the insurrectionists who had committed murder; the crowd, incited by chief priests, demanded his release and Jesus'' crucifixion.',
        'Matthew 27:16-26; Mark 15:7',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Final Week","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"final-week","mechanic":"final-week","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My patronymic surname means ''son of the father.''","I was a convicted violent revolutionary awaiting execution on a Roman cross.","By custom of the festival, I walked out of death row a free man while Jesus took my cross."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l33-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        33,
        3,
        'Who sent an urgent message to Pontius Pilate sitting on the judgment seat: ''Have nothing to do with that righteous man, for I have suffered much today in a dream because of him''?',
        '"Pilate's wife","Bernice","Herodias","Salome"'::text[],
        'Pilate''s wife',
        'While Pilate was sitting on the judgment seat, his wife sent him word warning him not to condemn that righteous man because of a terrifying dream.',
        'Matthew 27:19',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Final Week","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"final-week","mechanic":"final-week","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the Roman aristocratic spouse of the governor of Judea.","I experienced a deeply unsettling daytime dream concerning Jesus of Nazareth.","I dispatched an urgent runner to interrupt formal courtroom proceedings with my warning."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l33-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        33,
        4,
        'Which Roman military officer standing facing Jesus on the cross witnessed how He died and exclaimed: ''Truly this man was the Son of God!''?',
        '"Cornelius of Caesarea","Claudius Lysias","Julius of the Augustan Cohort","The Centurion at the cross"'::text[],
        'The Centurion at the cross',
        'When the centurion who stood facing Jesus saw the manner of His death, he declared: ''Truly this was the Son of God!''',
        'Mark 15:39',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Final Week","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"final-week","mechanic":"final-week","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a hardened Roman commander of eighty to a hundred legionaries.","I supervised the agonizing executions on Golgotha.","The way Jesus breathed His last tore through my pagan worldview and wrung out my confession."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l33-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        33,
        5,
        'Which ruler of Galilee happened to be visiting Jerusalem for Passover, hoped to see Jesus perform a miraculous sign, and mocked Him in an elegant robe before sending Him back?',
        '"Herod Agrippa I","Archelaus","Herod Antipas","Philip the Tetrarch"'::text[],
        'Herod Antipas',
        'Pilate sent Jesus to Herod Antipas, who had long desired to see Him; Herod questioned Jesus with many words, but Jesus gave him no answer.',
        'Luke 23:7-11',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"The Final Week","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"final-week","mechanic":"final-week","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the tetrarch who had earlier executed John the Baptist.","I was thrilled when Pilate transferred Jesus into my municipal jurisdiction.","Jesus spoke not a single syllable to me, so I dressed Him in mock splendour and returned Him."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l34-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        34,
        1,
        'Which woman came to the tomb while it was still dark, found the stone taken away, mistook the risen Lord for the gardener, and heard Him call her ''Mary''?',
        '"Mary Magdalene","Mary the mother of James","Mary of Bethany","Salome"'::text[],
        'Mary Magdalene',
        'Mary Magdalene wept outside the tomb; Jesus appeared to her first, called her by name, and sent her as the first witness to announce His resurrection to the apostles.',
        'John 20:1-16',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Resurrection Witnesses","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"resurrection-witnesses","mechanic":"resurrection-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["Jesus had previously delivered me from seven tormenting demons.","I stood weeping alone in the dawn mist outside the empty limestone tomb.","When He called my name, I turned and cried out in Aramaic: ''Rabboni!''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l34-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        34,
        2,
        'Which disciple, absent when the risen Lord first appeared on Sunday evening, insisted he would never believe unless he placed his finger in the nail marks and hand in His side?',
        '"Philip","Thomas","Bartholomew","James son of Alphaeus"'::text[],
        'Thomas',
        'Eight days later Jesus appeared again and invited Thomas to put his finger into His hands and his hand into His side; Thomas fell in worship.',
        'John 20:24-28',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Resurrection Witnesses","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"resurrection-witnesses","mechanic":"resurrection-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was not with the ten disciples behind locked doors on resurrection night.","I demanded tangible empirical proof before accepting their testimony.","One week later I uttered: ''My Lord and my God!''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l34-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        34,
        3,
        'In John 21:2, which seven disciples were gathered fishing on the Sea of Tiberias when the risen Jesus stood on the shore at dawn and prepared fish and bread?',
        '"Peter, Cleopas, Barnabas, and four unnamed women","All eleven remaining apostles together","Peter, Andrew, James, John, and Matthew","Peter, Thomas, Nathanael, the sons of Zebedee, and two other disciples"'::text[],
        'Peter, Thomas, Nathanael, the sons of Zebedee, and two other disciples',
        'John 21:2 enumerates: Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, the sons of Zebedee (James and John), and two others of His disciples.',
        'John 21:1-4',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Resurrection Witnesses","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"resurrection-witnesses","mechanic":"resurrection-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We had toiled all night on the lake without netting a single fish.","A figure on the shore directed us to cast our net on the right side of the boat.","We dragged 153 large fish ashore and breakfasted on the beach with Jesus."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l34-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        34,
        4,
        'In 1 Corinthians 15:6, the Apostle Paul reports that the risen Christ appeared in a single resurrection event to more than how many brothers at once?',
        '"More than 500 brothers at one time","Exactly 120 disciples","More than 70 disciples","Exactly 3,000 believers"'::text[],
        'More than 500 brothers at one time',
        'Paul wrote that Jesus appeared to more than 500 brothers at one time, most of whom were still alive when 1 Corinthians was written.',
        '1 Corinthians 15:6',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Resurrection Witnesses","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"resurrection-witnesses","mechanic":"resurrection-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["This was the largest single mass sighting of the resurrected Christ.","Paul noted that the majority of these eyewitnesses were still living when he penned his letter.","It provided overwhelming legal and historical validation of the empty tomb."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l34-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        34,
        5,
        'In 1 Corinthians 15:7, to which specific earthly brother of Jesus did the risen Lord appear individually, transforming him from a skeptic into a pillars-leader of the Jerusalem church?',
        '"Jude","Joses","Simon","James the brother of the Lord"'::text[],
        'James the brother of the Lord',
        'Paul records: ''Then he appeared to James, then to all the apostles.'' This appearance convinced James, who later presided over the Jerusalem Council.',
        '1 Corinthians 15:7; Galatians 1:19',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Resurrection Witnesses","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"resurrection-witnesses","mechanic":"resurrection-witnesses","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["During Jesus'' earthly ministry, my brothers and I did not believe in Him.","The risen Christ met me personally and privately after His resurrection.","I became the widely respected presiding overseer of the mother church in Jerusalem."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l35-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        35,
        1,
        'Which prominent Pharisee and Sanhedrin ruler brought a lavish mixture of myrrh and aloes weighing about seventy-five Roman pounds to assist in burying Jesus?',
        '"Gamaliel","Joseph of Arimathea","Simon the Pharisee","Nicodemus"'::text[],
        'Nicodemus',
        'Nicodemus, who had at first come to Jesus by night, brought about seventy-five pounds of myrrh and aloes to wrap Jesus'' body with spices according to Jewish burial custom.',
        'John 19:39-40',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Gospel Character Boss","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"gospel-boss","mechanic":"gospel-boss","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I initially sought Jesus under cover of darkness to inquire about being born again.","I had defended Jesus'' right to a fair legal hearing before my hostile colleagues.","I contributed a royal quantity of 100 Roman pounds of aromatic spices for His tomb."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l35-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        35,
        2,
        'When Jesus cleansed the Jerusalem temple of money changers, which two Old Testament prophets did He combine: ''My house shall be called a house of prayer'' and ''a den of robbers''?',
        '"Hosea and Micah","Isaiah and Jeremiah","Elijah and Elisha","Ezekiel and Daniel"'::text[],
        'Isaiah and Jeremiah',
        'Jesus combined Isaiah 56:7 (''for my house shall be called a house of prayer for all nations'') with Jeremiah 7:11 (''has this house... become a den of robbers in your eyes?'').',
        'Matthew 21:13; Isaiah 56:7; Jeremiah 7:11',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Gospel Character Boss","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"gospel-boss","mechanic":"gospel-boss","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["Our ancient prophetic scrolls exposed hypocritical sacrificial trade.","One of us foretold a house of prayer for all Gentile nations.","The other condemned Judeans who turned God''s sanctuary into a cave of bandits."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l35-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        35,
        3,
        'Which high priest made the unconscious prophetic statement to the Sanhedrin: ''It is better for you that one man should die for the people, and not that the whole nation perish''?',
        '"Jonathan son of Annas","Annas","Caiaphas","Theophilus son of Annas"'::text[],
        'Caiaphas',
        'Joseph Caiaphas, being high priest that fateful year, prophesied without realizing it that Jesus was about to die for the nation and gather God''s scattered children.',
        'John 11:49-52',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Gospel Character Boss","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"gospel-boss","mechanic":"gospel-boss","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the official high priest who presided over Jesus'' trial.","I presided over the Sanhedrin plot after the resurrection of Lazarus.","John notes that being high priest that year, God spoke a profound substitutionary prophecy through my words."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l35-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        35,
        4,
        'Which young man fled naked through the garden of Gethsemane on the night of Jesus'' arrest, leaving behind his linen garment in the hands of the arresting mob?',
        '"An unnamed young follower (traditionally John Mark)","John the Apostle","James son of Alphaeus","Tychicus"'::text[],
        'An unnamed young follower (traditionally John Mark)',
        'Mark alone preserves the detail of a young man wearing only a linen cloth over his naked body who fled naked when seized by the temple guards.',
        'Mark 14:51-52',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Gospel Character Boss","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"gospel-boss","mechanic":"gospel-boss","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was roused from sleep wearing only a night linen wrapper.","I trailed the armed detachment into the olive groves of Gethsemane.","When the guards grabbed my cloth, I slipped free and sprinted into the darkness naked."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l35-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        35,
        5,
        'Which woman is identified in Mark 15:40 and 16:1 as being at the crucifixion and empty tomb, identified elsewhere in Matthew as the mother of Zebedee''s sons?',
        '"Susanna","Martha","Salome","Joanna"'::text[],
        'Salome',
        'Comparing Mark 15:40 with Matthew 27:56 reveals that Salome is the mother of James and John, the sons of Zebedee.',
        'Mark 15:40; Matthew 27:56',
        '{"stage":7,"stage_title":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","level_theme":"Gospel Character Boss","category":"Parables, Encounters and the Final Week","challengeType":"gospel-boss","mechanic":"gospel-boss","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I had followed and ministered to Jesus throughout His journeys in Galilee.","I had once requested premier seats for my two sons on the right and left of His kingdom.","I carried morning spices to the limestone garden tomb on the first Easter morning."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l36-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        36,
        1,
        'Which disciple was chosen by lot to replace Judas Iscariot as the twelfth apostle after prayer, chosen over Joseph called Barsabbas (Justus)?',
        '"Stephen","Barnabas","Matthias","Silas"'::text[],
        'Matthias',
        'Two men were proposed: Joseph called Barsabbas and Matthias; after prayer, the lots fell on Matthias, and he was numbered with the eleven apostles.',
        'Acts 1:21-26',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Acts of the Apostles","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"acts-apostles","mechanic":"acts-apostles","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I accompanied Jesus from John''s baptism until His ascension.","My qualifications matched Peter''s requirement for a resurrection witness.","The apostolic lot fell upon me in the upper room."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l36-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        36,
        2,
        'Which respected Pharisee and doctor of the law in the Sanhedrin cautioned the council regarding Peter and John, citing the failed rebellions of Theudas and Judas the Galilean?',
        '"Gamaliel","Alexander","Caiaphas","Nicodemus"'::text[],
        'Gamaliel',
        'Gamaliel, a teacher of the law held in honor by all the people, advised: ''If this counsel or work is of men, it will fail; but if it is of God, you cannot overthrow it.''',
        'Acts 5:34-40',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Acts of the Apostles","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"acts-apostles","mechanic":"acts-apostles","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the grandson of the famous Rabbi Hillel and leader of the School of Hillel.","Saul of Tarsus had sat at my feet to be trained in the strict law.","My calm judicial intervention saved the early apostles from immediate execution."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l36-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        36,
        3,
        'Which sorcerer in Samaria had astonished the populace claiming to be ''that power of God which is called Great'', yet offered Peter money to purchase the gift of the Holy Spirit?',
        '"Elymas","Theudas","Simon Magus (the Sorcerer)","Alexander"'::text[],
        'Simon Magus (the Sorcerer)',
        'Simon the sorcerer practiced magic in Samaria; after baptism, he attempted to buy apostolic power, prompting Peter to say his heart was not right before God.',
        'Acts 8:9-24',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Acts of the Apostles","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"acts-apostles","mechanic":"acts-apostles","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["The entire Samaritan public had venerated me as an embodiment of divine energy.","Philip''s authentic miracles completely shattered my magical prestige.","Peter severely rebuked me for thinking the gift of God could be bought with silver."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l36-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        36,
        4,
        'Which chief official of the island of Malta welcomed Paul and his shipmates hospitably, whose father Paul healed of fever and dysentery through prayer and laying on of hands?',
        '"Gallio","Publius","Theophilus","Julius"'::text[],
        'Publius',
        'Publius, the leading man of Malta, owned estates near the shipwreck site; Paul entered and healed his bedridden father, prompting all island sick to come.',
        'Acts 28:7-8',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Acts of the Apostles","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"acts-apostles","mechanic":"acts-apostles","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the supreme magistrate and wealthiest landholder on the island of Malta.","I opened my private estate to shelter 276 soaked shipwreck survivors for three days.","Paul''s miraculous healing of my father opened the entire island to the gospel."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l36-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        36,
        5,
        'In Acts 7, whose speech to the Sanhedrin retells the entire Old Testament story from Abraham to Solomon before being stoned as the first Christian martyr?',
        '"Stephen","Peter","Paul","Philip"'::text[],
        'Stephen',
        'Stephen, a man full of grace and power, reviewed Israel''s history of rejecting God''s messengers and saw heaven opened with the Son of Man standing at God''s right hand.',
        'Acts 6:8-15; Acts 7:1-60',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Acts of the Apostles","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"acts-apostles","mechanic":"acts-apostles","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My face shone like the face of an angel before the Sanhedrin council.","I delivered the longest theological address recorded in the Book of Acts.","As jagged stones battered my body, I cried: ''Lord, do not hold this sin against them.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l37-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        37,
        1,
        'Which Macedonian believer from Thessalonica was dragged into the Ephesus theater riot alongside Gaius and later accompanied Paul on his voyage to Rome as a fellow prisoner?',
        '"Tychicus","Aristarchus","Secundus","Epaphras"'::text[],
        'Aristarchus',
        'Aristarchus of Thessalonica was seized in Ephesus, sailed with Paul on the prison ship to Rome, and is greeted by Paul as ''my fellow prisoner'' in Colossians 4:10.',
        'Acts 19:29; Acts 27:2; Colossians 4:10',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"pauls-companions","mechanic":"pauls-companions","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I hailed from the bustling Macedonian port city of Thessalonica.","A screaming pagan mob hauled me into the 25,000-seat amphitheater at Ephesus.","Paul specifically called me his fellow prisoner when writing from Roman custody."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l37-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        37,
        2,
        'Which faithful minister from Colossae evangelized the Lycus Valley cities (Colossae, Laodicea, and Hierapolis) and was described by Paul as ''always laboring fervently for you in prayers''?',
        '"Epaphras","Philemon","Trophimus","Archippus"'::text[],
        'Epaphras',
        'Epaphras founded the church in Colossae and shared Paul''s imprisonment in Rome, constantly wrestling in prayer for his home congregations.',
        'Colossians 1:7; Colossians 4:12-13; Philemon 1:23',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"pauls-companions","mechanic":"pauls-companions","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the local evangelist who planted the church in Colossae.","I carried news of the Colossian heresy directly to Paul''s prison quarters.","Paul described me as a prayer warrior wrestling on my knees for your maturity."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l37-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        37,
        3,
        'Which trusted emissary and ''beloved brother'' from Asia was dispatched by Paul to deliver the circular letters to Ephesus and Colossae, carrying personal news of Paul''s affairs?',
        '"Artemas","Trophimus","Tychicus","Erastus"'::text[],
        'Tychicus',
        'Paul called Tychicus a beloved brother and faithful minister who would tell them all his news and encourage their hearts; he carried the letters to Ephesus and Colossae.',
        'Ephesians 6:21-22; Colossians 4:7-8; 2 Timothy 4:12',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"pauls-companions","mechanic":"pauls-companions","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an Asian Christian delegate representing the churches during the famine collection.","Paul trusted me with the physical manuscripts of the Ephesian and Colossian epistles.","I served as Paul''s reliable courier and replacement pastor for Titus and Timothy."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l37-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        37,
        4,
        'Which Ephesian companion was mistakenly assumed by Jerusalem Jews to have been brought into the forbidden temple courts by Paul, triggering the riot that led to Paul''s arrest?',
        '"Sosthenes","Tychicus","Alexander","Trophimus"'::text[],
        'Trophimus',
        'The mob rioted because they had seen Trophimus the Ephesian in the city with Paul and wrongly assumed Paul had brought a Gentile past the temple barrier.',
        'Acts 21:29; 2 Timothy 4:20',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"pauls-companions","mechanic":"pauls-companions","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a Gentile believer from the major metropolis of Ephesus.","My casual stroll through the streets of Jerusalem sparked a wild riot.","Later, Paul had to leave me behind ill at Miletus."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l37-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        37,
        5,
        'Which runaway slave belonging to Philemon met Paul in Roman prison, was converted to Christ, and was sent back by Paul as ''a beloved brother'' carrying a personal plea?',
        '"Tychicus","Tertius","Onesimus","Epaphroditus"'::text[],
        'Onesimus',
        'Onesimus, whose name means ''useful'', had run away from Philemon; Paul led him to faith and sent him back not merely as a bondservant, but as a beloved brother.',
        'Philemon 1:10-16; Colossians 4:9',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"pauls-companions","mechanic":"pauls-companions","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My Greek name literally meant ''useful'' or ''profitable.''","I was a fugitive slave who escaped across the Mediterranean to imperial Rome.","Paul became my spiritual father in chains and petitioned my master to welcome me as a brother."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l38-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        38,
        1,
        'Which native of Alexandria was an eloquent speaker mighty in the Scriptures who accurately taught about Jesus, yet knew only the baptism of John until Priscilla and Aquila instructed him?',
        '"Barnabas","Apollos","Titus","Stephen"'::text[],
        'Apollos',
        'Apollos was eloquent and mighty in the Scriptures, but when Priscilla and Aquila heard him in Ephesus, they took him aside and explained the way of God more accurately.',
        'Acts 18:24-28',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Early Church Leaders","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"early-leaders","mechanic":"early-leaders","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I came from the great intellectual center of Alexandria in Egypt.","I was fervent in spirit and debated Jewish opponents forcefully in public.","A tentmaking couple gently pulled me aside to complete my understanding of Christian baptism."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l38-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        38,
        2,
        'Which deaconess (or servant) of the church in Cenchreae was commended by Paul to the Roman believers as a benefactor and courier of the Epistle to the Romans?',
        '"Phoebe","Chloe","Priscilla","Lydia"'::text[],
        'Phoebe',
        'Paul commended Phoebe, a deaconess of the church at Cenchreae (the eastern port of Corinth), who had been a patron of many and of Paul himself.',
        'Romans 16:1-2',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Early Church Leaders","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"early-leaders","mechanic":"early-leaders","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I served the congregation in Cenchreae, the bustling eastern harbor of Corinth.","Paul honored me with the title of diakonos and recognized me as a patron/benefactor.","I had the historic honor of physically transporting Paul''s theological masterpiece to Rome."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l38-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        38,
        3,
        'Which tentmaking husband-and-wife team had fled Rome under Emperor Claudius'' edict, welcomed Paul into their home and workshop in Corinth, and risked their necks for his life?',
        '"Aquila and Priscilla","Ananias and Sapphira","Philemon and Apphia","Andronicus and Junia"'::text[],
        'Aquila and Priscilla',
        'Aquila, a native of Pontus, and his wife Priscilla were leatherworkers/tentmakers like Paul; they hosted a church in their home and risked their lives for Paul.',
        'Acts 18:1-3; Romans 16:3-4',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Early Church Leaders","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"early-leaders","mechanic":"early-leaders","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We were Jewish refugees expelled from the capital by the imperial decree of Claudius.","We shared the identical trade of leatherworking and tent manufacturing with Paul.","All the churches of the Gentiles give thanks for our courageous life-risking loyalty."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l38-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        38,
        4,
        'Which Levite from Cyprus sold his field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet, earning the nickname ''Son of Encouragement'' from the Twelve?',
        '"Matthias","Mnason","Stephen","Barnabas (Joseph)"'::text[],
        'Barnabas (Joseph)',
        'Joseph, a Levite of Cypriot origin, was surnamed Barnabas (''Son of Encouragement'') by the apostles after selling an agricultural tract and donating all proceeds.',
        'Acts 4:36-37',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Early Church Leaders","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"early-leaders","mechanic":"early-leaders","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My birth name was Joseph, born of the priestly tribe of Levi in Cyprus.","I sponsored the suspected persecutor Saul when all the Jerusalem disciples feared him.","The apostles gave me an affectionate Aramaic surname celebrating my gift of encouragement."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l38-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        38,
        5,
        'Which prominent Corinthian Christian is described in Romans 16:23 as ''host to me and to the whole church'', whom Paul personally baptized along with Crispus?',
        '"Gaius","Quartus","Erastus","Stephanas"'::text[],
        'Gaius',
        'Gaius was Paul''s generous host in Corinth whose home was large enough to accommodate the entire assembled city church.',
        'Romans 16:23; 1 Corinthians 1:14',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Early Church Leaders","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"early-leaders","mechanic":"early-leaders","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was one of the very few converts Paul personally baptized in Corinth.","My home was spacious enough to host gatherings for the entire urban congregation.","Paul wrote the final greeting of Romans while enjoying my gracious hospitality."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l39-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        39,
        1,
        'Which Roman centurion of the Italian Cohort stationed in Caesarea was a devout God-fearer who gave alms generously, and was instructed by an angel to send for Peter at Joppa?',
        '"Julius","Publius","Cornelius","Sergius Paulus"'::text[],
        'Cornelius',
        'Cornelius was a devout centurion whose prayers and alms ascended as a memorial before God; Peter preached to his household and the Holy Spirit fell on them.',
        'Acts 10:1-8, 44-48',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Conversion Stories","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"conversion-stories","mechanic":"conversion-stories","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I commanded a unit of one hundred soldiers in the prestigious Italian Cohort.","An angel visited me at the ninth hour of prayer while I fasted.","My home became the landmark site where Gentiles first received the Holy Spirit and baptism."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l39-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        39,
        2,
        'Which wealthy businesswoman from Thyatira who sold expensive purple textiles in Philippi had her heart opened by the Lord to pay attention to Paul''s message, and baptized her whole house?',
        '"Chloe","Lydia","Phoebe","Priscilla"'::text[],
        'Lydia',
        'Lydia was a worshiper of God from Thyatira; the Lord opened her heart, and she was baptized along with her household, urging Paul to lodge at her house.',
        'Acts 16:14-15',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Conversion Stories","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"conversion-stories","mechanic":"conversion-stories","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an immigrant merchant originating from the textile hub of Thyatira.","I was praying by a riverbank outside Philippi on the Sabbath when missionaries arrived.","I became the very first recorded Christian convert on the continent of Europe."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l39-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        39,
        3,
        'Which Roman civil official in Philippi drew his sword to commit suicide after a midnight earthquake flapped open all prison doors, before Paul shouted: ''Do not harm yourself, for we are all here!''?',
        '"The Philippian Jailer","The Chief Magistrate","The City Praetor","The Town Clerk"'::text[],
        'The Philippian Jailer',
        'The Philippian jailer fell trembling before Paul and Silas, asked ''What must I do to be saved?'', washed their flogging stripes, and was baptized that night with his entire family.',
        'Acts 16:27-34',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Conversion Stories","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"conversion-stories","mechanic":"conversion-stories","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["Roman law held me personally liable on pain of death if any prisoner escaped.","A violent midnight earthquake shattered cell walls and snapped iron fetters.","I washed my prisoners'' lacerated backs and shared a joyful midnight meal with them."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l39-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        39,
        4,
        'Which member of the prestigious Athenian judicial council of the Areopagus believed Paul''s gospel after hearing him address the altar ''To the Unknown God'' on Mars Hill?',
        '"Justus","Theophilus","Gallio","Dionysius the Areopagite"'::text[],
        'Dionysius the Areopagite',
        'Acts 17:34 notes that among those who joined Paul in Athens and believed was Dionysius the Areopagite, alongside a prominent woman named Damaris.',
        'Acts 17:34',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Conversion Stories","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"conversion-stories","mechanic":"conversion-stories","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I sat as an elite judicial magistrate on the supreme legal council of Athens.","I listened to Paul critique Greek philosophy and announce the resurrection of the dead.","While many mocked, I embraced the gospel of Christ along with a woman named Damaris."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l39-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        39,
        5,
        'Which synagogue ruler in Corinth believed in the Lord with his entire household after hearing Paul preach, prompting many Corinthians to hear, believe, and be baptized?',
        '"Sosthenes","Jairus","Alexander","Crispus"'::text[],
        'Crispus',
        'Crispus, the ruler of the synagogue, believed in the Lord together with his entire household; Paul noted in 1 Corinthians 1:14 that he personally baptized Crispus.',
        'Acts 18:8; 1 Corinthians 1:14',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Conversion Stories","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"conversion-stories","mechanic":"conversion-stories","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the highest presiding administrative officer of the Jewish synagogue in Corinth.","My public conversion to Christ shook the entire local Jewish community.","Paul personally baptized me with his own hands alongside Gaius."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l40-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        40,
        1,
        'Which synagogue leader in Corinth was dragged before the judgment seat (bema) of Proconsul Gallio and beaten by the crowd when Gallio refused to judge Jewish religious laws?',
        '"Crispus","Alexander","Sosthenes","Jason"'::text[],
        'Sosthenes',
        'The mob seized Sosthenes, the ruler of the synagogue, and beat him before the judgment seat, but Gallio paid no attention; Sosthenes later appears as Paul''s brother in 1 Cor 1:1.',
        'Acts 18:17; 1 Corinthians 1:1',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Missionary Challenge","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"missionary-challenge","mechanic":"missionary-challenge","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I stepped into the synagogue leadership after Crispus converted to Christianity.","Angry onlookers battered me publicly right in front of the Roman tribunal chair.","I subsequently converted and co-authored the opening greeting of First Corinthians with Paul."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l40-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        40,
        2,
        'Which silversmith in Ephesus manufactured silver shrines of the pagan goddess Artemis and ignited a massive citywide riot when Paul''s preaching threatened his lucrative trade?',
        '"Demetrius","Philetus","Alexander","Hermogenes"'::text[],
        'Demetrius',
        'Demetrius gathered fellow craftsmen warning that Paul''s message that man-made gods are not gods threatened their trade and Artemis'' magnificence, sparking a two-hour riot.',
        'Acts 19:24-29',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Missionary Challenge","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"missionary-challenge","mechanic":"missionary-challenge","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["My guild created miniature silver souvenirs of one of the Seven Wonders of the World.","I gathered unionized artisan craftsmen to defend our financial bottom line.","My inflammatory speech filled the entire metropolis with hysterical chanting for Artemis."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l40-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        40,
        3,
        'Which Roman military tribune in Jerusalem rescued Paul from a murderous mob in the temple courts, wrote a letter to Governor Felix, and transferred Paul by night with 470 soldiers?',
        '"Claudius Lysias","Julius","Cornelius","Publius"'::text[],
        'Claudius Lysias',
        'Claudius Lysias, the chiliarch (commander of 1,000 soldiers in the Antonia Fortress), rescued Paul from assassination and sent him under heavy military guard to Caesarea.',
        'Acts 21:31-33; Acts 23:26',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Missionary Challenge","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"missionary-challenge","mechanic":"missionary-challenge","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I purchased my prized Roman citizenship for an exorbitant sum of money.","I rushed down with legionary centurions to stop a public lynching in the temple.","I drafted an official military dispatch to Governor Felix and assigned 470 troops to escort Paul."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l40-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        40,
        4,
        'Which professional orator and trial lawyer was hired by High Priest Ananias and Jewish elders to present formal treason charges against Paul before Roman Governor Felix at Caesarea?',
        '"Gallio","Gamaliel","Alexander","Tertullus"'::text[],
        'Tertullus',
        'Ananias came down with elders and an orator named Tertullus, who flattered Felix and accused Paul of being a plague, an instigator of riots, and a ringleader of the Nazarene sect.',
        'Acts 24:1-8',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Missionary Challenge","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"missionary-challenge","mechanic":"missionary-challenge","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an eloquent courtroom advocate skilled in Roman jurisprudence and classical rhetoric.","I opened my case with lavish sycophantic flattery toward Governor Felix.","I labeled Paul a biological plague and the ringleader of an illegal seditious sect."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l40-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        40,
        5,
        'Which Roman centurion belonging to the prestigious Augustan Cohort was entrusted with transporting Paul and other imperial prisoners by sea from Caesarea to Rome?',
        '"Julius","Cornelius","Claudius Lysias","Publius"'::text[],
        'Julius',
        'Paul was delivered to a centurion of the Augustan Cohort named Julius, who treated Paul kindly, allowed his friends to attend him, and prevented the sailors from killing prisoners.',
        'Acts 27:1-3',
        '{"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Early Church","level_theme":"Missionary Challenge","category":"The Early Church","challengeType":"missionary-challenge","mechanic":"missionary-challenge","difficulty":"very-hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an officer in the elite Augustan Cohort of the imperial army.","I permitted Paul to visit Christian companions during a port stop in Sidon.","During the shipwreck at Malta, I ordered the soldiers not to kill the prisoners to save Paul''s life."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l41-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        41,
        1,
        'Which eighty-year-old Gileadite nobleman from Rogelim provided beds, basins, wheat, barley, honey, and cheese to sustain King David and his troops when fleeing Absalom at Mahanaim?',
        '"Shobi son of Nahash","Machir son of Ammiel","Chimham","Barzillai the Gileadite"'::text[],
        'Barzillai the Gileadite',
        'Barzillai was a very aged and wealthy Gileadite who provided King David food during Absalom''s revolt; David invited him to Jerusalem, but he sent his son Chimham in his stead.',
        '2 Samuel 17:27-29; 2 Samuel 19:31-39',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Minor Character Test","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"minor-characters","mechanic":"minor-characters","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an eighty-year-old pastoral patriarch living beyond the Jordan in Rogelim.","I hauled wagonloads of food, cheese, and supplies to David''s exhausted forces at Mahanaim.","When David offered me a permanent royal pension, I declined due to my advanced age."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l41-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        41,
        2,
        'Which Philistine military exile from Gath arrived with 600 men and swore unwavering loyalty to King David during Absalom''s rebellion, saying ''In whatever place my lord the king shall be... there will your servant be''?',
        '"Ittai the Gittite","Uriah the Hittite","Ahimelech","Benaiah son of Jehoiada"'::text[],
        'Ittai the Gittite',
        'Ittai the Gittite, a foreigner from Goliath''s hometown, refused David''s offer to turn back and was given command of one-third of David''s royal army in battle.',
        '2 Samuel 15:19-22; 2 Samuel 18:2',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Minor Character Test","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"minor-characters","mechanic":"minor-characters","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an alien commander from the Philistine stronghold of Gath.","I had only recently arrived with 600 veteran warriors when civil war erupted.","David placed one-third of his entire combat army under my strategic command."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l41-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        41,
        3,
        'Which concubine of Saul, daughter of Aiah, took sackcloth and spread it for herself on a rock, guarding the hanging corpses of her two sons from birds and beasts from barley harvest until rain fell?',
        '"Michal","Merab","Abital","Rizpah"'::text[],
        'Rizpah',
        'Rizpah watched vigilantly over the bodies of her sons Armoni and Mephibosheth whom the Gibeonites hanged, defending their remains until David gathered their bones for honorable burial.',
        '2 Samuel 21:8-14',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Minor Character Test","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"minor-characters","mechanic":"minor-characters","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a royal concubine in King Saul''s household.","Two of my sons were executed by the Gibeonites to avenge Saul''s bloodguilt.","I conducted a solitary five-month vigil on bare stone, chasing off vultures and hyenas."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l41-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        41,
        4,
        'Which lame son of Jonathan was sought out by King David for Jonathan''s sake, restored all Saul''s family estates, and dined continuously at the royal palace table like a king''s son?',
        '"Ish-bosheth","Michal","Mephibosheth (Merib-baal)","Armoni"'::text[],
        'Mephibosheth (Merib-baal)',
        'David asked if any survived of Saul''s house that he might show kindness for Jonathan''s sake; Mephibosheth, lame in both feet from a nurse''s fall, was brought from Lo-debar.',
        '2 Samuel 9:6-13',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Minor Character Test","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"minor-characters","mechanic":"minor-characters","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was five years old when news came that my father and grandfather died on Gilboa.","My nurse dropped me in panicked flight, leaving both my feet permanently crippled.","David brought me from obscurity in Lo-debar to eat as family at the sovereign table."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l41-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        41,
        5,
        'Which deceitful steward of Saul''s estate told David that Mephibosheth was treasonously hoping to reclaim Saul''s kingdom, deceiving David into granting him all his master''s property?',
        '"Ahithophel","Ziba","Shimei","Doeg"'::text[],
        'Ziba',
        'Ziba brought David bread and summer fruit while slandering Mephibosheth; when David returned victorious, Mephibosheth had not cared for his feet or clothes in mourning, exposing Ziba''s deceit.',
        '2 Samuel 16:1-4; 2 Samuel 19:24-30',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Minor Character Test","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"minor-characters","mechanic":"minor-characters","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I had fifteen sons and twenty servants managing Saul''s former farmland.","I brought wine and provisions to David during his flight to curry opportunistic favor.","I falsely accused my disabled master of celebrating the king''s downfall."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l42-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        42,
        1,
        'Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own?',
        '"Jochebed and Miriam","Bilhah and Zilpah","Rachel and Leah","Shiphrah and Puah"'::text[],
        'Shiphrah and Puah',
        'The king of Egypt ordered Hebrew midwives Shiphrah and Puah to kill male babies; because they feared God and preserved the boys, God gave them households.',
        'Exodus 1:15-21',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Women of the Bible","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"women-of-bible","mechanic":"women-of-bible","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["Our names are preserved forever in Scripture while Pharaoh''s name is forgotten.","We practiced courageous civil disobedience against genocidal state legislation.","We told Pharaoh that Hebrew women gave birth before the midwife arrived."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l42-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        42,
        2,
        'Which five brave sisters from the tribe of Manasseh boldly approached Moses and the congregation claiming that their deceased father''s inheritance should not be lost because he had no sons?',
        '"Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah","Miriam, Deborah, Huldah, Anna, and Phoebe","Tryphena, Tryphosa, Persis, Junia, and Chloe","Leah, Rachel, Bilhah, Zilpah, and Dinah"'::text[],
        'Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah',
        'The daughters of Zelophehad (Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah) successfully petitioned Moses for property rights, establishing landmark inheritance laws in Israel.',
        'Numbers 27:1-7; Joshua 17:3',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Women of the Bible","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"women-of-bible","mechanic":"women-of-bible","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["Our father Zelophehad died in the wilderness without having any sons.","We stood together at the entrance of the Tabernacle before Moses and the elders.","God affirmed our petition: ''The daughters of Zelophehad speak right; you shall give them possession.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l42-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        42,
        3,
        'Which Midianite princess, daughter of Zur, was boldly brought into the camp of Israel by Zimri during the Baal of Peor crisis, and was executed by Phinehas with a javelin?',
        '"Cozbi","Shelomith","Keturah","Zipporah"'::text[],
        'Cozbi',
        'Phinehas, grandson of Aaron, took a spear and pierced Zimri of Simeon and Cozbi, daughter of a Midianite prince, turning away God''s fierce anger and ending the plague.',
        'Numbers 25:6-18',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Women of the Bible","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"women-of-bible","mechanic":"women-of-bible","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My father was Zur, a tribal chieftain and king of Midian.","My brazen entry into Israel''s camp with a Simeonite prince defied the weeping leaders.","A priest''s javelin pierced both of us, arresting a plague that had wiped out 24,000."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l42-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        42,
        4,
        'In Romans 16:12, which two Christian women are singled out and greeted by Paul by name as having ''labored hard in the Lord''?',
        '"Lois and Eunice","Euodia and Syntyche","Tryphena and Tryphosa","Martha and Mary"'::text[],
        'Tryphena and Tryphosa',
        'Paul writes: ''Greet Tryphena and Tryphosa, those women who work hard in the Lord. Greet the beloved Persis, who has worked hard in the Lord.''',
        'Romans 16:12',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Women of the Bible","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"women-of-bible","mechanic":"women-of-bible","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["Our Greek names derived from words signifying luxurious delicacy.","In contrast to our names, we worked until exhausted in Christian kingdom service.","Paul sends personal apostolic salutations to both of us in Romans 16."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l42-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        42,
        5,
        'In Romans 16:7, which prominent Jewish-Christian woman is greeted alongside Andronicus as Paul''s fellow countryman and fellow prisoner, who was ''well known among the apostles''?',
        '"Priscilla","Chloe","Junia","Phoebe"'::text[],
        'Junia',
        'Paul greets Andronicus and Junia, ''my kinsmen and my fellow prisoners. They are well known to the apostles, and they were in Christ before me.''',
        'Romans 16:7',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Women of the Bible","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"women-of-bible","mechanic":"women-of-bible","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I became a believer in Jesus Christ before Saul of Tarsus was converted.","I endured incarceration in Roman prison alongside the Apostle Paul.","Paul honored my partner Andronicus and me as outstanding among the messengers/apostles."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l43-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        43,
        1,
        'Which craftsman from the tribe of Judah was filled with the Spirit of God in wisdom and craftsmanship to design and construct the Tabernacle and its sacred furniture?',
        '"Oholiab son of Ahisamach","Hur","Hiram-abi","Bezalel son of Uri"'::text[],
        'Bezalel son of Uri',
        'God specifically named Bezalel son of Uri, son of Hur, of Judah, filling him with divine skill to craft gold, silver, bronze, stones, and wood for the sanctuary.',
        'Exodus 31:1-5; Exodus 35:30',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Unusual Names","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"unusual-names","mechanic":"unusual-names","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My name literally means ''in the shadow of God.''","I was the first person in Scripture explicitly described as filled with the Spirit of God.","I personally directed the casting and fabrication of the Ark of the Covenant."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l43-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        43,
        2,
        'Which judge of Israel delivered the nation by striking down six hundred Philistine warriors using only an agricultural oxgoad?',
        '"Ehud","Shamgar son of Anath","Tola","Othniel"'::text[],
        'Shamgar son of Anath',
        'After Ehud came Shamgar son of Anath, who struck down 600 Philistines with an oxgoad; he also delivered Israel.',
        'Judges 3:31',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Unusual Names","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"unusual-names","mechanic":"unusual-names","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I am mentioned in only two verses across the entire Old Testament.","I wielded an eight-foot iron-tipped cattle stick instead of a military broadsword.","I single-handedly slew six hundred hostile Philistine invaders."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l43-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        43,
        3,
        'Which valiant commander of David''s royal bodyguard struck down two lion-like champions of Moab, chased and killed a lion in a snowy pit, and slew an Egyptian giant?',
        '"Eleazar son of Dodo","Benaiah son of Jehoiada","Abishai","Asahel"'::text[],
        'Benaiah son of Jehoiada',
        'Benaiah son of Jehoiada from Kabzeel performed heroic feats including slaying a lion in a pit on a snowy day; Solomon promoted him to supreme commander of the army.',
        '2 Samuel 23:20-23; 1 Kings 2:34-35',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Unusual Names","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"unusual-names","mechanic":"unusual-names","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I hailed from the southern town of Kabzeel in Judah.","On a freezing winter day, I leapt into an underground cistern to battle a live lion.","I snatched a spear like a weaver''s beam out of an Egyptian giant''s hands and killed him."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l43-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        43,
        4,
        'Which symbolic child was fathered by the prophet Isaiah, whose name meant ''Quick to the plunder, swift to the spoil'', signifying Damascus and Samaria''s sudden fall?',
        '"Lo-Ammi","Immanuel","Shear-jashub","Maher-shalal-hash-baz"'::text[],
        'Maher-shalal-hash-baz',
        'God commanded Isaiah to write on a large tablet ''Maher-shalal-hash-baz'' and name his newborn son this to show Assyria would plunder Damascus and Samaria.',
        'Isaiah 8:1-4',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Unusual Names","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"unusual-names","mechanic":"unusual-names","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I bore the longest personal name found anywhere in the Bible.","My father had to record my name on a legal billboard before reliable witnesses.","Before I could speak ''my father'' or ''my mother'', Assyria pillaged Syria and Israel."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l43-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        43,
        5,
        'In 2 Timothy 1:15, which two Christians from the province of Asia are named by Paul with sorrow as having abandoned and turned away from him during his final imprisonment?',
        '"Phygelus and Hermogenes","Alexander and Demas","Euodia and Syntyche","Hymenaeus and Philetus"'::text[],
        'Phygelus and Hermogenes',
        'Paul wrote: ''You are aware that all who are in Asia turned away from me, among whom are Phygelus and Hermogenes.''',
        '2 Timothy 1:15',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Unusual Names","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"unusual-names","mechanic":"unusual-names","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We were prominent believers from the Roman province of Asia.","When Paul was arrested and brought to the death row dungeon in Rome, we shunned him.","Paul recorded our names in infamy in his final canonical letter."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l44-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        44,
        1,
        'Which enigmatic king of Salem and priest of God Most High in Genesis 14 is highlighted in Hebrews 7 as a royal-priestly prototype of Jesus Christ without genealogy?',
        '"Balaam","Abimelech","Jethro","Melchizedek"'::text[],
        'Melchizedek',
        'Melchizedek brought out bread and wine to Abraham; Hebrews portrays his priesthood as perpetual, superior to Levi, foreshadowing Christ''s eternal high priesthood.',
        'Genesis 14:18-20; Psalm 110:4; Hebrews 7:1-17',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Hidden Connections","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"hidden-connections","mechanic":"hidden-connections","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["My dual titles mean ''King of Righteousness'' and ''King of Peace.''","Abraham tithed one-tenth of all his battle spoils to me.","The Messiah is sworn with an oath to be a priest forever according to my order."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l44-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        44,
        2,
        'Which Mesopotamian diviner hired by Balak king of Moab to curse Israel is explicitly condemned in 2 Peter, Jude, and Revelation for teaching Balak to set a stumbling block?',
        '"Korah","Sanballat","Balaak","Balaam son of Beor"'::text[],
        'Balaam son of Beor',
        'Balaam loved the wages of unrighteousness; Revelation 2:14 condemns the Nicolaitans who held the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balak to entice Israel to eat idol meat and commit sexual immorality.',
        'Numbers 22-24; 2 Peter 2:15; Jude 1:11; Revelation 2:14',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Hidden Connections","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"hidden-connections","mechanic":"hidden-connections","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["A speaking donkey saved my life from an angelic executioner with a drawn sword.","God constrained my mouth to pronounce majestic blessings over Israel.","I covertly orchestrated Israel''s downfall through idolatrous seduction at Baal-peor."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l44-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        44,
        3,
        'Which Levite rebel led 250 prominent community leaders against Moses and Aaron in Numbers 16, whose fatal rebellion is linked in Jude 11 with the error of Balaam?',
        '"Dathan son of Eliab","On son of Peleth","Abiram son of Eliab","Korah son of Izhar"'::text[],
        'Korah son of Izhar',
        'Korah challenged the priestly monopoly of Aaron; the earth opened its mouth and swallowed him and his conspirators alive; Jude warns false teachers perish in Korah''s rebellion.',
        'Numbers 16:1-35; Jude 1:11',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Hidden Connections","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"hidden-connections","mechanic":"hidden-connections","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was Moses and Aaron''s first cousin, belonging to the Kohathite clan of Levi.","I organized a political mutiny claiming ''all the congregation are holy, every one of them.''","The solid earth split apart under our tents, swallowing our households alive into Sheol."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l44-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        44,
        4,
        'In 2 Timothy 3:8, which two traditional names does Paul reveal for the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses before Pharaoh, comparing them to corrupt end-times teachers?',
        '"Hymenaeus and Philetus","Dathan and Abiram","Sanballat and Tobiah","Jannes and Jambres"'::text[],
        'Jannes and Jambres',
        'Paul writes: ''Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so these men also oppose the truth, men of corrupt minds and disqualified regarding the faith.''',
        '2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Hidden Connections","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"hidden-connections","mechanic":"hidden-connections","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["We utilized ancient Egyptian occult arts to replicate the early plagues of blood and frogs.","Our enchantments collapsed completely when lice were summoned from dust.","Paul revealed our specific personal names over a millennium after the Exodus."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l44-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        44,
        5,
        'In Jude 1:14-15, which pre-flood patriarch, ''the seventh from Adam'', is cited as prophesying: ''Behold, the Lord comes with ten thousands of His holy ones''?',
        '"Methuselah","Noah","Enoch","Lamech"'::text[],
        'Enoch',
        'Jude quotes Enoch, the seventh from Adam, who prophesied the Lord''s return in judgment upon all ungodly persons.',
        'Jude 1:14-15; Genesis 5:21-24',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Hidden Connections","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"hidden-connections","mechanic":"hidden-connections","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the father of Methuselah and walked intimately with God.","I never experienced physical death because God took me away.","Jude quotes my ancient apocalyptic prophecy of the Lord executing global judgment."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l45-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        45,
        1,
        'In Romans 16:22, what is the personal name of the amanuensis (secretary) who actually penned the ink on the manuscript of Paul''s Epistle to the Romans?',
        '"Quartus","Gaius","Erastus","Tertius"'::text[],
        'Tertius',
        'Romans 16:22 includes the scribe''s direct greeting: ''I Tertius, who wrote down this letter, greet you in the Lord.''',
        'Romans 16:22',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"forgotten-boss","mechanic":"forgotten-boss","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the professional Christian scribe who transcribed Paul''s dictation.","My Latin name literally means ''the Third.''","I inserted my own brief personal greeting right inside the closing doxology of Romans."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l45-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        45,
        2,
        'Which Christian brother is briefly greeted right beside Tertius in Romans 16:23 with the simple, affectionate title ''Quartus, a brother''?',
        '"Quartus","Gaius","Erastus","Stephanas"'::text[],
        'Quartus',
        'Paul writes: ''Erastus, the city treasurer, greets you, and Quartus, a brother.''',
        'Romans 16:23',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"forgotten-boss","mechanic":"forgotten-boss","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["My Latin name indicates I was likely named ''the Fourth.''","I held no flashy ecclesiastical office or civic title.","Scripture immortalized my name for two thousand years simply as ''a brother.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l45-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        45,
        3,
        'Which civic official in Corinth is described in Romans 16:23 as the ''city treasurer'' (or director of public works) whose name has been confirmed on a 1st-century pavement inscription in Corinth?',
        '"Sosthenes","Gaius","Crispus","Erastus"'::text[],
        'Erastus',
        'Erastus, the city treasurer (oikonomos), greeted Rome; archaeologists in Corinth excavated a limestone pavement reading ''Erastus in return for his aedileship paved it at his own expense.''',
        'Romans 16:23; Acts 19:22',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"forgotten-boss","mechanic":"forgotten-boss","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I held high political and fiscal office as treasurer of a major Roman commercial colony.","I embraced the humble apostolic message and supported missionary journeys.","My civic dedication was unearthed by modern archaeologists in Corinth in 1929."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l45-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        45,
        4,
        'Which faithful believer from Ephesus repeatedly sought out Paul in chains in Rome, was not ashamed of his imprisonment, and refreshed his spirit?',
        '"Philemon","Tychicus","Epaphras","Onesiphorus"'::text[],
        'Onesiphorus',
        'Paul prayed mercy on the household of Onesiphorus, for he often refreshed Paul, was not ashamed of his chains, and searched diligently for him in Rome until he found him.',
        '2 Timothy 1:16-18',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"forgotten-boss","mechanic":"forgotten-boss","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["While Asian believers abandoned Paul in imperial custody, I went hunting for his dungeon.","I walked through the dangerous Roman streets until I discovered the apostle''s cell.","Paul prayed that the Lord would grant mercy to my household on the Day of Judgment."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l45-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        45,
        5,
        'In 2 Timothy 4:13, in whose home at Troas did Paul leave his winter traveling cloak, books, and especially the parchments, asking Timothy to bring them before winter?',
        '"Carpus","Philemon","Trophimus","Erastus"'::text[],
        'Carpus',
        'Paul instructed Timothy: ''When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, also the books, and above all the parchments.''',
        '2 Timothy 4:13',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","category":"The People You Might Have Forgotten","challengeType":"forgotten-boss","mechanic":"forgotten-boss","difficulty":"expert","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I resided in the Aegean maritime harbor city of Troas.","Paul lodged in my home and left valuable personal belongings in my safekeeping.","In his chilly death row cell, the apostle desperately requested the heavy mantle I was guarding."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l46-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        46,
        1,
        '• I was David''s premier counselor whose advice was esteemed like the oracle of God.
• I defected to join Absalom''s conspiracy against David.
• When my battle advice was rejected in favor of Hushai, I went home, put my house in order, and hanged myself.
Who am I?',
        '"Joab son of Zeruiah","Ahithophel the Gilonite","Abiathar the Priest","Hushai the Archite"'::text[],
        'Ahithophel the Gilonite',
        'Ahithophel''s strategic advice was regarded as God''s word; when Absalom chose Hushai''s plan instead, Ahithophel went home and hanged himself.',
        '2 Samuel 15:12; 2 Samuel 16:23; 2 Samuel 17:23',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Three Clues, One Person","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"three-clues","mechanic":"three-clues","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I hailed from the town of Giloh in the hill country of Judah.","I was the grandfather of Bathsheba, whom David wronged.","I was David''s close companion whose treason prefigured Judas Iscariot in Psalm 41."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l46-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        46,
        2,
        '• I was the grandson of Aaron the high priest through Eleazar.
• When an Israelite prince brought a Midianite woman into the camp, my righteous anger was kindled.
• God made with me and my descendants an everlasting covenant of peace and priesthood.
Who am I?',
        '"Ithamar","Nadab","Abihu","Phinehas son of Eleazar"'::text[],
        'Phinehas son of Eleazar',
        'Phinehas executed Zimri and Cozbi with a spear, turning away God''s wrath; Psalm 106 records that this was counted to him as righteousness for all generations.',
        'Numbers 25:7-13; Psalm 106:30-31',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Three Clues, One Person","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"three-clues","mechanic":"three-clues","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the third high priest in Israel''s history.","I halted a deadly divine plague that had slaughtered 24,000 Israelites at Shittim.","Scripture records that my righteous action was counted to me as righteousness forever."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l46-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        46,
        3,
        '• I was an Egyptian-born Hebrew prince who murdered an overseer and fled into exile.
• I spent forty years tending sheep for a Midianite priest at Mount Horeb.
• I stood on the Mount of Transfiguration speaking with Jesus about His departure.
Who am I?',
        '"Joseph","Elijah","Joshua","Moses"'::text[],
        'Moses',
        'Moses fled Egypt to Midian, served as shepherd 40 years, led Israel 40 years, and appeared in glory on the Mount of Transfiguration with Elijah talking to Jesus.',
        'Exodus 2:11-15; Exodus 3:1; Luke 9:30-31',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Three Clues, One Person","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"three-clues","mechanic":"three-clues","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was hidden in a papyrus basket among the reeds of the Nile.","I spoke with God face to face, as a man speaks to his intimate friend.","I appeared in heavenly glory on a high mountain discussing Christ''s coming exodus at Jerusalem."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l46-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        46,
        4,
        '• I was born a Levite in Cyprus, yet sold my real estate to lay all proceeds at the apostles'' feet.
• I took the former persecutor Saul by the hand and introduced him to skeptical apostles in Jerusalem.
• I later parted ways with Paul over giving my young cousin John Mark a second chance.
Who am I?',
        '"Luke","Timothy","Barnabas","Silas"'::text[],
        'Barnabas',
        'Barnabas, son of encouragement, championed Saul when everyone doubted him, traveled on the first missionary journey, and mentored John Mark after separating from Paul.',
        'Acts 4:36-37; Acts 9:27; Acts 15:37-39',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Three Clues, One Person","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"three-clues","mechanic":"three-clues","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["My real birth name was Joseph, born on the Mediterranean island of Cyprus.","I traveled to Tarsus specifically to recruit Paul to co-pastor the church at Antioch.","My willingness to restore fallen young workers preserved Mark for the Kingdom."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l46-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        46,
        5,
        '• I was a king of Judah who ascended the throne at age eight.
• When Hilkiah found the long-lost Book of the Law, I tore my clothes in sorrow.
• I carried out the most thorough religious purge in Judah''s history, destroying the high places and Bethel''s altar.
Who am I?',
        '"Hezekiah","Joash","Manasseh","Josiah"'::text[],
        'Josiah',
        'Josiah reigned 31 years, repaired the temple, restored the Passover, and destroyed idolatrous shrines; the prophet from Judah had prophesied him by name 300 years earlier.',
        '2 Kings 22:1-2; 2 Kings 23:15-25',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Three Clues, One Person","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"three-clues","mechanic":"three-clues","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["A prophet from Judah predicted my exact name three centuries before I was born.","I began to seek the God of my father David when I was only sixteen years old.","There was no king before me or after me who turned to the Lord with all his heart like I did."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l47-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        47,
        1,
        'Who were the father and mother of Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, both belonging to the tribe of Levi?',
        '"Kohath and Elisheba","Amram and Jochebed","Elkanah and Hannah","Zechariah and Elizabeth"'::text[],
        'Amram and Jochebed',
        'Amram married his father''s sister Jochebed, and she bore him Aaron, Moses, and their sister Miriam.',
        'Exodus 6:20; Numbers 26:59',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Family Tree Trap","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"family-tree-trap","mechanic":"family-tree-trap","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["Our household gave birth to the three foremost leaders of the Exodus.","Our son Aaron was the first high priest, our son Moses was the lawgiver, and our daughter Miriam was a prophetess.","Our names are recorded in the priestly genealogy of Exodus 6 and Numbers 26."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l47-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        47,
        2,
        'According to 1 Samuel 14:50-51, what was the precise familial relationship between King Saul and his supreme military commander Abner?',
        '"Abner was Saul's brother-in-law","Saul and Abner were first cousins (Abner was son of Ner, Saul's uncle)","Saul and Abner were half-brothers","Abner was Saul's nephew"'::text[],
        'Saul and Abner were first cousins (Abner was son of Ner, Saul''s uncle)',
        'Kish was the father of Saul, and Ner the father of Abner was Saul''s uncle (Ner was son of Abiel, making Saul and Abner first cousins).',
        '1 Samuel 14:50-51',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Family Tree Trap","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"family-tree-trap","mechanic":"family-tree-trap","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["Our fathers Kish and Ner were blood brothers, sons of Abiel.","One of us was the anointed monarch and the other was his commanding general.","Our shared Benjamite clan ties cemented our military coalition."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l47-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        47,
        3,
        'Which of David''s older brothers was the firstborn of Jesse, whose towering height and handsome appearance led the prophet Samuel to wrongly conclude: ''Surely the Lord''s anointed is before Him''?',
        '"Abinadab","Eliab","Shimea","Nethanel"'::text[],
        'Eliab',
        'When Samuel saw Eliab, he was impressed by his height; but God said: ''Do not look on his appearance... for man looks on the outward appearance, but the Lord looks on the heart.''',
        '1 Samuel 16:6-7; 1 Samuel 17:28',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Family Tree Trap","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"family-tree-trap","mechanic":"family-tree-trap","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the tall, imposing firstborn son of Jesse of Bethlehem.","I scolded young David when he arrived at the Valley of Elah with cheese and bread.","The Lord rejected my outward regal bearing in favor of my shepherd little brother."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l47-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        47,
        4,
        'According to Colossians 4:10, what was the exact family connection between John Mark (the author of Mark''s Gospel) and the apostle Barnabas?',
        '"John Mark was the younger brother of Barnabas","John Mark was the son-in-law of Barnabas","John Mark was the nephew of Barnabas","John Mark was the cousin of Barnabas"'::text[],
        'John Mark was the cousin of Barnabas',
        'Paul explicitly writes in Colossians 4:10: ''Mark the cousin of Barnabas (concerning whom you have received instructions).'' (Greek: anepsios, cousin).',
        'Colossians 4:10',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Family Tree Trap","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"family-tree-trap","mechanic":"family-tree-trap","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["Our shared family had wealth and prominent homes in Jerusalem and Cyprus.","My mother Mary hosted the prayer meeting when Peter was delivered from prison.","My influential cousin Barnabas championed me even when Paul refused to travel with me."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l47-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        47,
        5,
        'According to Mark 15:21 and Romans 16:13, which two brothers were the sons of Simon of Cyrene, one of whom was greeted by Paul as ''chosen in the Lord'' along with his mother?',
        '"Hermogenes and Philetus","James and John","Tryphena and Tryphosa","Alexander and Rufus"'::text[],
        'Alexander and Rufus',
        'Mark identifies Simon of Cyrene as ''the father of Alexander and Rufus''; in Romans 16:13 Paul greets ''Rufus, chosen in the Lord, and his mother, who has been a mother to me, too.''',
        'Mark 15:21; Romans 16:13',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Family Tree Trap","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"family-tree-trap","mechanic":"family-tree-trap","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["Our father was the North African pilgrim conscripted to carry Jesus'' wooden cross.","Our names were well known in the Roman congregation where Mark first published his Gospel.","Paul sent special greetings to one of us, saying his mother had treated Paul as her own son."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l48-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        48,
        1,
        'Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Thrown into a pit at Dothan -> Sold to Potiphar -> Imprisoned on false charges -> Interpreted Pharaoh''s dreams -> Became Prime Minister of Egypt?',
        '"David","Joseph","Moses","Daniel"'::text[],
        'Joseph',
        'Joseph was sold at Dothan, worked in Potiphar''s house, was falsely accused by Potiphar''s wife, interpreted dreams in prison, and was elevated to second-in-command of Egypt at age thirty.',
        'Genesis 37-41',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Life Story Puzzle","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"life-story-puzzle","mechanic":"life-story-puzzle","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was my father''s pampered favorite who wore an ornate multicolored robe.","I went from a dry desert cistern to an Egyptian slave market to a royal palace.","I told my weeping brothers: ''You meant evil against me, but God meant it for good.''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l48-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        48,
        2,
        'Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Anointed as shepherd boy in Bethlehem -> Felled Goliath with a sling -> Fled as fugitive to Cave of Adullam -> Anointed king in Hebron -> Captured Jerusalem as national capital?',
        '"David","Solomon","Jehu","Saul"'::text[],
        'David',
        'David was anointed by Samuel, slew Goliath, fled Saul to the Cave of Adullam, ruled over Judah in Hebron for seven years, and conquered the Jebusite fortress of Zion to make Jerusalem his capital.',
        '1 Samuel 16-22; 2 Samuel 2-5',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Life Story Puzzle","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"life-story-puzzle","mechanic":"life-story-puzzle","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I played the harp to soothe a tormented monarch''s soul.","I was hunted across wilderness crags like a partridge on the mountains.","God established an everlasting covenant with my royal lineage."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l48-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        48,
        3,
        'Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Called while mending nets at Sea of Galilee -> Confessed Christ at Caesarea Philippi -> Denied the Lord three times by a courtyard fire -> Preached the Pentecost sermon in Jerusalem -> Miraculously delivered from Herod''s prison by an angel?',
        '"James","Andrew","Simon Peter","John"'::text[],
        'Simon Peter',
        'Simon Peter was called from his nets, made the great confession of Jesus as the Messiah, wept bitterly after three denials, preached at Pentecost, and was chained in prison until an angel struck off his chains.',
        'Matthew 4:18; Matthew 16:16; Matthew 26:69-75; Acts 2:14; Acts 12:6-11',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Life Story Puzzle","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"life-story-puzzle","mechanic":"life-story-puzzle","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I attempted to walk on the storm-tossed waters of Galilee.","Jesus declared to me: ''Upon this rock I will build my church.''","An angel escorted me past two guard posts right out of Herod''s iron prison gates."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l48-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        48,
        4,
        'Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens?',
        '"Paul (Saul of Tarsus)","Philip","Barnabas","Silas"'::text[],
        'Paul (Saul of Tarsus)',
        'Saul guarded the coats of those stoning Stephen, saw the blinding light near Damascus, was healed and baptized by Ananias, escaped Damascus in a wicker basket, and confronted Athenian philosophers at the Areopagus.',
        'Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Life Story Puzzle","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"life-story-puzzle","mechanic":"life-story-puzzle","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a Hebrew of Hebrews, a Pharisee born in Tarsus of Cilicia.","A voice from heaven arrested me: ''Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me?''","I bore in my body the brand-marks of Jesus across the Roman empire."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l48-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        48,
        5,
        'Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Placed in a reed basket on the Nile -> Raised in Pharaoh''s palace -> Fled to Midian after killing an Egyptian -> Encountered God at the burning bush -> Died atop Mount Nebo overlooking the Promised Land?',
        '"Moses","Joseph","Joshua","Aaron"'::text[],
        'Moses',
        'Moses was saved in an ark of bulrushes, grew up as royalty in Egypt, spent 40 years as an exile shepherd, spoke with God at the burning bush, and died at age 120 on Mount Nebo.',
        'Exodus 2-3; Deuteronomy 34:1-5',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Life Story Puzzle","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"life-story-puzzle","mechanic":"life-story-puzzle","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was hidden three months by my parents because they saw I was a beautiful child.","I chose to suffer affliction with the people of God rather than enjoy the pleasures of sin for a season.","The Lord buried me with His own hand in an unknown valley in Moab."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l49-c1',
        'bible-character-quest',
        49,
        1,
        'Which royal palace administrator in Samaria feared the Lord greatly, secretly hid one hundred prophets of the Lord by fifties in two caves, and fed them with bread and water during Jezebel''s purge?',
        '"Ahijah","Adoniram","Benaiah","Obadiah"'::text[],
        'Obadiah',
        'Obadiah, steward of Ahab''s palace, feared God from his youth; he hid 100 prophets from Jezebel and provided bread and water; Elijah met him while Obadiah was searching for grass for the royal mules.',
        '1 Kings 18:3-16',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Bible Character Investigator","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"character-investigator","mechanic":"character-investigator","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I worked at the very nerve center of Ahab and Jezebel''s royal regime.","I risked execution for high treason to run a secret underground logistics network for God''s prophets.","Elijah commanded me: ''Go, tell your master: Behold, Elijah is here!''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l49-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        49,
        2,
        'Which apostle was gathering a bundle of sticks on the cold, rainy island of Malta when a venomous viper fastened onto his hand, which he shook off into the fire suffering no ill effects?',
        '"Peter","Philip","John","Paul"'::text[],
        'Paul',
        'On Malta, a viper driven out by the heat fastened on Paul''s hand; islanders expected him to swell up or drop dead, but when no harm came, they changed their minds and said he was a god.',
        'Acts 28:1-6',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Bible Character Investigator","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"character-investigator","mechanic":"character-investigator","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was soaking wet and shivering beside a bonfire after our ship broke apart on the reefs.","Pagan onlookers observed the venomous reptile dangling from my hand and declared I was a murderer pursued by Justice.","I shook the beast into the flames and suffered neither swelling nor death, fulfilling Jesus'' promise."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l49-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        49,
        3,
        'Which desperate king disguised himself in common clothes, travelled by night to Endor with two men, and consulted a spiritist medium to conjure up the deceased prophet Samuel on the eve of his death?',
        '"Saul","Manasseh","Ahaziah","Ahab"'::text[],
        'Saul',
        'Saul disguised himself and visited the witch of Endor; when Samuel appeared, he foretold that the Lord had departed from Saul and that tomorrow Saul and his sons would be with him.',
        '1 Samuel 28:7-20',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Bible Character Investigator","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"character-investigator","mechanic":"character-investigator","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I had previously expelled all spiritists and mediums from the land of Israel.","With the Philistine army massing at Shunem and heaven refusing to answer me, I sought forbidden necromancy.","The ghostly appearance of the old mantle-wrapped prophet announced my impending death."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l49-c4',
        'bible-character-quest',
        49,
        4,
        'Which devout Roman soldier stationed in Caesarea was on his knees praying at three in the afternoon when an angel appeared in bright clothes saying ''Your prayers and your alms have ascended as a memorial before God''?',
        '"Publius","Cornelius","Sergius Paulus","Julius"'::text[],
        'Cornelius',
        'Cornelius, centurion of the Italian band, was a generous and praying Gentile whose vision orchestrated Peter''s journey to open the kingdom to non-Jewish nations.',
        'Acts 10:1-4',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Bible Character Investigator","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"character-investigator","mechanic":"character-investigator","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was an uncircumcised Gentile officer commanding Roman troops.","My consistent private prayer life and generous alms caught the attention of Almighty God.","An angel gave me specific navigational instructions to send messengers to Simon the tanner''s house in Joppa."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l49-c5',
        'bible-character-quest',
        49,
        5,
        'Which Benjamite judge delivered Israel by assassinating King Eglon of Moab in his cool summer rooftop chamber with an eighteen-inch two-edged dagger strapped to his right thigh?',
        '"Othniel son of Kenaz","Gideon","Ehud son of Gera","Shamgar son of Anath"'::text[],
        'Ehud son of Gera',
        'Ehud, a left-handed Benjamite, crafted a two-edged short sword, strapped it to his right thigh, delivered tribute to obese King Eglon, locked the doors after killing him, and escaped.',
        'Judges 3:15-26',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Bible Character Investigator","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"character-investigator","mechanic":"character-investigator","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true,"clues":["I was gifted with physical dexterity because I was left-handed.","I informed the Moabite monarch: ''I have a secret message from God for you.''","I slipped out through the roof porch and blew the ram''s horn in the hill country of Ephraim."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
