        'bible-character-quest',
        50,
        1,
        'According to Judges 18:30, what was the exact name of the Levite priest who established an unauthorized idolatrous priesthood for the tribe of Dan, revealed to be the grandson of Moses?',
        '"Phinehas son of Eleazar","Jonathan son of Gershom, son of Moses","Zechariah son of Jehoiada","Ahimelech son of Ahitub"'::text[],
        'Jonathan son of Gershom, son of Moses',
        'Judges 18:30 explicitly states that Jonathan son of Gershom, son of Moses (often obscured in scribal tradition as Manasseh to protect Moses'' honor), and his sons were priests to Dan until the captivity.',
        'Judges 18:30',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Ultimate Character Master","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"ultimate-master","mechanic":"ultimate-master","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":15,"curated":true,"clues":["I was a wandering young Levite from Bethlehem in Judah who sold my priestly services for ten shekels of silver and a suit of apparel.","The Danites stole Micah''s carved image and hired me away to be priest to an entire tribe.","My grandfather was the greatest lawgiver and prophet in Israel''s history."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l50-c2',
        'bible-character-quest',
        50,
        2,
        'Which young missionary abandoned Paul and Barnabas at Perga in Pamphylia, caused a bitter rupture between them at Antioch, yet was later commended by Paul in Rome as ''useful to me for ministry''?',
        '"Timothy","Titus","Demas","John Mark"'::text[],
        'John Mark',
        'John Mark left the first missionary journey at Perga, prompting Paul to refuse him on the second; years later in Roman prison Paul wrote: ''Get Mark and bring him with you, for he is very useful to me for ministry.''',
        'Acts 13:13; Acts 15:37-39; 2 Timothy 4:11',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Ultimate Character Master","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"ultimate-master","mechanic":"ultimate-master","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":15,"curated":true,"clues":["I sailed with Paul and my cousin Barnabas across Cyprus during their earliest campaign.","I deserted the missionary frontline when the team faced the rugged mountains of Pamphylia.","In my mature years, I authored the earliest canonical Gospel and won Paul''s highest praise."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-character-quest-l50-c3',
        'bible-character-quest',
        50,
        3,
        'Which wicked queen mother, the daughter of King Ahab and Jezebel of Israel, usurped the throne of Judah for six years and systematically attempted to exterminate the entire royal lineage of David?',
        '"Shelomith","Maakah","Athaliah","Jezebel"'::text[],
        'Athaliah',
        'When Athaliah saw her son King Ahaziah was dead, she arose and destroyed all the royal seed of the house of David, reigning six years until Jehoiada''s temple revolt.',
        '2 Kings 11:1-3; 2 Chronicles 22:10-12',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Ultimate Character Master","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"ultimate-master","mechanic":"ultimate-master","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":15,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the daughter of Israel''s most notorious idolatrous royal couple.","My marriage to King Jehoram of Judah poisoned the Davidic dynasty with Baal worship.","When young Joash was crowned, I ripped my robes screaming ''Treason! Treason!'' before being executed at the horse gate."]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
