        'bible-character-quest',
        50,
        4,
        'Which courageous court prophet confronted King David after his adulterous murder of Uriah the Hittite, telling the piercing parable of a rich man who stole a poor man''s single pet ewe lamb?',
        '"Nathan","Gad the Seer","Shemaiah","Ahijah"'::text[],
        'Nathan',
        'Nathan confronted David with the story of the stolen ewe lamb; when David''s anger burned against the rich man, Nathan boldly pointed: ''You are the man!''',
        '2 Samuel 12:1-15',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Ultimate Character Master","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"ultimate-master","mechanic":"ultimate-master","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":15,"curated":true,"clues":["I served as court prophet and royal counselor during David''s golden era.","I narrated an evocative legal grievance about an impoverished man''s cherished household pet.","I looked Israel''s most powerful warrior monarch in the eye and uttered four words: ''You are the man!''"]}'::jsonb
      ),
(
