        'bible-character-quest',
        50,
        5,
        'Which beloved apostle was banished in elderly exile to the penal island of Patmos on the Lord''s Day, heard a voice like a trumpet, and collapsed as though dead before the blazing glorified Son of Man?',
        '"John the Apostle","Paul","Simon Peter","James the brother of Jesus"'::text[],
        'John the Apostle',
        'John was on the island called Patmos for the word of God and testimony of Jesus; he turned and saw the glorified Christ and fell at His feet like a dead man, but Jesus laid His right hand on him saying: ''Fear not, I am the first and the last.''',
        'Revelation 1:9-17',
        '{"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Character Quest","level_theme":"Ultimate Character Master","category":"The Ultimate Character Quest","challengeType":"ultimate-master","mechanic":"ultimate-master","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":15,"curated":true,"clues":["I was the youngest of the original Twelve and leaned on Jesus'' chest at the Last Supper.","Roman authorities banished me to a rocky penal quarry in the Aegean Sea.","I was in the Spirit on the Lord''s Day when I beheld the Alpha and Omega holding the seven stars and the keys of Death and Hades."]}'::jsonb
