        'Complete the foundational Bible crossword with key people, places, and events.',
        '"HERODANTIPAS","ADONIRAMHADORAM","LYSANIAS","UZZIAHAZARIAH","TIBNISONOFGINATH","ARCHELAUS","ZIMRI","MAAKAH","CANDACE","ADONIJAH"'::text[],
        'HERODANTIPAS|ADONIRAMHADORAM|LYSANIAS|UZZIAHAZARIAH|TIBNISONOFGINATH|ARCHELAUS|ZIMRI|MAAKAH|CANDACE|ADONIJAH',
        '1. HERODANTIPAS: Which ruler foolishly bound himself with an oath before banquet guests to grant a dancing girl anything, resulting in the beheading of John the Baptist? (Matthew 14:6-10) 2. ADONIRAMHADORAM: Which royal supervisor of forced labor was dispatched by King Rehoboam to negotiate with the rebellious northern tribes, only to be stoned to death by all Israel? (1 Kings 12:18) 3. LYSANIAS: Which regional ruler was tetrarch of Abilene during the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, as recorded in Luke''s historical synchronization? (Luke 3:1) 4. UZZIAHAZARIAH: Which king of Judah ruled for 52 years and prospered greatly, but was struck with leprosy in the temple after arrogantly trying to burn incense? (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 5. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 6. ARCHELAUS: Which son of Herod the Great ruled over Judea after Herod''s death, whose cruel reputation caused Joseph to avoid Judea and take Jesus to Galilee? (Matthew 2:22) 7. ZIMRI: Which military commander seized the throne of the northern kingdom of Israel and reigned for only seven days in Tirzah before setting fire to the palace over himself? (1 Kings 16:15-18) 8. MAAKAH: Which queen mother (Gebirah) of Judah was stripped of her royal dignity by King Asa because she had erected an abominable image for Asherah? (1 Kings 15:13) 9. CANDACE: Which royal title and name belonged to the queen of the Ethiopians whose chief court treasurer was baptized by Philip on the desert road? (Acts 8:27) 10. ADONIJAH: Which ambitious son of David by Haggith declared himself king at En-rogel when David was old, backed by General Joab and Priest Abiathar? (1 Kings 1:5-9)',
