        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 3. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 4. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 5. MATTHIAS: The man chosen to replace Judas among the Twelve (Acts 1:23-26) 6. UZZIAH: The king struck with leprosy after unlawfully burning incense (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 7. MEPHIBOSHETH: Jonathan’s son whom David showed kindness (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 8. MICAIAH: The prophet who warned Ahab despite the other prophets’ assurances (1 Kings 22:13-28) 9. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 10. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5)',
        'Jeremiah 36:20-26; Judges 3:15-22; Jeremiah 38:7-13; 2 Kings 22:14-20; Acts 1:23-26; 2 Chronicles 26:16-21; 2 Samuel 9:1-13; 1 Kings 22:13-28; Judges 4:17-22; Exodus 31:1-5',
