        '1. UZZIAHAZARIAH: Which king of Judah ruled for 52 years and prospered greatly, but was struck with leprosy in the temple after arrogantly trying to burn incense? (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 2. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 3. HADADTHEEDOMITE: Which Edomite of royal descent fled to Egypt as a child when Joab wiped out Edom''s males, married Queen Tahpenes'' sister, and returned to oppose King Solomon? (1 Kings 11:14-22) 4. ITTAITHEGITTITE: Which loyal warrior from Gath brought six hundred soldiers to David’s side during Absalom’s rebellion, declaring he would stay with David in life or death? (2 Samuel 15:19-22; 18:2) 5. GIDEONJERUBBAAL: Which son of Joash the Abiezrite tore down his father’s altar of Baal, reduced his army from 32,000 to 300 men, and attacked with torches in clay pitchers? (Judges 6:25-32; 7:1-22) 6. BALAKSONOFZIPPOR: Which Moabite king hired the Mesopotamian seer Balaam to put a curse upon the children of Israel camping on the plains of Moab? (Numbers 22:2-6) 7. ZERUIAH: Which prominent sister of Joab and Abishai was mother to Asahel, her sons frequently known as ''the sons of Zeruiah''? (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 8. ONESIPHORUS: Which Christian brother in Ephesus repeatedly refreshed the imprisoned apostle Paul in Rome, not being ashamed of his chains? (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 9. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 10. SIMONSONOFJONAH: Which New Testament believer was named ''Peter'' (Cephas / Rock) by Jesus after confessing Him as ''the Christ, the Son of the living God''? (Matthew 16:16-18; John 1:42)',
