        '1. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 2. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 3. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 4. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 5. SIMONSONOFJONAH: Which New Testament believer was named ''Peter'' (Cephas / Rock) by Jesus after confessing Him as ''the Christ, the Son of the living God''? (Matthew 16:16-18; John 1:42) 6. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 7. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 8. UZZIAHAZARIAH: Which king of Judah ruled for 52 years and prospered greatly, but was struck with leprosy in the temple after arrogantly trying to burn incense? (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 9. HERODANTIPAS: Which ruler foolishly bound himself with an oath before banquet guests to grant a dancing girl anything, resulting in the beheading of John the Baptist? (Matthew 14:6-10) 10. ADONIRAMHADORAM: Which royal supervisor of forced labor was dispatched by King Rehoboam to negotiate with the rebellious northern tribes, only to be stoned to death by all Israel? (1 Kings 12:18)',
