        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 3. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 4. MATTHIAS: The man chosen to replace Judas among the Twelve (Acts 1:23-26) 5. UZZIAH: The king struck with leprosy after unlawfully burning incense (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 6. MEPHIBOSHETH: Jonathan’s son whom David showed kindness (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 7. MICAIAH: The prophet who warned Ahab despite the other prophets’ assurances (1 Kings 22:13-28) 8. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 9. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5) 10. SHAMGAR: The judge who struck down six hundred Philistines with an oxgoad (Judges 3:31)',
