        'EHUD|ZACCHAEUS|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|SIMONTHEZEALOT|MIRIAM|ELEAZAR|ABIGAIL|ABISHAI|EUTYCHUS',
        '1. EHUD: • I was a judge in Israel.
• I was left-handed.
• I killed Eglon, king of Moab, with an eighteen-inch double-edged dagger.
Who am I? (Judges 3:15-22) 2. ZACCHAEUS: • I was a tax collector in Jericho.
• I was short in stature.
• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.
Who am I? (Luke 19:1-10) 3. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
Who am I? (Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31) 4. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 5. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 6. MIRIAM: Which prominent sister of Moses and Aaron watched over baby Moses in the Nile and later led Israel''s women in song at the Red Sea? (Exodus 2:4; 15:20-21; Numbers 26:59) 7. ELEAZAR: Which priest was the father of Phinehas, who succeeded Aaron as high priest atop Mount Hor? (Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28) 8. ABIGAIL: Which wife of David was the former wife of the harsh rancher Nabal, who acted with wisdom to prevent David from shedding blood? (1 Samuel 25:3, 39-42) 9. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21) 10. EUTYCHUS: Which young man at Troas sat in a third-story window while Paul preached past midnight, fell into a deep sleep, and plunged to the ground? (Acts 20:9-12)',
