        '1. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 2. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 3. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 4. ZERUBBABEL: Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel led the first return of exiles from Babylon; Zechariah prophesied: ''Not by might nor by power, but by my Spirit''. (Ezra 3:2-8; Zechariah 4:6-9) 5. ZECHARIAH: Zechariah prophesied the coming King entering Jerusalem humble and mounted on a donkey; contains 14 chapters. (Zechariah 1:1-8; Zechariah 9:9) 6. THELORDISPEACE: Gideon built an altar to the Lord at Ophrah and called it Yahweh-Shalom, which means ''The Lord is Peace''. (Judges 6:24) 7. ZAPHENATH: Pharaoh gave Joseph the name Zaphenath-paneah and gave him Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera priest of On, as his wife. (Genesis 41:45) 8. TIGLATHPILESER: Tiglath-Pileser III captured Ijon, Abel-beth-maacah, Gilead, and Galilee, carrying the northern tribes captive into Assyria. (2 Kings 15:29; 1 Chronicles 5:26) 9. ZELOPHEHAD: Zelophehad died in the wilderness having no sons; his five daughters (Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah) secured landmark land inheritance laws. (Numbers 27:1-7; Joshua 17:3) 10. PETERJAMESJOHN: Jesus took Peter, James, and John up the high mountain to behold His glory, and brought them closest to Him in Gethsemane. (Mark 9:2; Mark 14:33)',
