        'AMOS|DOEG|BEREA|ALTAR|ANGEL|AMRAM|BOAZ|DOVE|AARON|EHUD',
        '1. AMOS: Amos was a shepherd and grower of sycamore figs who prophesied divine justice against social oppression in northern Israel. (Amos 1:1; Amos 5:24) 2. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 3. BEREA: The place whose people examined the Scriptures daily (Acts 17:10-12) 4. ALTAR: Noah built an altar after the flood; Moses built the bronze altar of burnt offering for the Tabernacle court. (Genesis 8:20; Exodus 27:1) 5. ANGEL: Angels are ministering spirits sent out to serve for the sake of those who are to inherit salvation. (Luke 1:26; Hebrews 1:14) 6. AMRAM: Amram son of Kohath lived 137 years and fathered the priestly and prophetic leaders of the Exodus. (Exodus 6:18-20; 1 Chronicles 6:2-3) 7. BOAZ: Boaz son of Salmon married Ruth the Moabitess; their son Obed became father to Jesse and grandfather to David. (Ruth 2:1; Ruth 4:13-17) 8. DOVE: When Jesus was baptized, the heavens opened and the Spirit of God descended like a dove and rested upon Him. (Genesis 8:8-12; Matthew 3:16) 9. AARON: Aaron was Moses'' brother and spokesman; consecrated with holy oil, he wore the breastplate and gold plate on his turban. (Exodus 4:14; Exodus 28:1) 10. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22)',
