        1,
        'Trace the covenant families from Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob to the twelve tribes.',
        '"SHILOH","MIZPAH","JEZREEL","ZIKLAG","EBENEZER","SHIBBOLETH","MANAEN","LUCIUS","SOSIPATER","JASON"'::text[],
        'SHILOH|MIZPAH|JEZREEL|ZIKLAG|EBENEZER|SHIBBOLETH|MANAEN|LUCIUS|SOSIPATER|JASON',
        '1. SHILOH: Early central sanctuary in Ephraim where the Tabernacle stood and young Samuel ministered (Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 3:21) 2. MIZPAH: Watchtower town where Israel assembled before Samuel and where Governor Gedaliah governed (1 Samuel 7:5-6; 2 Kings 25:23) 3. JEZREEL: Fertile valley and royal winter city where Naboth kept a vineyard coveted by Ahab (1 Kings 21:1; Hosea 1:4) 4. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 5. EBENEZER: Memorial stone set up by Samuel between Mizpah and Shen saying "Thus far the LORD has helped us" (1 Samuel 7:12) 6. SHIBBOLETH: Password word used by Jephthah''s men at Jordan crossings to detect Ephraimites who pronounced it Sibboleth (Judges 12:6) 7. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 8. LUCIUS: Kinsman of Paul or prophet/teacher from Cyrene mentioned in Antioch and Romans (Acts 13:1; Romans 16:21) 9. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 10. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21)',
        'Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 3:21; 1 Samuel 7:5-6; 2 Kings 25:23; 1 Kings 21:1; Hosea 1:4; 1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1; 1 Samuel 7:12; Judges 12:6; Acts 13:1; Acts 13:1; Romans 16:21; Romans 16:21; Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21',
