        'Identify the monarchs, queens, and royal court figures of Scripture.',
        '"EHUD","DEBORAH","BARNABAS","ELEAZAR","ABISHAI","BARZILLAI","ERASTUS","BEZALEL","HULDAH","ZACCHAEUS"'::text[],
        'EHUD|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|ELEAZAR|ABISHAI|BARZILLAI|ERASTUS|BEZALEL|HULDAH|ZACCHAEUS',
        '1. EHUD: • I was a judge in Israel.
• I was left-handed.
• I killed Eglon, king of Moab, with an eighteen-inch double-edged dagger.
Who am I? (Judges 3:15-22) 2. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
Who am I? (Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31) 3. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 4. ELEAZAR: Which priest was the father of Phinehas, who succeeded Aaron as high priest atop Mount Hor? (Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28) 5. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21) 6. BARZILLAI: Which wealthy eighty-year-old Gileadite supplied David with wheat, barley, cheese, and beds while David was fleeing Absalom at Mahanaim? (2 Samuel 17:27-29; 19:31-37) 7. ERASTUS: Which Roman official and city treasurer of Corinth sent greetings to the Roman Christians at the conclusion of Paul''s epistle to the Romans? (Romans 16:23) 8. BEZALEL: Which master craftsman of the tribe of Judah was the son of Uri, son of Hur, appointed by God to build the ark of the covenant and tabernacle furnishings? (Exodus 31:1-5; 35:30) 9. HULDAH: Which prophetess and wife of Shallum keeper of the wardrobe was consulted by King Josiah’s royal delegation when the Book of the Law was found in the temple? (2 Kings 22:14-20; 2 Chronicles 34:22) 10. ZACCHAEUS: • I was a tax collector in Jericho.
• I was short in stature.
• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.
