        '1. PAULSAULOFTARSUS: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens? (Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22) 2. SHIPHRAHANDPUAH: Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own? (Exodus 1:15-21) 3. THEOLDERBROTHER: In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, who became furiously angry, refused to enter the celebration banquet, and complained that a young goat was never given to him? (Luke 15:28-30) 4. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Which of the twelve apostles is called ''the Cananite'' in Matthew and Mark, and ''the Zealot'' in Luke, to distinguish him from Simon Peter? (Matthew 10:4; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13) 5. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 6. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 7. SIMONSONOFJONAH: Which New Testament believer was named ''Peter'' (Cephas / Rock) by Jesus after confessing Him as ''the Christ, the Son of the living God''? (Matthew 16:16-18; John 1:42) 8. EHUD: • I was a judge in Israel.
