        '1. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 2. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 3. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 4. ELON: Judge from the tribe of Zebulun who led Israel for ten years (Judges 12:11-12) 5. NEREUS: Believer greeted with his sister and Olympas in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 6. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 7. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 8. ASYNCRITUS: Believer in Rome greeted by name in Paul''s extensive list of greetings (Romans 16:14) 9. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 10. EUBULUS: Brother in Rome who sent personal greetings to Timothy during Paul''s second Roman imprisonment (2 Timothy 4:21)',
