        '1. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 2. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 3. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 4. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 5. NEBUZARADAN: Captain of the Babylonian royal bodyguard who burned the Temple and broke down Jerusalem''s walls (2 Kings 25:8-11) 6. RABSHAKEH: Assyrian military envoy who shouted blasphemous intimidation in Hebrew on Jerusalem''s wall (2 Kings 18:17-35) 7. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 8. MELCHIZEDEK: King of Salem and priest of God Most High who blessed Abram (Genesis 14:18-20) 9. AMRAMANDJOCHEBED: Who were the father and mother of Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, both belonging to the tribe of Levi? (Exodus 6:20; Numbers 26:59) 10. TYCHICUS: Which trusted emissary and ''beloved brother'' from Asia was dispatched by Paul to deliver the circular letters to Ephesus and Colossae, carrying personal news of Paul''s affairs? (Ephesians 6:21-22; Colossians 4:7-8; 2 Timothy 4:12)',
