        'Stage 2 Boss: Overcome deep character riddles linking both Testaments.',
        '"ZACCHAEUS","DEBORAH","BARNABAS","SIMONTHEZEALOT","MIRIAM","ELEAZAR","EUTYCHUS","RHODA","BARZILLAI","TAMAR"'::text[],
        'ZACCHAEUS|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|SIMONTHEZEALOT|MIRIAM|ELEAZAR|EUTYCHUS|RHODA|BARZILLAI|TAMAR',
        '1. ZACCHAEUS: • I was a tax collector in Jericho.
• I was short in stature.
• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.
Who am I? (Luke 19:1-10) 2. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
Who am I? (Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31) 3. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 4. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 5. MIRIAM: Which prominent sister of Moses and Aaron watched over baby Moses in the Nile and later led Israel''s women in song at the Red Sea? (Exodus 2:4; 15:20-21; Numbers 26:59) 6. ELEAZAR: Which priest was the father of Phinehas, who succeeded Aaron as high priest atop Mount Hor? (Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28) 7. EUTYCHUS: Which young man at Troas sat in a third-story window while Paul preached past midnight, fell into a deep sleep, and plunged to the ground? (Acts 20:9-12) 8. RHODA: Which servant girl was so overjoyed when she recognized Peter’s voice at Mary''s house that she ran inside without opening the gate? (Acts 12:13-16) 9. BARZILLAI: Which wealthy eighty-year-old Gileadite supplied David with wheat, barley, cheese, and beds while David was fleeing Absalom at Mahanaim? (2 Samuel 17:27-29; 19:31-37) 10. TAMAR: Which daughter-in-law of Judah disguised herself at the entrance to Enaim, bearing the twin sons Perez and Zerah? (Genesis 38:13-30)',
        'Luke 19:1-10; Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31; Acts 4:36-37; Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4; Exodus 2:4; 15:20-21; Numbers 26:59; Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28; Acts 20:9-12; Acts 12:13-16; 2 Samuel 17:27-29; 19:31-37; Genesis 38:13-30',
        '{"entries":[{"number":1,"answer":"ZACCHAEUS","clue":"• I was a tax collector in Jericho.\n• I was short in stature.\n• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.\nWho am I?","reference":"Luke 19:1-10","direction":"across"},{"number":2,"answer":"DEBORAH","clue":"• I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.\n• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.\n• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.\nWho am I?","reference":"Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31","direction":"down"},{"number":3,"answer":"BARNABAS","clue":"• I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.\n• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.\n• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.\nWho am I?","reference":"Acts 4:36-37","direction":"across"},{"number":4,"answer":"SIMONTHEZEALOT","clue":"Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''?","reference":"Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4","direction":"down"},{"number":5,"answer":"MIRIAM","clue":"Which prominent sister of Moses and Aaron watched over baby Moses in the Nile and later led Israel''s women in song at the Red Sea?","reference":"Exodus 2:4; 15:20-21; Numbers 26:59","direction":"across"},{"number":6,"answer":"ELEAZAR","clue":"Which priest was the father of Phinehas, who succeeded Aaron as high priest atop Mount Hor?","reference":"Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28","direction":"down"},{"number":7,"answer":"EUTYCHUS","clue":"Which young man at Troas sat in a third-story window while Paul preached past midnight, fell into a deep sleep, and plunged to the ground?","reference":"Acts 20:9-12","direction":"across"},{"number":8,"answer":"RHODA","clue":"Which servant girl was so overjoyed when she recognized Peter’s voice at Mary''s house that she ran inside without opening the gate?","reference":"Acts 12:13-16","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"BARZILLAI","clue":"Which wealthy eighty-year-old Gileadite supplied David with wheat, barley, cheese, and beds while David was fleeing Absalom at Mahanaim?","reference":"2 Samuel 17:27-29; 19:31-37","direction":"across"},{"number":10,"answer":"TAMAR","clue":"Which daughter-in-law of Judah disguised herself at the entrance to Enaim, bearing the twin sons Perez and Zerah?","reference":"Genesis 38:13-30","direction":"down"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"Biblical People","stage":2,"stage_title":"Biblical People","level_theme":"Character Crossword Boss","difficulty":"Hard","timerSeconds":200,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
