        'PAULSAULOFTARSUS|JANNESANDJAMBRES|KORAHSONOFIZHAR|SHIPHRAHANDPUAH|ITTAITHEGITTITE|MARYMAGDALENE|PONTIUSPILATE|THESADDUCEES|THEOLDERBROTHER|SIMONOFCYRENE',
        '1. PAULSAULOFTARSUS: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens? (Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22) 2. JANNESANDJAMBRES: In 2 Timothy 3:8, which two traditional names does Paul reveal for the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses before Pharaoh, comparing them to corrupt end-times teachers? (2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11) 3. KORAHSONOFIZHAR: Which Levite rebel led 250 prominent community leaders against Moses and Aaron in Numbers 16, whose fatal rebellion is linked in Jude 11 with the error of Balaam? (Numbers 16:1-35; Jude 1:11) 4. SHIPHRAHANDPUAH: Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own? (Exodus 1:15-21) 5. ITTAITHEGITTITE: Which Philistine military exile from Gath arrived with 600 men and swore unwavering loyalty to King David during Absalom''s rebellion, saying ''In whatever place my lord the king shall be... there will your servant be''? (2 Samuel 15:19-22; 2 Samuel 18:2) 6. MARYMAGDALENE: Which woman came to the tomb while it was still dark, found the stone taken away, mistook the risen Lord for the gardener, and heard Him call her ''Mary''? (John 20:1-16) 7. PONTIUSPILATE: Which Roman procurator interrogated Jesus during His civil trial, asking ''Are you the King of the Jews?'' and the cynical question ''What is truth?'' (John 18:33-38) 8. THESADDUCEES: Which religious group in Jerusalem, who denied the resurrection of the dead, challenged Jesus with the hypothetical problem of a woman married to seven brothers? (Matthew 22:23-28; Luke 20:27-33) 9. THEOLDERBROTHER: In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, who became furiously angry, refused to enter the celebration banquet, and complained that a young goat was never given to him? (Luke 15:28-30) 10. SIMONOFCYRENE: Distinguish these biblical Simons: Which Simon from North Africa was compelled by Roman soldiers to carry Jesus'' heavy wooden cross-beam, whose sons were Alexander and Rufus? (Matthew 27:32; Mark 15:21)',
