        '"ANNA","ANNAS","ABIGAIL","ABISHAI","COZBI","CHUZA","AGABUS","DAVID","ENOCH","CARPUS"'::text[],
        'ANNA|ANNAS|ABIGAIL|ABISHAI|COZBI|CHUZA|AGABUS|DAVID|ENOCH|CARPUS',
        '1. ANNA: • I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.
• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.
• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.
Who am I? (Luke 2:36-38) 2. ANNAS: Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane? (John 18:13) 3. ABIGAIL: Which wife of David was the former wife of the harsh rancher Nabal, who acted with wisdom to prevent David from shedding blood? (1 Samuel 25:3, 39-42) 4. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21) 5. COZBI: Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor? (Numbers 25:15-18) 6. CHUZA: Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth? (Luke 8:3) 7. AGABUS: • I was a prophet who came down from Judea to Antioch and Caesarea.
• I predicted by the Holy Spirit a severe famine across the entire Roman empire under Emperor Claudius.
• I tied my own hands and feet with Paul''s belt to foretell his Jerusalem arrest.
Who am I? (Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11) 8. DAVID: When the angel Gabriel announced the virgin birth of Jesus to Mary in Nazareth, he stated that God would give Him the royal throne of which Old Testament king? (Luke 1:32) 9. ENOCH: In Jude 1:14-15, which pre-flood patriarch, ''the seventh from Adam'', is cited as prophesying: ''Behold, the Lord comes with ten thousands of His holy ones''? (Jude 1:14-15; Genesis 5:21-24) 10. CARPUS: In 2 Timothy 4:13, in whose home at Troas did Paul leave his winter traveling cloak, books, and especially the parchments, asking Timothy to bring them before winter? (2 Timothy 4:13)',
        'Luke 2:36-38; John 18:13; 1 Samuel 25:3, 39-42; 2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21; Numbers 25:15-18; Luke 8:3; Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11; Luke 1:32; Jude 1:14-15; Genesis 5:21-24; 2 Timothy 4:13',
        '{"entries":[{"number":1,"answer":"ANNA","clue":"• I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.\n• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.\n• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.\nWho am I?","reference":"Luke 2:36-38","direction":"across"},{"number":2,"answer":"ANNAS","clue":"Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane?","reference":"John 18:13","direction":"down"},{"number":3,"answer":"ABIGAIL","clue":"Which wife of David was the former wife of the harsh rancher Nabal, who acted with wisdom to prevent David from shedding blood?","reference":"1 Samuel 25:3, 39-42","direction":"across"},{"number":4,"answer":"ABISHAI","clue":"Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear?","reference":"2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21","direction":"down"},{"number":5,"answer":"COZBI","clue":"Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor?","reference":"Numbers 25:15-18","direction":"across"},{"number":6,"answer":"CHUZA","clue":"Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth?","reference":"Luke 8:3","direction":"across"},{"number":7,"answer":"AGABUS","clue":"• I was a prophet who came down from Judea to Antioch and Caesarea.\n• I predicted by the Holy Spirit a severe famine across the entire Roman empire under Emperor Claudius.\n• I tied my own hands and feet with Paul''s belt to foretell his Jerusalem arrest.\nWho am I?","reference":"Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11","direction":"down"},{"number":8,"answer":"DAVID","clue":"When the angel Gabriel announced the virgin birth of Jesus to Mary in Nazareth, he stated that God would give Him the royal throne of which Old Testament king?","reference":"Luke 1:32","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"ENOCH","clue":"In Jude 1:14-15, which pre-flood patriarch, ''the seventh from Adam'', is cited as prophesying: ''Behold, the Lord comes with ten thousands of His holy ones''?","reference":"Jude 1:14-15; Genesis 5:21-24","direction":"down"},{"number":10,"answer":"CARPUS","clue":"In 2 Timothy 4:13, in whose home at Troas did Paul leave his winter traveling cloak, books, and especially the parchments, asking Timothy to bring them before winter?","reference":"2 Timothy 4:13","direction":"across"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"Biblical People","stage":2,"stage_title":"Biblical People","level_theme":"Character Crossword Boss","difficulty":"Hard","timerSeconds":200,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
