        '"ZIKLAG","PHILADELPHIA","ZEPHANIAH","ZACCHAEUS","TABERNACLE","ZACHARIAS","SIMONTHEZEALOT","SIMONSONOFJONAH","ZAPHENATHPANEAH","ZERUIAH"'::text[],
        'ZIKLAG|PHILADELPHIA|ZEPHANIAH|ZACCHAEUS|TABERNACLE|ZACHARIAS|SIMONTHEZEALOT|SIMONSONOFJONAH|ZAPHENATHPANEAH|ZERUIAH',
        '1. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 2. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 3. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 4. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 5. TABERNACLE: The portable sanctuary Israel built in the wilderness (Exodus 25:8-9) 6. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 7. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 8. SIMONSONOFJONAH: Which New Testament believer was named ''Peter'' (Cephas / Rock) by Jesus after confessing Him as ''the Christ, the Son of the living God''? (Matthew 16:16-18; John 1:42) 9. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 10. ZERUIAH: Which prominent sister of Joab and Abishai was mother to Asahel, her sons frequently known as ''the sons of Zeruiah''? (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18)',
