        'BEREA|DOEG|EHUD|AGABUS|COZBI|DERBE|AIJALON|ABIGAIL|EPHOD|ABISHAI',
        '1. BEREA: Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings (Acts 17:10-12) 2. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 3. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 4. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 5. COZBI: Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor? (Numbers 25:15-18) 6. DERBE: Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra (Acts 14:20-21) 7. AIJALON: Valley over which Joshua commanded the moon to stand motionless during the fight for Gibeon (Joshua 10:12-13) 8. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 9. EPHOD: A priestly garment associated with the high priest (Exodus 28:6-12) 10. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21)',
        'Acts 17:10-12; 1 Samuel 22:9-19; Judges 3:15-22; Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11; Numbers 25:15-18; Acts 14:20-21; Joshua 10:12-13; 1 Samuel 25:23-42; Exodus 28:6-12; 2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21',
