        '1. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 2. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 3. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 4. MEPHIBOSHETH: Jonathan’s son whom David showed kindness (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 5. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 6. TROPHIMUS: The Ephesian whom Paul left sick at Miletus (2 Timothy 4:20) 7. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 8. TABERNACLE: The portable sanctuary Israel built in the wilderness (Exodus 25:8-9) 9. PENTATEUCH: The collective name for the first five books of the Bible (Luke 24:44) 10. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13)',
