        '1. ABDONSONOFHILLEL: Which ruler from Pirathon in Ephraim had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys? (Judges 12:13-15) 2. BALAKSONOFZIPPOR: Which Moabite king hired the Mesopotamian seer Balaam to put a curse upon the children of Israel camping on the plains of Moab? (Numbers 22:2-6) 3. ZERUIAH: Which prominent sister of Joab and Abishai was mother to Asahel, her sons frequently known as ''the sons of Zeruiah''? (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 4. ONESIPHORUS: Which Christian brother in Ephesus repeatedly refreshed the imprisoned apostle Paul in Rome, not being ashamed of his chains? (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 5. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 6. SIMONSONOFJONAH: Which New Testament believer was named ''Peter'' (Cephas / Rock) by Jesus after confessing Him as ''the Christ, the Son of the living God''? (Matthew 16:16-18; John 1:42) 7. EPHRONSONOFZOHAR: Which Hittite elder of Hebron sold the field and cave of Machpelah to Abraham for four hundred shekels of silver? (Genesis 23:8-16) 8. HOBABSONOFREUEL: Which brother-in-law of Moses did Moses urge to travel with Israel through the wilderness to serve as ''eyes for us''? (Numbers 10:29-32) 9. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 10. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13)',
