        'SAMSON|RAHAB|ABDONSONOFHILLEL|JEPHTHAH|PURAH|BALAKSONOFZIPPOR|ELDADANDMEDAD|KORAH|EPAPHRODITUS|ADONIZEDEK',
        '1. SAMSON: Which Danite judge was born to Manoah and his barren wife, tore a young lion with his bare hands, and pushed down the pillars of the Philistine temple of Dagon? (Judges 13:2-5; 14:5-6; 16:28-30) 2. RAHAB: Which Canaanite innkeeper of Jericho hid Joshua''s two spies on her roof beneath stalks of flax and hung a scarlet cord from her window? (Joshua 2:1-21; Hebrews 11:31) 3. ABDONSONOFHILLEL: Which ruler from Pirathon in Ephraim had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys? (Judges 12:13-15) 4. JEPHTHAH: Which judge of Gilead made a solemn vow before the battle with the Ammonites that resulted in his daughter coming out first to meet him? (Judges 11:30-40) 5. PURAH: Which servant of Gideon accompanied him down into the Midianite camp to overhear the dream of the tumbling loaf of barley bread? (Judges 7:9-11) 6. BALAKSONOFZIPPOR: Which Moabite king hired the Mesopotamian seer Balaam to put a curse upon the children of Israel camping on the plains of Moab? (Numbers 22:2-6) 7. ELDADANDMEDAD: Which two elders remained in the camp and prophesied when the Holy Spirit rested upon them, despite not going out to the tabernacle? (Numbers 11:26-29) 8. KORAH: Which Levite led a famous wilderness rebellion with 250 well-known community leaders, claiming that all the congregation was holy? (Numbers 16:1-3, 31-35) 9. EPAPHRODITUS: Which faithful co-worker was sent by Paul to Philippi, described as his ''brother, fellow worker, and fellow soldier'', who risked his life for Christ''s work? (Philippians 2:25-30) 10. ADONIZEDEK: Which Amorite king of Jerusalem formed a five-king southern alliance to attack Gibeon after Gibeon made peace with Joshua? (Joshua 10:1-5)',
