        '1. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 2. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 3. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 4. BEREA: The place whose people examined the Scriptures daily (Acts 17:10-12) 5. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 6. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5) 7. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 8. EPHOD: A priestly garment associated with the high priest (Exodus 28:6-12) 9. BENAIAH: Mighty warrior who struck down a lion in a pit on a snowy day and led David''s bodyguard (2 Samuel 23:20-23) 10. HUR: Companion of Moses and Aaron who helped hold up Moses'' arms during the battle with Amalek (Exodus 17:10-12)',
        'Judges 3:15-22; 1 Samuel 22:9-19; Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11; Acts 17:10-12; Judges 4:17-22; Exodus 31:1-5; 1 Samuel 25:23-42; Exodus 28:6-12; 2 Samuel 23:20-23; Exodus 17:10-12',
