        'SHILOH|AIJALON|GIBEON|MIZPAH|JEZREEL|ZIKLAG|ENGEDI|EBENEZER|SHIBBOLETH|GESHEM',
        '1. SHILOH: Early central sanctuary in Ephraim where the Tabernacle stood and young Samuel ministered (Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 3:21) 2. AIJALON: Valley over which Joshua commanded the moon to stand motionless during the fight for Gibeon (Joshua 10:12-13) 3. GIBEON: City whose inhabitants tricked Joshua with moldy bread, where the sun stood still in battle (Joshua 9:3-15; 10:12) 4. MIZPAH: Watchtower town where Israel assembled before Samuel and where Governor Gedaliah governed (1 Samuel 7:5-6; 2 Kings 25:23) 5. JEZREEL: Fertile valley and royal winter city where Naboth kept a vineyard coveted by Ahab (1 Kings 21:1; Hosea 1:4) 6. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 7. ENGEDI: Oasis and crag of wild goats by the Dead Sea where David cut off the corner of Saul''s robe in a cave (1 Samuel 24:1-4) 8. EBENEZER: Memorial stone set up by Samuel between Mizpah and Shen saying "Thus far the LORD has helped us" (1 Samuel 7:12) 9. SHIBBOLETH: Password word used by Jephthah''s men at Jordan crossings to detect Ephraimites who pronounced it Sibboleth (Judges 12:6) 10. GESHEM: Arab leader who joined Sanballat and Tobiah in falsely accusing Nehemiah of planning rebellion (Nehemiah 2:19; 6:1-6)',
        'Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 3:21; Joshua 10:12-13; Joshua 9:3-15; 10:12; 1 Samuel 7:5-6; 2 Kings 25:23; 1 Kings 21:1; Hosea 1:4; 1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1; 1 Samuel 24:1-4; 1 Samuel 7:12; Judges 12:6; Nehemiah 2:19; 6:1-6',
