        'JEHOIAKIM|EHUD|EBEDMELECH|HULDAH|MATTHIAS|ABIGAIL|UZZIAH|BARNABAS|MEPHIBOSHETH|MICAIAH',
        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 3. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 4. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 5. MATTHIAS: The man chosen to replace Judas among the Twelve (Acts 1:23-26) 6. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 7. UZZIAH: The king struck with leprosy after unlawfully burning incense (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 8. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 9. MEPHIBOSHETH: Jonathan’s son whom David showed kindness (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 10. MICAIAH: The prophet who warned Ahab despite the other prophets’ assurances (1 Kings 22:13-28)',
        'Jeremiah 36:20-26; Judges 3:15-22; Jeremiah 38:7-13; 2 Kings 22:14-20; Acts 1:23-26; 1 Samuel 25:23-42; 2 Chronicles 26:16-21; Acts 4:36-37; 2 Samuel 9:1-13; 1 Kings 22:13-28',
