        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 3. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 4. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 5. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 6. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 7. SMYRNA: City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death (Revelation 2:8-10) 8. PATMOS: Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation (Revelation 1:9) 9. PAPHOS: City on Cyprus where proconsul Sergius Paulus was converted after Elymas was struck blind (Acts 13:6-12) 10. ICONIUM: City in Asia Minor where a great multitude of Jews and Greeks believed despite severe opposition (Acts 14:1-5)',
