        '1. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 2. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 3. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 4. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 5. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 6. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13) 7. SECUNDUS: Thessalonian Christian who accompanied Paul on his journey carrying the relief collection to Jerusalem (Acts 20:4) 8. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 9. SAPPHIRA: Wife of Ananias who colluded in withholding money and fell dead before Peter (Acts 5:1-10) 10. PROCHORUS: One of the seven godly men chosen to oversee daily food distribution to Greek-speaking widows (Acts 6:5)',
        'Revelation 3:7-8; Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20; 1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1; Romans 16:21; Romans 16:15; Titus 3:13; Acts 20:4; Acts 24:1-8; Acts 5:1-10; Acts 6:5',
