        'THEOLDERBROTHER|TIBNISONOFGINATH|ZAPHENATHPANEAH|EHUD|ZACCHAEUS|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|SIMONTHEZEALOT|MIRIAM|ELEAZAR',
        '1. THEOLDERBROTHER: In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, who became furiously angry, refused to enter the celebration banquet, and complained that a young goat was never given to him? (Luke 15:28-30) 2. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 3. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 4. EHUD: • I was a judge in Israel.
• I was left-handed.
• I killed Eglon, king of Moab, with an eighteen-inch double-edged dagger.
Who am I? (Judges 3:15-22) 5. ZACCHAEUS: • I was a tax collector in Jericho.
• I was short in stature.
• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.
Who am I? (Luke 19:1-10) 6. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
Who am I? (Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31) 7. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 8. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Two prominent apostles were named Simon. Which Simon was also designated as ''the Zealot'' or ''the Cananaean''? (Luke 6:15; Matthew 10:4) 9. MIRIAM: Which prominent sister of Moses and Aaron watched over baby Moses in the Nile and later led Israel''s women in song at the Red Sea? (Exodus 2:4; 15:20-21; Numbers 26:59) 10. ELEAZAR: Which priest was the father of Phinehas, who succeeded Aaron as high priest atop Mount Hor? (Exodus 6:25; Numbers 20:25-28)',
