        'ANNA|CHUZA|DAVID|ANNAS|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|ELIAB|ELEAZAR|ABIGAIL|ABISHAI',
        '1. ANNA: • I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.
• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.
• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.
Who am I? (Luke 2:36-38) 2. CHUZA: Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth? (Luke 8:3) 3. DAVID: When the angel Gabriel announced the virgin birth of Jesus to Mary in Nazareth, he stated that God would give Him the royal throne of which Old Testament king? (Luke 1:32) 4. ANNAS: Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane? (John 18:13) 5. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
