        '1. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 2. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 3. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 4. JOHNTHEAPOSTLE: Which beloved apostle was banished in elderly exile to the penal island of Patmos on the Lord''s Day, heard a voice like a trumpet, and collapsed as though dead before the blazing glorified Son of Man? (Revelation 1:9-17) 5. PAULSAULOFTARSUS: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens? (Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22) 6. SIMONPETER: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Called while mending nets at Sea of Galilee -> Confessed Christ at Caesarea Philippi -> Denied the Lord three times by a courtyard fire -> Preached the Pentecost sermon in Jerusalem -> Miraculously delivered from Herod''s prison by an angel? (Matthew 4:18; Matthew 16:16; Matthew 26:69-75; Acts 2:14; Acts 12:6-11) 7. JANNESANDJAMBRES: In 2 Timothy 3:8, which two traditional names does Paul reveal for the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses before Pharaoh, comparing them to corrupt end-times teachers? (2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11) 8. KORAHSONOFIZHAR: Which Levite rebel led 250 prominent community leaders against Moses and Aaron in Numbers 16, whose fatal rebellion is linked in Jude 11 with the error of Balaam? (Numbers 16:1-35; Jude 1:11) 9. SHIPHRAHANDPUAH: Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of th