        '1. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 2. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 3. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 4. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 5. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 6. NEBUZARADAN: Captain of the Babylonian royal bodyguard who burned the Temple and broke down Jerusalem''s walls (2 Kings 25:8-11) 7. RABSHAKEH: Assyrian military envoy who shouted blasphemous intimidation in Hebrew on Jerusalem''s wall (2 Kings 18:17-35) 8. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 9. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 10. TRYPHENA: Faithful Christian worker in Rome greeted warmly by the Apostle Paul (Romans 16:12)',
