        'PHYLACTERY|BREASTPIECE|MERCYSEAT|CANDLESTICK|FRANKINCENSE|SHOWBREAD|JEHOIAKIM|EHUD|EBEDMELECH|HULDAH',
        '1. PHYLACTERY: Small leather box containing Scripture verses worn on forehead and arm during prayer (Matthew 23:5; Deuteronomy 6:8) 2. BREASTPIECE: Square embroidered pouch mounted with twelve precious engraved gemstones worn by the high priest (Exodus 28:15-21) 3. MERCYSEAT: Pure gold lid atop the Ark of the Covenant between the wings of two golden cherubim (Exodus 25:17-22) 4. CANDLESTICK: Seven-branched pure gold lampstand hammered from a single talent of gold for the Holy Place (Exodus 25:31-37) 5. FRANKINCENSE: Fragrant white resin burned on the altar of incense and presented as a gift by the Magi (Exodus 30:34; Matthew 2:11) 6. SHOWBREAD: Twelve consecrated loaves of bread arranged weekly before the LORD on the golden table (Leviticus 24:5-9) 7. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 8. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 9. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 10. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20)',
