        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 3. OLYMPAS: Roman disciple greeted alongside Philologus, Julia, and Nereus (Romans 16:15) 4. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 5. PATROBAS: Christian disciple in Rome greeted by Paul in Romans 16:14 (Romans 16:14) 6. PHLEGON: Roman brother greeted alongside Hermes, Patrobas, and Hermas in Romans 16 (Romans 16:14) 7. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13) 8. PUDENS: Roman believer who sent greetings to Timothy in Paul''s final letter (2 Timothy 4:21) 9. EPAPHRODITUS: Philippian messenger who risked his life carrying aid to Paul in prison and fell gravely ill (Philippians 2:25-30) 10. SOPATER: Son of Pyrrhus from Berea who traveled with Paul into Asia (Acts 20:4)',
