        '1. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 2. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 3. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13) 4. SECUNDUS: Thessalonian Christian who accompanied Paul on his journey carrying the relief collection to Jerusalem (Acts 20:4) 5. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 6. SAPPHIRA: Wife of Ananias who colluded in withholding money and fell dead before Peter (Acts 5:1-10) 7. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 8. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 9. NEBUZARADAN: Captain of the Babylonian royal bodyguard who burned the Temple and broke down Jerusalem''s walls (2 Kings 25:8-11) 10. RABSHAKEH: Assyrian military envoy who shouted blasphemous intimidation in Hebrew on Jerusalem''s wall (2 Kings 18:17-35)',
