        '1. MELCHIZEDEK: King of Salem and priest of God Most High who blessed Abram (Genesis 14:18-20) 2. ONESIPHORUS: Ephesian Christian who searched diligently for Paul in Rome and refreshed him (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 3. EBEDMELECH: Cushite royal official who rescued Jeremiah from the muddy cistern with rags (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 4. EPAPHRAS: Faithful minister from Colossae who wrestled intensely in prayer for the saints (Colossians 1:7; 4:12) 5. HULDAH: Prophetess in Jerusalem consulted by King Josiah when the Book of the Law was recovered (2 Kings 22:14-20) 6. TYCHICUS: Dear brother and faithful minister Paul sent with epistles to Ephesus and Colossae (Ephesians 6:21; Colossians 4:7) 7. ARISTARCHUS: Macedonian of Thessalonica and fellow prisoner with Paul dragged into the Ephesian theater (Acts 19:29; 27:2; Colossians 4:10) 8. SOSTHENES: Ruler of the Corinthian synagogue beaten before Gallio, later co-sender of 1 Corinthians (Acts 18:17; 1 Corinthians 1:1) 9. TERTIUS: Scribe who penned the Epistle to the Romans as Paul dictated (Romans 16:22) 10. ZILPAH: Leah''s handmaid who bore Gad and Asher to Jacob (Genesis 30:9-13)',
