        '1. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 2. EPHOD: A priestly garment associated with the high priest (Exodus 28:6-12) 3. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 4. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 5. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 6. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 7. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5) 8. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 9. HAGGAI: The prophet who urged the returned exiles to rebuild the temple (Haggai 1:1-8) 10. GIDEON: The judge who reduced his army to three hundred men (Judges 7:1-8)',
