        '1. GIBEON: City whose inhabitants tricked Joshua with moldy bread, where the sun stood still in battle (Joshua 9:3-15; 10:12) 2. GEHAZI: Greedy servant of Elisha struck with Naaman''s leprosy after running after silver and garments (2 Kings 5:20-27) 3. PASSOVER: The feast commemorating Israel’s deliverance from Egypt (Exodus 12:1-14) 4. URIM: An object kept in the high priest’s breastpiece for decision-making (Exodus 28:30) 5. HULDAH: Prophetess in Jerusalem consulted by King Josiah when the Book of the Law was recovered (2 Kings 22:14-20) 6. SHOFAR: A ram’s horn sounded at Jericho (Joshua 6:4-5) 7. JEROBOAM: The king whose rebellion divided the kingdom after Solomon (1 Kings 12:16-20) 8. HABAKKUK: The prophet who asked why injustice seemed to go unpunished (Habakkuk 1:2-4) 9. NAHUM: The prophet whose book announces judgment against Nineveh (Nahum 1:1) 10. SHEPHERD: The image Jesus used when describing his care for the sheep (John 10:11-14)',
