        '"SHIBBOLETH","SANBALLAT","ZERUIAH","MEPHIBOSHETH","ZACHARIAS","TABERNACLE","ZACCHAEUS","TROPHIMUS","ZEPHANIAH","JEHOIAKIM"'::text[],
        'SHIBBOLETH|SANBALLAT|ZERUIAH|MEPHIBOSHETH|ZACHARIAS|TABERNACLE|ZACCHAEUS|TROPHIMUS|ZEPHANIAH|JEHOIAKIM',
        '1. SHIBBOLETH: Password word used by Jephthah''s men at Jordan crossings to detect Ephraimites who pronounced it Sibboleth (Judges 12:6) 2. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 3. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 4. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 5. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 6. TABERNACLE: The portable sanctuary Israel built in the wilderness (Exodus 25:8-9) 7. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 8. TROPHIMUS: The Ephesian whom Paul left sick at Miletus (2 Timothy 4:20) 9. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 10. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26)',
        'Judges 12:6; Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8; 1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18; 2 Samuel 9:1-13; Luke 1:5-13; Exodus 25:8-9; Luke 19:1-10; 2 Timothy 4:20; Zephaniah 1:1-7; Jeremiah 36:20-26',
