        '1. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 2. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 3. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 4. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 5. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 6. SMYRNA: City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death (Revelation 2:8-10) 7. PATMOS: Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation (Revelation 1:9) 8. PAPHOS: City on Cyprus where proconsul Sergius Paulus was converted after Elymas was struck blind (Acts 13:6-12) 9. LYSTRA: City where Paul healed a crippled man, was hailed as Hermes, and was subsequently stoned and left for dead (Acts 14:8-19) 10. MILETUS: Port city where Paul gave his poignant farewell address to the elders of the church of Ephesus (Acts 20:17-38)',
        'Revelation 3:14-17; Revelation 3:7-8; Revelation 3:1-3; Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20; Revelation 2:12-13; Revelation 2:8-10; Revelation 1:9; Acts 13:6-12; Acts 14:8-19; Acts 20:17-38',
