        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 3. LUCIUS: Kinsman of Paul or prophet/teacher from Cyrene mentioned in Antioch and Romans (Acts 13:1; Romans 16:21) 4. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 5. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 6. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 7. OLYMPAS: Roman disciple greeted alongside Philologus, Julia, and Nereus (Romans 16:15) 8. NEREUS: Believer greeted with his sister and Olympas in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 9. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 10. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15)',
