        'ARCHELAUS|CANDACE|ADONIJAH|LYSANIAS|DRUSILLA|COZBI|MAAKAH|JEHOSHEBA|ABNERSONOFNER|MANAEN',
        '1. ARCHELAUS: Which son of Herod the Great ruled over Judea after Herod''s death, whose cruel reputation caused Joseph to avoid Judea and take Jesus to Galilee? (Matthew 2:22) 2. CANDACE: Which royal title and name belonged to the queen of the Ethiopians whose chief court treasurer was baptized by Philip on the desert road? (Acts 8:27) 3. ADONIJAH: Which ambitious son of David by Haggith declared himself king at En-rogel when David was old, backed by General Joab and Priest Abiathar? (1 Kings 1:5-9) 4. LYSANIAS: Which regional ruler was tetrarch of Abilene during the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, as recorded in Luke''s historical synchronization? (Luke 3:1) 5. DRUSILLA: Which Jewish royal woman, the daughter of Herod Agrippa I and sister of Bernice, was the wife of Roman Governor Felix when Paul spoke to them in Caesarea? (Acts 24:24) 6. COZBI: Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor? (Numbers 25:15-18) 7. MAAKAH: Which queen mother (Gebirah) of Judah was stripped of her royal dignity by King Asa because she had erected an abominable image for Asherah? (1 Kings 15:13) 8. JEHOSHEBA: Which royal princess of Judah stole away baby prince Joash when Queen Mother Athaliah was slaughtering all royal heirs, hiding him in the temple? (2 Kings 11:2) 9. ABNERSONOFNER: Who was Saul''s commander-in-chief who crowned Saul''s son Ish-bosheth king at Mahanaim, but was later stabbed to death by Joab at Hebron''s city gate? (2 Samuel 2:8; 2 Samuel 3:27) 10. MANAEN: Which Christian teacher in Antioch was intimately connected to royalty, having been brought up with (a foster-brother of) Herod the tetrarch? (Acts 13:1)',
