        'HERODANTIPAS|ADONIRAMHADORAM|LYSANIAS|UZZIAHAZARIAH|TIBNISONOFGINATH|ZIMRI|JEHOSHEBA|ABNERSONOFNER|HADADTHEEDOMITE|CAESARAUGUSTUS',
        '1. HERODANTIPAS: Which ruler foolishly bound himself with an oath before banquet guests to grant a dancing girl anything, resulting in the beheading of John the Baptist? (Matthew 14:6-10) 2. ADONIRAMHADORAM: Which royal supervisor of forced labor was dispatched by King Rehoboam to negotiate with the rebellious northern tribes, only to be stoned to death by all Israel? (1 Kings 12:18) 3. LYSANIAS: Which regional ruler was tetrarch of Abilene during the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, as recorded in Luke''s historical synchronization? (Luke 3:1) 4. UZZIAHAZARIAH: Which king of Judah ruled for 52 years and prospered greatly, but was struck with leprosy in the temple after arrogantly trying to burn incense? (2 Chronicles 26:16-21) 5. TIBNISONOFGINATH: Following Zimri''s death, which rival claimant divided Israel and battled Omri for four years before dying, leaving Omri sole monarch? (1 Kings 16:21-22) 6. ZIMRI: Which military commander seized the throne of the northern kingdom of Israel and reigned for only seven days in Tirzah before setting fire to the palace over himself? (1 Kings 16:15-18) 7. JEHOSHEBA: Which royal princess of Judah stole away baby prince Joash when Queen Mother Athaliah was slaughtering all royal heirs, hiding him in the temple? (2 Kings 11:2) 8. ABNERSONOFNER: Who was Saul''s commander-in-chief who crowned Saul''s son Ish-bosheth king at Mahanaim, but was later stabbed to death by Joab at Hebron''s city gate? (2 Samuel 2:8; 2 Samuel 3:27) 9. HADADTHEEDOMITE: Which Edomite of royal descent fled to Egypt as a child when Joab wiped out Edom''s males, married Queen Tahpenes'' sister, and returned to oppose King Solomon? (1 Kings 11:14-22) 10. CAESARAUGUSTUS: Which Roman emperor issued the royal decree that a census should be taken of the entire Roman world, leading Joseph and Mary to travel to Bethlehem? (Luke 2:1)',
