        'ZEPHANIAH|ZACCHAEUS|ZACHARIAS|LAODICEA|PHILADELPHIA|SARDIS|THYATIRA|PERGAMUM|SMYRNA|PATMOS',
        '1. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 2. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 3. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 4. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 5. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 6. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 7. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 8. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 9. SMYRNA: City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death (Revelation 2:8-10) 10. PATMOS: Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation (Revelation 1:9)',
        'Zephaniah 1:1-7; Luke 19:1-10; Luke 1:5-13; Revelation 3:14-17; Revelation 3:7-8; Revelation 3:1-3; Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20; Revelation 2:12-13; Revelation 2:8-10; Revelation 1:9',
