        '1. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 2. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 3. SHIBBOLETH: Password word used by Jephthah''s men at Jordan crossings to detect Ephraimites who pronounced it Sibboleth (Judges 12:6) 4. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 5. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 6. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 7. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 8. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 9. NEBUZARADAN: Captain of the Babylonian royal bodyguard who burned the Temple and broke down Jerusalem''s walls (2 Kings 25:8-11) 10. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18)',
