        'PATMOS|PAPHOS|ICONIUM|LYSTRA|DERBE|CENCHREAE|BEREA|LAODICEA|MILETUS|AIJALON',
        '1. PATMOS: Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation (Revelation 1:9) 2. PAPHOS: City on Cyprus where proconsul Sergius Paulus was converted after Elymas was struck blind (Acts 13:6-12) 3. ICONIUM: City in Asia Minor where a great multitude of Jews and Greeks believed despite severe opposition (Acts 14:1-5) 4. LYSTRA: City where Paul healed a crippled man, was hailed as Hermes, and was subsequently stoned and left for dead (Acts 14:8-19) 5. DERBE: Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra (Acts 14:20-21) 6. CENCHREAE: Port of Corinth where Paul had his hair cut because of a vow, and home of deaconess Phoebe (Acts 18:18; Romans 16:1) 7. BEREA: Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings (Acts 17:10-12) 8. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 9. MILETUS: Port city where Paul gave his poignant farewell address to the elders of the church of Ephesus (Acts 20:17-38) 10. AIJALON: Valley over which Joshua commanded the moon to stand motionless during the fight for Gibeon (Joshua 10:12-13)',
        'Revelation 1:9; Acts 13:6-12; Acts 14:1-5; Acts 14:8-19; Acts 14:20-21; Acts 18:18; Romans 16:1; Acts 17:10-12; Revelation 3:14-17; Acts 20:17-38; Joshua 10:12-13',
        '{"entries":[{"number":1,"answer":"PATMOS","clue":"Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation","reference":"Revelation 1:9","direction":"across"},{"number":2,"answer":"PAPHOS","clue":"City on Cyprus where proconsul Sergius Paulus was converted after Elymas was struck blind","reference":"Acts 13:6-12","direction":"down"},{"number":3,"answer":"ICONIUM","clue":"City in Asia Minor where a great multitude of Jews and Greeks believed despite severe opposition","reference":"Acts 14:1-5","direction":"across"},{"number":4,"answer":"LYSTRA","clue":"City where Paul healed a crippled man, was hailed as Hermes, and was subsequently stoned and left for dead","reference":"Acts 14:8-19","direction":"down"},{"number":5,"answer":"DERBE","clue":"Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra","reference":"Acts 14:20-21","direction":"down"},{"number":6,"answer":"CENCHREAE","clue":"Port of Corinth where Paul had his hair cut because of a vow, and home of deaconess Phoebe","reference":"Acts 18:18; Romans 16:1","direction":"across"},{"number":7,"answer":"BEREA","clue":"Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings","reference":"Acts 17:10-12","direction":"across"},{"number":8,"answer":"LAODICEA","clue":"Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth","reference":"Revelation 3:14-17","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"MILETUS","clue":"Port city where Paul gave his poignant farewell address to the elders of the church of Ephesus","reference":"Acts 20:17-38","direction":"across"},{"number":10,"answer":"AIJALON","clue":"Valley over which Joshua commanded the moon to stand motionless during the fight for Gibeon","reference":"Joshua 10:12-13","direction":"down"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"Scripture Knowledge","stage":5,"stage_title":"Scripture Knowledge","level_theme":"Scripture Crossword Boss","difficulty":"Very Hard","timerSeconds":150,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
