(
        'bible-crossword-l25-c4',
        'bible-crossword',
        25,
        4,
        'Stage 5 Boss: Connect dense cross-testament scriptural themes against the clock.',
        '"PHILADELPHIA","SARDIS","THYATIRA","PERGAMUM","SMYRNA","SHILOH","ZIKLAG","RABBONI","TALITHA","MARANATHA"'::text[],
        'PHILADELPHIA|SARDIS|THYATIRA|PERGAMUM|SMYRNA|SHILOH|ZIKLAG|RABBONI|TALITHA|MARANATHA',
        '1. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 2. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 3. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 4. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 5. SMYRNA: City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death (Revelation 2:8-10) 6. SHILOH: Early central sanctuary in Ephraim where the Tabernacle stood and young Samuel ministered (Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 3:21) 7. ZIKLAG: Philistine border city given to David by King Achish, raided and burned by Amalekites (1 Samuel 27:6; 30:1) 8. RABBONI: Aramaic title meaning "My Great Teacher", spoken joyfully by Mary Magdalene outside the empty tomb (John 20:16) 9. TALITHA: Aramaic word spoken by Jesus meaning "Little girl" before saying "arise" (Mark 5:41) 10. MARANATHA: Aramaic prayer meaning "Our Lord, come!" with which Paul closed 1 Corinthians (1 Corinthians 16:22)',
