        '1. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 2. EHUD: • I was a judge in Israel.
• I was left-handed.
• I killed Eglon, king of Moab, with an eighteen-inch double-edged dagger.
Who am I? (Judges 3:15-22) 3. ZACCHAEUS: • I was a tax collector in Jericho.
• I was short in stature.
• I climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus over the crowd.
Who am I? (Luke 19:1-10) 4. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
