        '1. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 2. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 3. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 4. LUCIUS: Kinsman of Paul or prophet/teacher from Cyrene mentioned in Antioch and Romans (Acts 13:1; Romans 16:21) 5. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 6. OLYMPAS: Roman disciple greeted alongside Philologus, Julia, and Nereus (Romans 16:15) 7. NEREUS: Believer greeted with his sister and Olympas in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 8. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 9. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 10. PHLEGON: Roman brother greeted alongside Hermes, Patrobas, and Hermas in Romans 16 (Romans 16:14)',
