        'ABNER|ABDON|ELON|JASON|ARTEMAS|BARUCH|AMASA|CLAUDIA|CARPUS|APPHIA',
        '1. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 2. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 3. ELON: Judge from the tribe of Zebulun who led Israel for ten years (Judges 12:11-12) 4. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 5. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 6. BARUCH: Faithful scribe who recorded Jeremiah''s prophecies from dictation onto a papyrus scroll (Jeremiah 36:4-10) 7. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 8. CLAUDIA: Christian sister in Rome who sent greetings to Timothy alongside Eubulus, Pudens, and Linus (2 Timothy 4:21) 9. CARPUS: Believer in Troas at whose house Paul left his cloak and parchments (2 Timothy 4:13) 10. APPHIA: Christian sister greeted in Philemon alongside Archippus and the church in Philemon''s house (Philemon 1:2)',
        '2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12; Judges 12:13-15; Judges 12:11-12; Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21; Titus 3:12; Jeremiah 36:4-10; 2 Samuel 20:9-10; 2 Timothy 4:21; 2 Timothy 4:13; Philemon 1:2',
