        '1. EBEDMELECH: Cushite royal official who rescued Jeremiah from the muddy cistern with rags (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 2. EPAPHRAS: Faithful minister from Colossae who wrestled intensely in prayer for the saints (Colossians 1:7; 4:12) 3. HULDAH: Prophetess in Jerusalem consulted by King Josiah when the Book of the Law was recovered (2 Kings 22:14-20) 4. BEZALEL: Chief craftsman filled with the Spirit of God to construct the Tabernacle furnishings (Exodus 31:1-5) 5. ARISTARCHUS: Macedonian of Thessalonica and fellow prisoner with Paul dragged into the Ephesian theater (Acts 19:29; 27:2; Colossians 4:10) 6. EHUD: Left-handed Benjaminite judge who delivered Israel by striking down King Eglon of Moab (Judges 3:15-22) 7. JAEL: Wife of Heber the Kenite who drove a tent peg into Sisera while he slept (Judges 4:17-22) 8. BENAIAH: Mighty warrior who struck down a lion in a pit on a snowy day and led David''s bodyguard (2 Samuel 23:20-23) 9. MAHLAH: Eldest daughter of Zelophehad who petitioned Moses for land possession among their father''s brothers (Numbers 27:1-7) 10. HOGLAH: Third daughter of Zelophehad who secured ancestral inheritance in Manasseh (Numbers 26:33; 27:1)',
