        '1. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 2. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 3. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 4. RABBONI: Aramaic title meaning "My Great Teacher", spoken joyfully by Mary Magdalene outside the empty tomb (John 20:16) 5. TALITHA: Aramaic word spoken by Jesus meaning "Little girl" before saying "arise" (Mark 5:41) 6. MARANATHA: Aramaic prayer meaning "Our Lord, come!" with which Paul closed 1 Corinthians (1 Corinthians 16:22) 7. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 8. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 9. PATROBAS: Christian disciple in Rome greeted by Paul in Romans 16:14 (Romans 16:14) 10. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13)',
