        '1. DERBE: Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra (Acts 14:20-21) 2. BEREA: Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings (Acts 17:10-12) 3. APPHIA: Christian sister greeted in Philemon alongside Archippus and the church in Philemon''s house (Philemon 1:2) 4. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 5. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 6. CORBAN: Hebrew/Aramaic term meaning a gift devoted to God, rebuked when used to bypass caring for parents (Mark 7:11) 7. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 8. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 9. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 10. CLAUDIA: Christian sister in Rome who sent greetings to Timothy alongside Eubulus, Pudens, and Linus (2 Timothy 4:21)',
