        '1. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 2. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 3. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 4. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5) 5. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 6. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 7. BEREA: The place whose people examined the Scriptures daily (Acts 17:10-12) 8. EPHOD: A priestly garment associated with the high priest (Exodus 28:6-12) 9. LYDIA: The seller of purple goods who hosted Paul in Philippi (Acts 16:14-15) 10. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26)',
        'Judges 3:15-22; 2 Kings 22:14-20; Judges 4:17-22; Exodus 31:1-5; 1 Samuel 25:23-42; Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11; Acts 17:10-12; Exodus 28:6-12; Acts 16:14-15; Jeremiah 36:20-26',
