        '"LAODICEA","PHILADELPHIA","SARDIS","THYATIRA","PERGAMUM","SMYRNA","TROAS","RABBONI","TALITHA","MARANATHA"'::text[],
        'LAODICEA|PHILADELPHIA|SARDIS|THYATIRA|PERGAMUM|SMYRNA|TROAS|RABBONI|TALITHA|MARANATHA',
        '1. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 2. PHILADELPHIA: City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut (Revelation 3:7-8) 3. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 4. THYATIRA: City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel (Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20) 5. PERGAMUM: City described in Revelation as the place "where Satan has his throne" (Revelation 2:12-13) 6. SMYRNA: City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death (Revelation 2:8-10) 7. TROAS: Coastal city in Mysia where Paul saw the night vision of the man of Macedonia pleading "Come over and help us" (Acts 16:8-10) 8. RABBONI: Aramaic title meaning "My Great Teacher", spoken joyfully by Mary Magdalene outside the empty tomb (John 20:16) 9. TALITHA: Aramaic word spoken by Jesus meaning "Little girl" before saying "arise" (Mark 5:41) 10. MARANATHA: Aramaic prayer meaning "Our Lord, come!" with which Paul closed 1 Corinthians (1 Corinthians 16:22)',
        'Revelation 3:14-17; Revelation 3:7-8; Revelation 3:1-3; Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20; Revelation 2:12-13; Revelation 2:8-10; Acts 16:8-10; John 20:16; Mark 5:41; 1 Corinthians 16:22',
        '{"entries":[{"number":1,"answer":"LAODICEA","clue":"Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth","reference":"Revelation 3:14-17","direction":"across"},{"number":2,"answer":"PHILADELPHIA","clue":"City whose faithful church was set before an open door that no one could shut","reference":"Revelation 3:7-8","direction":"down"},{"number":3,"answer":"SARDIS","clue":"City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ","reference":"Revelation 3:1-3","direction":"across"},{"number":4,"answer":"THYATIRA","clue":"City known for its purple dye trade, home of Lydia, and rebuked in Revelation for tolerating Jezebel","reference":"Acts 16:14; Revelation 2:18-20","direction":"down"},{"number":5,"answer":"PERGAMUM","clue":"City described in Revelation as the place \"where Satan has his throne\"","reference":"Revelation 2:12-13","direction":"across"},{"number":6,"answer":"SMYRNA","clue":"City of Asia Minor whose persecuted church was promised the crown of life if faithful unto death","reference":"Revelation 2:8-10","direction":"down"},{"number":7,"answer":"TROAS","clue":"Coastal city in Mysia where Paul saw the night vision of the man of Macedonia pleading \"Come over and help us\"","reference":"Acts 16:8-10","direction":"across"},{"number":8,"answer":"RABBONI","clue":"Aramaic title meaning \"My Great Teacher\", spoken joyfully by Mary Magdalene outside the empty tomb","reference":"John 20:16","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"TALITHA","clue":"Aramaic word spoken by Jesus meaning \"Little girl\" before saying \"arise\"","reference":"Mark 5:41","direction":"across"},{"number":10,"answer":"MARANATHA","clue":"Aramaic prayer meaning \"Our Lord, come!\" with which Paul closed 1 Corinthians","reference":"1 Corinthians 16:22","direction":"down"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"The Forgotten People","stage":6,"stage_title":"The Forgotten People","level_theme":"Paul''s Companions","difficulty":"Difficult","timerSeconds":160,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
