(
        'bible-crossword-l29-c3',
        'bible-crossword',
        29,
        3,
        'Navigate generational lists, ancestral houses, and tribal allotments in the grid.',
        '"SOSIPATER","PHILOLOGUS","ZENAS","SECUNDUS","TERTULLUS","SAPPHIRA","PROCHORUS","SANBALLAT","ZERESH","VASHTI"'::text[],
        'SOSIPATER|PHILOLOGUS|ZENAS|SECUNDUS|TERTULLUS|SAPPHIRA|PROCHORUS|SANBALLAT|ZERESH|VASHTI',
        '1. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 2. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 3. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13) 4. SECUNDUS: Thessalonian Christian who accompanied Paul on his journey carrying the relief collection to Jerusalem (Acts 20:4) 5. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 6. SAPPHIRA: Wife of Ananias who colluded in withholding money and fell dead before Peter (Acts 5:1-10) 7. PROCHORUS: One of the seven godly men chosen to oversee daily food distribution to Greek-speaking widows (Acts 6:5) 8. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 9. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 10. VASHTI: Queen of Persia who refused King Ahasuerus'' command to display her beauty before banquet guests (Esther 1:10-12)',
        'Romans 16:21; Romans 16:15; Titus 3:13; Acts 20:4; Acts 24:1-8; Acts 5:1-10; Acts 6:5; Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8; Esther 5:14; 6:13; Esther 1:10-12',
