        'ANNA|CHUZA|AGABUS|ANNAS|DAVID|COZBI|DEBORAH|BARNABAS|ABIGAIL|ABISHAI',
        '1. ANNA: • I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.
• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.
• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.
Who am I? (Luke 2:36-38) 2. CHUZA: Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth? (Luke 8:3) 3. AGABUS: • I was a prophet who came down from Judea to Antioch and Caesarea.
• I predicted by the Holy Spirit a severe famine across the entire Roman empire under Emperor Claudius.
• I tied my own hands and feet with Paul''s belt to foretell his Jerusalem arrest.
Who am I? (Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11) 4. ANNAS: Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane? (John 18:13) 5. DAVID: When the angel Gabriel announced the virgin birth of Jesus to Mary in Nazareth, he stated that God would give Him the royal throne of which Old Testament king? (Luke 1:32) 6. COZBI: Which Midianite princess, daughter of Zur, was boldly brought into the camp of Israel by Zimri during the Baal of Peor crisis, and was executed by Phinehas with a javelin? (Numbers 25:6-18) 7. DEBORAH: • I was a prophetess who judged Israel under a palm tree.
• I summoned Barak to take ten thousand men to Mount Tabor.
• I sang a victory song with Barak after Sisera’s defeat.
Who am I? (Judges 4:4-14; 5:1-31) 8. BARNABAS: • I was an early Christian disciple from Cyprus.
• My original name was Joseph, but the apostles gave me a new name meaning ''Son of Encouragement''.
• I sold a field and laid the money at the apostles'' feet.
Who am I? (Acts 4:36-37) 9. ABIGAIL: Which wife of David was the former wife of the harsh rancher Nabal, who acted with wisdom to prevent David from shedding blood? (1 Samuel 25:3, 39-42) 10. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21)',
