        'Stage 6 Boss: Conquer a formidable grid of obscure biblical men and women.',
        '"PAULSAULOFTARSUS","JANNESANDJAMBRES","SHIPHRAHANDPUAH","THESADDUCEES","THEOLDERBROTHER","SIMONOFCYRENE","LAZARUSOFBETHANY","SIMONTHELEPER","SIMONTHEZEALOT","SERGIUSPAULUS"'::text[],
        'PAULSAULOFTARSUS|JANNESANDJAMBRES|SHIPHRAHANDPUAH|THESADDUCEES|THEOLDERBROTHER|SIMONOFCYRENE|LAZARUSOFBETHANY|SIMONTHELEPER|SIMONTHEZEALOT|SERGIUSPAULUS',
        '1. PAULSAULOFTARSUS: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens? (Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22) 2. JANNESANDJAMBRES: In 2 Timothy 3:8, which two traditional names does Paul reveal for the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses before Pharaoh, comparing them to corrupt end-times teachers? (2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11) 3. SHIPHRAHANDPUAH: Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own? (Exodus 1:15-21) 4. THESADDUCEES: Which religious group in Jerusalem, who denied the resurrection of the dead, challenged Jesus with the hypothetical problem of a woman married to seven brothers? (Matthew 22:23-28; Luke 20:27-33) 5. THEOLDERBROTHER: In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, who became furiously angry, refused to enter the celebration banquet, and complained that a young goat was never given to him? (Luke 15:28-30) 6. SIMONOFCYRENE: Distinguish these biblical Simons: Which Simon from North Africa was compelled by Roman soldiers to carry Jesus'' heavy wooden cross-beam, whose sons were Alexander and Rufus? (Matthew 27:32; Mark 15:21) 7. LAZARUSOFBETHANY: Distinguish these biblical Lazaruses: Which Lazarus was the beloved friend whom Jesus wept over and raised to life after being dead in a rock tomb for four days? (John 11:1-44) 8. SIMONTHELEPER: In whose house in Bethany was Jesus reclining at table when a woman poured a costly alabaster flask of pure nard over His head? (Matthew 26:6; Mark 14:3) 9. SIMONTHEZEALOT: Which of the twelve apostles is called ''the Cananite'' in Matthew and Mark, and ''the Zealot'' in Luke, to distinguish him from Simon Peter? (Matthew 10:4; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13) 10. SERGIUSPAULUS: Which Roman proconsul of Cyprus desired to hear the word of God and believed after seeing the false prophet and sorcerer Elymas struck blind by Paul? (Acts 13:6-12)',
        'Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22; 2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11; Exodus 1:15-21; Matthew 22:23-28; Luke 20:27-33; Luke 15:28-30; Matthew 27:32; Mark 15:21; John 11:1-44; Matthew 26:6; Mark 14:3; Matthew 10:4; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13; Acts 13:6-12',
