ence":"John 11:1-44","direction":"across"},{"number":8,"answer":"SIMONTHELEPER","clue":"In whose house in Bethany was Jesus reclining at table when a woman poured a costly alabaster flask of pure nard over His head?","reference":"Matthew 26:6; Mark 14:3","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"SIMONTHEZEALOT","clue":"Which of the twelve apostles is called ''the Cananite'' in Matthew and Mark, and ''the Zealot'' in Luke, to distinguish him from Simon Peter?","reference":"Matthew 10:4; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13","direction":"across"},{"number":10,"answer":"SERGIUSPAULUS","clue":"Which Roman proconsul of Cyprus desired to hear the word of God and believed after seeing the false prophet and sorcerer Elymas struck blind by Paul?","reference":"Acts 13:6-12","direction":"down"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"The Forgotten People","stage":6,"stage_title":"The Forgotten People","level_theme":"Forgotten People Boss","difficulty":"Difficult","timerSeconds":140,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
