        '1. MELCHIZEDEK: King of Salem and priest of God Most High who blessed Abram (Genesis 14:18-20) 2. ONESIPHORUS: Ephesian Christian who searched diligently for Paul in Rome and refreshed him (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 3. EBEDMELECH: Cushite royal official who rescued Jeremiah from the muddy cistern with rags (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 4. TYCHICUS: Dear brother and faithful minister Paul sent with epistles to Ephesus and Colossae (Ephesians 6:21; Colossians 4:7) 5. ARISTARCHUS: Macedonian of Thessalonica and fellow prisoner with Paul dragged into the Ephesian theater (Acts 19:29; 27:2; Colossians 4:10) 6. SOSTHENES: Ruler of the Corinthian synagogue beaten before Gallio, later co-sender of 1 Corinthians (Acts 18:17; 1 Corinthians 1:1) 7. TERTIUS: Scribe who penned the Epistle to the Romans as Paul dictated (Romans 16:22) 8. ZILPAH: Leah''s handmaid who bore Gad and Asher to Jacob (Genesis 30:9-13) 9. QUARTUS: Believer in Corinth whom Paul greeted in Romans as "our brother" (Romans 16:23) 10. TIRZAH: One of the five inheritance-seeking daughters of Zelophehad, also early capital of northern Israel (Numbers 27:1; 1 Kings 14:17)',
        'Genesis 14:18-20; 2 Timothy 1:16-18; Jeremiah 38:7-13; Ephesians 6:21; Colossians 4:7; Acts 19:29; 27:2; Colossians 4:10; Acts 18:17; 1 Corinthians 1:1; Romans 16:22; Genesis 30:9-13; Romans 16:23; Numbers 27:1; 1 Kings 14:17',
