        '1. BEREA: The place whose people examined the Scriptures daily (Acts 17:10-12) 2. COZBI: Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor? (Numbers 25:15-18) 3. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 4. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 5. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 6. ABISHAI: Which brother of Joab and Asahel was chief of the Thirty champions and once slew 300 enemy warriors with his spear? (2 Samuel 23:18-19; 1 Chronicles 11:20-21) 7. EPHOD: A priestly garment associated with the high priest (Exodus 28:6-12) 8. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42) 9. BETHUEL: Which Aramean father of Rebekah and Laban acknowledged God’s hand when Abraham’s servant asked for Rebekah as Isaac’s bride? (Genesis 24:15, 50) 10. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5)',
