        '"ADONIRAMHADORAM","LYSANIAS","ARCHELAUS","ZIMRI","MAAKAH","CANDACE","ADONIJAH","DRUSILLA","JEHOSHEBA","ABNERSONOFNER"'::text[],
        'ADONIRAMHADORAM|LYSANIAS|ARCHELAUS|ZIMRI|MAAKAH|CANDACE|ADONIJAH|DRUSILLA|JEHOSHEBA|ABNERSONOFNER',
        '1. ADONIRAMHADORAM: Which royal supervisor of forced labor was dispatched by King Rehoboam to negotiate with the rebellious northern tribes, only to be stoned to death by all Israel? (1 Kings 12:18) 2. LYSANIAS: Which regional ruler was tetrarch of Abilene during the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, as recorded in Luke''s historical synchronization? (Luke 3:1) 3. ARCHELAUS: Which son of Herod the Great ruled over Judea after Herod''s death, whose cruel reputation caused Joseph to avoid Judea and take Jesus to Galilee? (Matthew 2:22) 4. ZIMRI: Which military commander seized the throne of the northern kingdom of Israel and reigned for only seven days in Tirzah before setting fire to the palace over himself? (1 Kings 16:15-18) 5. MAAKAH: Which queen mother (Gebirah) of Judah was stripped of her royal dignity by King Asa because she had erected an abominable image for Asherah? (1 Kings 15:13) 6. CANDACE: Which royal title and name belonged to the queen of the Ethiopians whose chief court treasurer was baptized by Philip on the desert road? (Acts 8:27) 7. ADONIJAH: Which ambitious son of David by Haggith declared himself king at En-rogel when David was old, backed by General Joab and Priest Abiathar? (1 Kings 1:5-9) 8. DRUSILLA: Which Jewish royal woman, the daughter of Herod Agrippa I and sister of Bernice, was the wife of Roman Governor Felix when Paul spoke to them in Caesarea? (Acts 24:24) 9. JEHOSHEBA: Which royal princess of Judah stole away baby prince Joash when Queen Mother Athaliah was slaughtering all royal heirs, hiding him in the temple? (2 Kings 11:2) 10. ABNERSONOFNER: Who was Saul''s commander-in-chief who crowned Saul''s son Ish-bosheth king at Mahanaim, but was later stabbed to death by Joab at Hebron''s city gate? (2 Samuel 2:8; 2 Samuel 3:27)',
