        '1. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 2. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 3. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 4. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 5. ASYNCRITUS: Believer in Rome greeted by name in Paul''s extensive list of greetings (Romans 16:14) 6. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 7. EUBULUS: Brother in Rome who sent personal greetings to Timothy during Paul''s second Roman imprisonment (2 Timothy 4:21) 8. LINUS: Roman Christian mentioned in 2 Timothy, recognized early in church history as an elder of Rome (2 Timothy 4:21) 9. CLAUDIA: Christian sister in Rome who sent greetings to Timothy alongside Eubulus, Pudens, and Linus (2 Timothy 4:21) 10. CARPUS: Believer in Troas at whose house Paul left his cloak and parchments (2 Timothy 4:13)',
        'Acts 13:1; Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21; Romans 16:15; Romans 16:14; Titus 3:12; 2 Timothy 4:21; 2 Timothy 4:13',
