        '1. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 2. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 3. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 4. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 5. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 6. CLAUDIA: Christian sister in Rome who sent greetings to Timothy alongside Eubulus, Pudens, and Linus (2 Timothy 4:21) 7. CARPUS: Believer in Troas at whose house Paul left his cloak and parchments (2 Timothy 4:13) 8. APPHIA: Christian sister greeted in Philemon alongside Archippus and the church in Philemon''s house (Philemon 1:2) 9. ADONIJAH: Eldest surviving son of David who exalted himself saying "I will be king" before Solomon was crowned (1 Kings 1:5-10) 10. CHIMHAM: Son of Barzillai who accompanied David to Jerusalem in place of his elderly father (2 Samuel 19:37-40)',
