        '1. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21) 2. PHILOLOGUS: Roman Christian greeted together with Julia, Nereus, and Olympas (Romans 16:15) 3. SECUNDUS: Thessalonian Christian who accompanied Paul on his journey carrying the relief collection to Jerusalem (Acts 20:4) 4. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 5. SAPPHIRA: Wife of Ananias who colluded in withholding money and fell dead before Peter (Acts 5:1-10) 6. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 7. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 8. NEBUZARADAN: Captain of the Babylonian royal bodyguard who burned the Temple and broke down Jerusalem''s walls (2 Kings 25:8-11) 9. RABSHAKEH: Assyrian military envoy who shouted blasphemous intimidation in Hebrew on Jerusalem''s wall (2 Kings 18:17-35) 10. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18)',
