        '1. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 2. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 3. JOHNTHEAPOSTLE: Which beloved apostle was banished in elderly exile to the penal island of Patmos on the Lord''s Day, heard a voice like a trumpet, and collapsed as though dead before the blazing glorified Son of Man? (Revelation 1:9-17) 4. PAULSAULOFTARSUS: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Consented to Stephen''s stoning -> Struck blind on the road to Damascus -> Baptized by Ananias -> Lowered through a wall in a basket at Damascus -> Preached on Mars Hill in Athens? (Acts 8:1; Acts 9:1-25; Acts 17:22) 5. SIMONPETER: Which biblical figure experienced these life milestones in chronological order: Called while mending nets at Sea of Galilee -> Confessed Christ at Caesarea Philippi -> Denied the Lord three times by a courtyard fire -> Preached the Pentecost sermon in Jerusalem -> Miraculously delivered from Herod''s prison by an angel? (Matthew 4:18; Matthew 16:16; Matthew 26:69-75; Acts 2:14; Acts 12:6-11) 6. JANNESANDJAMBRES: In 2 Timothy 3:8, which two traditional names does Paul reveal for the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses before Pharaoh, comparing them to corrupt end-times teachers? (2 Timothy 3:8; Exodus 7:11) 7. KORAHSONOFIZHAR: Which Levite rebel led 250 prominent community leaders against Moses and Aaron in Numbers 16, whose fatal rebellion is linked in Jude 11 with the error of Balaam? (Numbers 16:1-35; Jude 1:11) 8. SHIPHRAHANDPUAH: Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own? (Exodus 1:15-21) 9. ITTAITHEGITTITE: Which Philistine military exile from Gath arrived with 600 men and swore unwavering loyalty to King David during Absalom''s rebellion, saying ''In whatever place my lord the king shall be... there will your servant be''? (2 Samuel 15:19-22; 2 Samuel 18:2) 10. MARYMAGDALENE: Which woman came to the tomb while it was still dark, found the stone taken away, mistook the risen Lord for the gardener, and heard Him call her ''Mary''? (John 20:1-16)',
