n is linked in Jude 11 with the error of Balaam?","reference":"Numbers 16:1-35; Jude 1:11","direction":"across"},{"number":8,"answer":"SHIPHRAHANDPUAH","clue":"Which two Hebrew midwives feared God rather than the Egyptian monarch, defied Pharaoh''s royal decree to murder male infants at birth, and were blessed by God with families of their own?","reference":"Exodus 1:15-21","direction":"down"},{"number":9,"answer":"ITTAITHEGITTITE","clue":"Which Philistine military exile from Gath arrived with 600 men and swore unwavering loyalty to King David during Absalom''s rebellion, saying ''In whatever place my lord the king shall be... there will your servant be''?","reference":"2 Samuel 15:19-22; 2 Samuel 18:2","direction":"across"},{"number":10,"answer":"MARYMAGDALENE","clue":"Which woman came to the tomb while it was still dark, found the stone taken away, mistook the risen Lord for the gardener, and heard Him call her ''Mary''?","reference":"John 20:1-16","direction":"down"}],"crosswordVersion":5,"category":"Bible Investigator","stage":8,"stage_title":"Bible Investigator","level_theme":"Who Said It?","difficulty":"Expert","timerSeconds":140,"clueCount":10,"curated":true}'::jsonb
