        'ZAPHENATHPANEAH|ANNA|ANNAS|ABDON|ABNER|AMASA|EHUD|COZBI|CHUZA|AGABUS',
        '1. ZAPHENATHPANEAH: What Egyptian title of honor did Pharaoh bestow upon Joseph when appointing him prime minister over the granaries of Egypt? (Genesis 41:45) 2. ANNA: • I was an elderly prophetess of the tribe of Asher.
• I had lived as a widow for eighty-four years after seven years of marriage.
• I never left the temple courts, fasting and praying, and gave thanks when the infant Messiah arrived.
Who am I? (Luke 2:36-38) 3. ANNAS: Which former high priest, the father-in-law of Caiaphas, had Jesus brought to him first for preliminary interrogation immediately following His arrest in Gethsemane? (John 18:13) 4. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 5. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 6. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 7. EHUD: Left-handed Benjaminite judge who delivered Israel by striking down King Eglon of Moab (Judges 3:15-22) 8. COZBI: Which Midianite woman, daughter of tribal chief Zur, was executed by Phinehas alongside the Simeonite prince Zimri at Peor? (Numbers 25:15-18) 9. CHUZA: Who was the royal household steward/administrator of Herod Antipas whose wife Joanna financed Jesus'' itinerant ministry out of her private wealth? (Luke 8:3) 10. AGABUS: • I was a prophet who came down from Judea to Antioch and Caesarea.
• I predicted by the Holy Spirit a severe famine across the entire Roman empire under Emperor Claudius.
• I tied my own hands and feet with Paul''s belt to foretell his Jerusalem arrest.
Who am I? (Acts 11:27-28; Acts 21:10-11)',
