        '1. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 2. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 3. MEPHIBOSHETH: Lame son of Jonathan welcomed by David to eat at the king''s royal table continually (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 4. ONESIPHORUS: Ephesian Christian who searched diligently for Paul in Rome and refreshed him (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 5. MELCHIZEDEK: King of Salem and priest of God Most High who blessed Abram (Genesis 14:18-20) 6. EBEDMELECH: Cushite royal official who rescued Jeremiah from the muddy cistern with rags (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 7. EPAPHRAS: Faithful minister from Colossae who wrestled intensely in prayer for the saints (Colossians 1:7; 4:12) 8. HULDAH: Prophetess in Jerusalem consulted by King Josiah when the Book of the Law was recovered (2 Kings 22:14-20) 9. TYCHICUS: Dear brother and faithful minister Paul sent with epistles to Ephesus and Colossae (Ephesians 6:21; Colossians 4:7) 10. BEZALEL: Chief craftsman filled with the Spirit of God to construct the Tabernacle furnishings (Exodus 31:1-5)',
