        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 3. LUCIUS: Kinsman of Paul or prophet/teacher from Cyrene mentioned in Antioch and Romans (Acts 13:1; Romans 16:21) 4. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 5. OLYMPAS: Roman disciple greeted alongside Philologus, Julia, and Nereus (Romans 16:15) 6. NEREUS: Believer greeted with his sister and Olympas in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 7. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 8. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 9. PATROBAS: Christian disciple in Rome greeted by Paul in Romans 16:14 (Romans 16:14) 10. PHLEGON: Roman brother greeted alongside Hermes, Patrobas, and Hermas in Romans 16 (Romans 16:14)',
