        'AMASA|ABNER|ABDON|APPHIA|ASAHEL|BARUCH|ELON|ACHSAH|EHUD|ARTEMAS',
        '1. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 2. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 3. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 4. APPHIA: Christian sister greeted in Philemon alongside Archippus and the church in Philemon''s house (Philemon 1:2) 5. ASAHEL: Brother of Joab, as fleet of foot as a gazelle, slain by Abner''s reversed spear (2 Samuel 2:18-23) 6. BARUCH: Faithful scribe who recorded Jeremiah''s prophecies from dictation onto a papyrus scroll (Jeremiah 36:4-10) 7. ELON: Judge from the tribe of Zebulun who led Israel for ten years (Judges 12:11-12) 8. ACHSAH: Daughter of Caleb who asked her father for both upper and lower water springs (Joshua 15:16-19) 9. EHUD: Left-handed Benjaminite judge who delivered Israel by striking down King Eglon of Moab (Judges 3:15-22) 10. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12)',
