        '1. MANAEN: Teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch (Acts 13:1) 2. JASON: Thessalonian host whose house was dragged before magistrates because he welcomed Paul and Silas (Acts 17:5-9; Romans 16:21) 3. OLYMPAS: Roman disciple greeted alongside Philologus, Julia, and Nereus (Romans 16:15) 4. NEREUS: Believer greeted with his sister and Olympas in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 5. JULIA: Christian woman in Rome greeted in Romans 16:15 (Romans 16:15) 6. HERMAS: Brother in the Lord in Rome mentioned in Paul''s greetings to the house churches (Romans 16:14) 7. ASYNCRITUS: Believer in Rome greeted by name in Paul''s extensive list of greetings (Romans 16:14) 8. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 9. PATROBAS: Christian disciple in Rome greeted by Paul in Romans 16:14 (Romans 16:14) 10. PHLEGON: Roman brother greeted alongside Hermes, Patrobas, and Hermas in Romans 16 (Romans 16:14)',
