        'EHUD|ATHALIAH|BARUCH|GEHAZI|HAZAEL|JEHU|BERNICE|CRISPUS|CLEOPAS|CLOPAS',
        '1. EHUD: Left-handed Benjaminite judge who delivered Israel by striking down King Eglon of Moab (Judges 3:15-22) 2. ATHALIAH: Wicked daughter of Ahab and Jezebel who usurped the throne of Judah and destroyed royal heirs (2 Kings 11:1-3) 3. BARUCH: Faithful scribe who recorded Jeremiah''s prophecies from dictation onto a papyrus scroll (Jeremiah 36:4-10) 4. GEHAZI: Greedy servant of Elisha struck with Naaman''s leprosy after running after silver and garments (2 Kings 5:20-27) 5. HAZAEL: Syrian officer who smothered his master King Ben-Hadad with a wet thick cloth and seized the throne (2 Kings 8:7-15) 6. JEHU: Furious chariot-driver anointed king of Israel to execute judgment on the house of Ahab (2 Kings 9:1-24) 7. BERNICE: Sister of King Agrippa II who sat beside him in grand pomp to hear Paul''s defense in Caesarea (Acts 25:13, 23) 8. CRISPUS: Corinthian synagogue ruler who believed in the Lord with his entire household and was baptized by Paul (Acts 18:8; 1 Corinthians 1:14) 9. CLEOPAS: One of the two disciples whose hearts burned as the risen Jesus walked with them to Emmaus (Luke 24:13-32) 10. CLOPAS: Husband of Mary who stood near the cross of Jesus alongside his mother (John 19:25)',
