        '1. ONESIPHORUS: Ephesian Christian who searched diligently for Paul in Rome and refreshed him (2 Timothy 1:16-18) 2. SOSTHENES: Ruler of the Corinthian synagogue beaten before Gallio, later co-sender of 1 Corinthians (Acts 18:17; 1 Corinthians 1:1) 3. ZILPAH: Leah''s handmaid who bore Gad and Asher to Jacob (Genesis 30:9-13) 4. ZERUIAH: David''s sister whose three mighty sons Joab, Abishai, and Asahel served as military commanders (1 Chronicles 2:16; 2 Samuel 2:18) 5. ZADOK: Faithful high priest who anointed Solomon at Gihon spring alongside Nathan the prophet (1 Kings 1:38-39) 6. ZERESH: Wife of Haman who advised building a seventy-five-foot gallows to hang Mordecai (Esther 5:14; 6:13) 7. SANBALLAT: Horonite governor who conspired with Tobiah to mock and oppose the rebuilding of Jerusalem''s walls (Nehemiah 2:19; 4:1-8) 8. TERTULLUS: Professional orator hired by high priest Ananias to present formal charges against Paul before Felix (Acts 24:1-8) 9. ZENAS: Christian lawyer whom Paul instructed Titus to assist diligently on his journey (Titus 3:13) 10. SOSIPATER: Kinsman of Paul who sent warm greetings to the church in Rome (Romans 16:21)',
