        'Harmonize ancient covenants with New Testament apostolates and prophecies.',
        '"DERBE","BEREA","ABDON","AIJALON","ENGEDI","CORBAN","ARTEMAS","CARPUS","APPHIA","BARUCH"'::text[],
        'DERBE|BEREA|ABDON|AIJALON|ENGEDI|CORBAN|ARTEMAS|CARPUS|APPHIA|BARUCH',
        '1. DERBE: Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra (Acts 14:20-21) 2. BEREA: Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings (Acts 17:10-12) 3. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 4. AIJALON: Valley over which Joshua commanded the moon to stand motionless during the fight for Gibeon (Joshua 10:12-13) 5. ENGEDI: Oasis and crag of wild goats by the Dead Sea where David cut off the corner of Saul''s robe in a cave (1 Samuel 24:1-4) 6. CORBAN: Hebrew/Aramaic term meaning a gift devoted to God, rebuked when used to bypass caring for parents (Mark 7:11) 7. ARTEMAS: Co-worker Paul considered sending to Titus in Crete before calling Titus to Nicopolis (Titus 3:12) 8. CARPUS: Believer in Troas at whose house Paul left his cloak and parchments (2 Timothy 4:13) 9. APPHIA: Christian sister greeted in Philemon alongside Archippus and the church in Philemon''s house (Philemon 1:2) 10. BARUCH: Faithful scribe who recorded Jeremiah''s prophecies from dictation onto a papyrus scroll (Jeremiah 36:4-10)',
        'Acts 14:20-21; Acts 17:10-12; Judges 12:13-15; Joshua 10:12-13; 1 Samuel 24:1-4; Mark 7:11; Titus 3:12; 2 Timothy 4:13; Philemon 1:2; Jeremiah 36:4-10',
