        '1. MEPHIBOSHETH: Jonathan’s son whom David showed kindness (2 Samuel 9:1-13) 2. ZEPHANIAH: The prophet whose book begins with a warning about the day of the LORD (Zephaniah 1:1-7) 3. TROPHIMUS: The Ephesian whom Paul left sick at Miletus (2 Timothy 4:20) 4. ZACCHAEUS: The chief tax collector who climbed a tree to see Jesus (Luke 19:1-10) 5. SHEPHERD: The image Jesus used when describing his care for the sheep (John 10:11-14) 6. TABERNACLE: The portable sanctuary Israel built in the wilderness (Exodus 25:8-9) 7. PENTATEUCH: The collective name for the first five books of the Bible (Luke 24:44) 8. ZACHARIAS: The father of John the Baptist, named in Luke’s account (Luke 1:5-13) 9. SAPPHIRA: The wife of Ananias who lied about the proceeds of a sale (Acts 5:1-10) 10. ONESIPHORUS: Ephesian Christian who searched diligently for Paul in Rome and refreshed him (2 Timothy 1:16-18)',
