        '1. EHUD: The left-handed judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3:15-22) 2. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 3. EBEDMELECH: The Ethiopian official who rescued Jeremiah from the cistern (Jeremiah 38:7-13) 4. HULDAH: The prophetess consulted during Josiah’s reign (2 Kings 22:14-20) 5. DOEG: The Edomite who reported David’s visit to Ahimelech (1 Samuel 22:9-19) 6. AGABUS: The prophet who foretold a great famine and Paul’s arrest (Acts 11:27-28; 21:10-11) 7. MATTHIAS: The man chosen to replace Judas among the Twelve (Acts 1:23-26) 8. JAEL: The woman who killed Sisera with a tent peg (Judges 4:17-22) 9. BEZALEL: The craftsman appointed to make articles for the tabernacle (Exodus 31:1-5) 10. ABIGAIL: The wise woman who became David’s wife after Nabal died (1 Samuel 25:23-42)',
