        '1. PATMOS: Aegean island where the Apostle John was exiled for the word of God and received the Revelation (Revelation 1:9) 2. PAPHOS: City on Cyprus where proconsul Sergius Paulus was converted after Elymas was struck blind (Acts 13:6-12) 3. ICONIUM: City in Asia Minor where a great multitude of Jews and Greeks believed despite severe opposition (Acts 14:1-5) 4. LYSTRA: City where Paul healed a crippled man, was hailed as Hermes, and was subsequently stoned and left for dead (Acts 14:8-19) 5. DERBE: Galatian city where Paul and Barnabas preached and made many disciples after fleeing Lystra (Acts 14:20-21) 6. CENCHREAE: Port of Corinth where Paul had his hair cut because of a vow, and home of deaconess Phoebe (Acts 18:18; Romans 16:1) 7. BEREA: Macedonian city whose noble citizens examined the Scriptures daily to verify Paul''s teachings (Acts 17:10-12) 8. LAODICEA: Wealthy city whose lukewarm church was warned that Christ would spit them out of His mouth (Revelation 3:14-17) 9. SARDIS: City whose church had a reputation of being alive but was pronounced dead by Christ (Revelation 3:1-3) 10. MILETUS: Port city where Paul gave his poignant farewell address to the elders of the church of Ephesus (Acts 20:17-38)',
        'Revelation 1:9; Acts 13:6-12; Acts 14:1-5; Acts 14:8-19; Acts 14:20-21; Acts 18:18; Romans 16:1; Acts 17:10-12; Revelation 3:14-17; Revelation 3:1-3; Acts 20:17-38',
