        '1. JEHOIAKIM: The king who cut Jeremiah’s scroll with a knife and burned it (Jeremiah 36:20-26) 2. EBENEZER: Memorial stone set up by Samuel between Mizpah and Shen saying "Thus far the LORD has helped us" (1 Samuel 7:12) 3. RABBONI: Aramaic title meaning "My Great Teacher", spoken joyfully by Mary Magdalene outside the empty tomb (John 20:16) 4. BOANERGES: Aramaic nickname given by Jesus to James and John meaning "Sons of Thunder" (Mark 3:17) 5. AKELDAMA: Aramaic name meaning "Field of Blood", bought with the thirty pieces of silver (Acts 1:19; Matthew 27:8) 6. CORBAN: Hebrew/Aramaic term meaning a gift devoted to God, rebuked when used to bypass caring for parents (Mark 7:11) 7. MAHERSHALAL: Symbolic prophetic name given to Isaiah''s newborn son meaning "Speed the spoil, hasten the booty" (Isaiah 8:1-3) 8. TALITHA: Aramaic word spoken by Jesus meaning "Little girl" before saying "arise" (Mark 5:41) 9. EPHPHATHA: Aramaic command spoken by Jesus meaning "Be opened!" when healing a deaf and mute man (Mark 7:34) 10. MARANATHA: Aramaic prayer meaning "Our Lord, come!" with which Paul closed 1 Corinthians (1 Corinthians 16:22)',
