        'BEZALEL|EHUD|HUR|ELON|ABDON|ABNER|ASAHEL|AMASA|BARUCH|JAEL',
        '1. BEZALEL: Chief craftsman filled with the Spirit of God to construct the Tabernacle furnishings (Exodus 31:1-5) 2. EHUD: Left-handed Benjaminite judge who delivered Israel by striking down King Eglon of Moab (Judges 3:15-22) 3. HUR: Companion of Moses and Aaron who helped hold up Moses'' arms during the battle with Amalek (Exodus 17:10-12) 4. ELON: Judge from the tribe of Zebulun who led Israel for ten years (Judges 12:11-12) 5. ABDON: Judge of Pirathon who had forty sons and thirty grandsons who rode on seventy donkeys (Judges 12:13-15) 6. ABNER: Commander of Saul''s army who made Ishbosheth king before defecting to David (2 Samuel 2:8; 3:12) 7. ASAHEL: Brother of Joab, as fleet of foot as a gazelle, slain by Abner''s reversed spear (2 Samuel 2:18-23) 8. AMASA: Absalom''s army commander whom Joab deceitfully kissed and stabbed at the great rock of Gibeon (2 Samuel 20:9-10) 9. BARUCH: Faithful scribe who recorded Jeremiah''s prophecies from dictation onto a papyrus scroll (Jeremiah 36:4-10) 10. JAEL: Wife of Heber the Kenite who drove a tent peg into Sisera while he slept (Judges 4:17-22)',
