        'bible-puzzles',
        4,
        1,
        'SPOT THE BIBLICAL MISTAKE:
"David ran toward Goliath, drew his sharp sword from his sheath, and struck the giant down with a fatal sword stroke to the heart."',
        '"David struck Goliath with a sling and a stone; he only drew Goliath's own sword afterward to behead him","David used Jonathan's royal bronze sword, not his own sheath","David never touched a sword; Goliath died entirely from the impact of the stone","David shot Goliath from a distance with five smooth arrows from his bow"'::text[],
        'David struck Goliath with a sling and a stone; he only drew Goliath''s own sword afterward to behead him',
        '1 Samuel 17:50 explicitly notes: "there was no sword in the hand of David." David struck the giant with a sling and a stone, and only after Goliath fell did David draw Goliath''s own sword from its sheath to slay him and cut off his head.',
        '1 Samuel 17:49–51',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Read 1 Samuel 17:49–51 carefully.","Examine how David actually struck Goliath in the forehead.","Note when David actually drew a sword."],"hint":"Look closely at the weapon in David''s hand when Goliath fell to the earth.","stage":1,"category":"Puzzle Foundations","level_theme":"Spot the Mistake","difficulty":"Accessible","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
