        '"Pashur","Ebed-Melech","Gedaliah","Baruch"'::text[],
        'Ebed-Melech',
        'Ebed-Melech the Ethiopian eunuch boldly appealed to King Zedekiah and used ropes with soft rags under Jeremiah''s armpits to draw him up out of the muddy cistern. God promised to preserve his life because he trusted in Him.',
        'Jeremiah 38:7–13; 39:15–18',
