        11,
        1,
        'STORY SEQUENCE:
Reconstruct the exact chronological order of Naaman''s healing in 2 Kings 5:
1. Elisha sends a messenger saying wash in Jordan seven times.
2. Naaman becomes wroth and turns away in a rage.
3. Naaman''s servants urge him: "If the prophet had bid thee do some great thing..."
4. Naaman dips seven times in Jordan and his flesh becomes clean like a little child.',
        '"Servants urge obedience → Elisha sends messenger → Naaman dips and is healed → Naaman becomes angry","Naaman dips in Jordan → Naaman becomes angry → Elisha sends messenger → Servants urge obedience","Naaman becomes angry → Servants urge obedience → Naaman dips and is healed → Elisha sends messenger","Elisha sends messenger → Naaman becomes angry → Servants urge obedience → Naaman dips and is healed"'::text[],
        'Elisha sends messenger → Naaman becomes angry → Servants urge obedience → Naaman dips and is healed',
        '2 Kings 5:10–14: Elisha sent a messenger telling him to wash seven times; Naaman was wroth and turned away; his servants reasoned with him; he went down and dipped seven times and his flesh was restored.',
        '2 Kings 5:10–14',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Story Sequence Puzzle","clues":["Notice that Elisha did not even come out to greet Naaman in person.","Naaman was furious because he expected a grand waving of the hand over the leprosy.","His wise servants persuaded him to obey the simple command."],"hint":"The messenger came first, anger followed, servants counseled, and dipping brought healing.","stage":3,"category":"Stories and Events","level_theme":"Story Sequence Puzzles","difficulty":"Moderate","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
