        'STORY SEQUENCE:
Reconstruct the sequence of Peter''s miraculous escape from Herod''s prison in Acts 12:
1. An angel shines in prison, strikes Peter''s side, and chains fall off.
2. Peter passes two guards and the iron city gate opens of its own accord.
3. Peter knocks at Mary''s gate and maid Rhoda forgets to open in joy.
4. Peter enters, declares how the Lord brought him out, and departs.',
        '"Angel wakes Peter and chains fall → Iron gate opens → Rhoda hears knock at gate → Peter testifies to believers","Peter testifies to believers → Angel wakes Peter → Iron gate opens → Rhoda hears knock at gate","Rhoda hears knock at gate → Angel wakes Peter → Peter testifies to believers → Iron gate opens","Iron gate opens → Rhoda hears knock at gate → Angel wakes Peter → Peter testifies to believers"'::text[],
        'Angel wakes Peter and chains fall → Iron gate opens → Rhoda hears knock at gate → Peter testifies to believers',
        'Acts 12:7–17 records the angelic awakening and falling chains, passing through the iron gate, knocking at Mary''s door with Rhoda''s glad reaction, and Peter''s testimony to the astonished prayer meeting.',
        'Acts 12:7–17',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Story Sequence Puzzle","clues":["Peter thought he saw a vision while following the angel through the gates.","He only came to himself when left alone in the street.","He then walked to the house of Mary where disciples were praying."],"hint":"Chains fall first in prison, gate opens to the city, knocking at Mary''s house follows.","stage":3,"category":"Stories and Events","level_theme":"Story Sequence Puzzles","difficulty":"Moderate","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
