        '"Washed and came seeing → Made clay with spittle → Anointed eyes with clay → Bidden to wash in Siloam","Anointed eyes with clay → Made clay with spittle → Washed and came seeing → Bidden to wash in Siloam","Made clay with spittle → Anointed eyes with clay → Bidden to wash in Siloam → Washed and came seeing","Bidden to wash in Siloam → Washed and came seeing → Made clay with spittle → Anointed eyes with clay"'::text[],
        'Made clay with spittle → Anointed eyes with clay → Bidden to wash in Siloam → Washed and came seeing',
        'John 9:6–7: "he spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and he anointed the eyes of the blind man with the clay, And said unto him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam... He went his way therefore, and washed, and came seeing."',
        'John 9:6–7',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Story Sequence Puzzle","clues":["The disciples originally asked who sinned: this man or his parents.","Jesus declared it was that the works of God should be made manifest.","Siloam is translated \"Sent.\""],"hint":"Spittle made clay, eyes were anointed, Siloam washing completed the miracle.","stage":3,"category":"Stories and Events","level_theme":"Story Sequence Puzzles","difficulty":"Moderate","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
