        '"Rizpah","Maacah","Ahinoam","Abital"'::text[],
        'Rizpah',
        'Rizpah the daughter of Aiah took sackcloth and spread it on the rock for herself from the beginning of harvest until rain fell from the heavens on them. She kept birds of the air from landing on them by day and beasts of the field by night until David brought their bones for honorable burial.',
        '2 Samuel 21:8–14',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["She was the daughter of Aiah and a concubine of Saul.","Her two sons, Armoni and Mephibosheth (not Jonathan''s son), were given to the Gibeonites to be hanged.","From the beginning of harvest until rain fell, she did not allow birds by day nor beasts of the field by night to touch them."],"hint":"Her name is Rizpah, celebrated for guarding the bodies at Gibeah.","stage":4,"category":"The Missing Details","level_theme":"Silent Witnesses","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
