        'King Nebuchadnezzar displayed the Ark of the Covenant inside Marduk''s temple in Babylon along with Belshazzar''s goblets',
        'The Ark of the Covenant is never mentioned among the captured temple vessels taken to Babylon in 2 Kings 25 or Jeremiah 52 (which detail the bronze pillars, basins, and golden utensils). Scripture never states Nebuchadnezzar displayed the Ark in Marduk''s temple.',
        '2 Kings 25:13–17; Jeremiah 52:17–23; 2 Samuel 6:6–7',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["The Ark was built of acacia wood overlaid inside and out with pure gold.","It was captured by the Philistines at the battle of Aphek and placed in Dagon''s temple.","Examine its fate during the Babylonian exile under King Nebuchadnezzar."],"hint":"The Ark disappears from Old Testament historical narrative before the Babylonian looting inventory.","stage":4,"category":"The Missing Details","level_theme":"Missing Details Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
