(
        'bible-puzzles-l26-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        26,
        1,
        'BIBLE LOGIC GRID:
Three major biblical covenants were ratified with three distinct physical signs: a rainbow in the clouds, circumcision in the flesh, and the Sabbath day. Deduce which covenant mediator matches which sign:
1. Noah
2. Abraham
3. Moses',
        '"Noah: Sabbath; Abraham: Rainbow; Moses: Circumcision","Noah: Rainbow; Abraham: Circumcision; Moses: Sabbath","Noah: Rainbow; Abraham: Sabbath; Moses: Circumcision","Noah: Circumcision; Abraham: Sabbath; Moses: Rainbow"'::text[],
        'Noah: Rainbow; Abraham: Circumcision; Moses: Sabbath',
        'Noah received the rainbow as the token of the universal covenant (Genesis 9). Abraham received circumcision as the sign of the seed covenant (Genesis 17). Moses received the Sabbath as the perpetual covenant sign between God and Israel (Exodus 31).',
        'Genesis 9:12–17; Genesis 17:10–14; Exodus 31:13–17',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Noah was given a celestial sign never to destroy the earth with a flood again.","Abraham was given a generational token in the flesh of every eight-day-old male.","Moses was commanded that the covenant sign of perpetual rest be observed across generations."],"hint":"Noah = sky sign; Abraham = male flesh token; Moses = weekly holy day.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Grid Deductions","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
