- Fathered sons whose prophetic names were Shear-jashub ("A remnant shall return") and Maher-shalal-hash-baz ("Hurry to the spoil").',
        '"Hosea: Forbidden to mourn wife; Isaiah: Married Gomer; Ezekiel: Sons' prophetic names","Hosea: Prophetic names for sons; Isaiah: Forbidden to mourn wife; Ezekiel: Married Gomer","Hosea: Married Gomer; Isaiah: Prophetic names for sons; Ezekiel: Forbidden to mourn wife's death","Hosea: Married Gomer; Isaiah: Forbidden to mourn wife; Ezekiel: Prophetic names for sons"'::text[],
        'Hosea: Married Gomer; Isaiah: Prophetic names for sons; Ezekiel: Forbidden to mourn wife''s death',
        'Hosea was commanded to marry Gomer (Hosea 1). Isaiah''s sons were signs in Israel (Isaiah 8:18). Ezekiel''s wife died suddenly in Babylon and he was told not to mourn as a sign to the exiles (Ezekiel 24:16–18).',
        'Hosea 1:2–3; Isaiah 8:1–4, 18; Ezekiel 24:15–24',
