        '"Rahab: Teraphim in bed; Michal: Flax & rope; Wise woman: Sheba's head to Joab","Rahab: Flax & scarlet rope; Michal: Teraphim in bed; Wise woman: Sheba's head to Joab","Rahab: Bread in oven; Michal: Window basket; Wise woman: Flax on roof","Rahab: Flax & scarlet rope; Michal: Sheba's head; Wise woman: Teraphim in bed"'::text[],
        'Rahab: Flax & scarlet rope; Michal: Teraphim in bed; Wise woman: Sheba''s head to Joab',
        'Rahab hid the spies under flax (Joshua 2). Michal helped David escape by placing teraphim in his bed (1 Samuel 19). The wise woman of Abel negotiated peace by tossing rebel Sheba''s head to Joab (2 Samuel 20).',
