        'CONDITIONAL SEQUENCES:
When King David committed adultery with Bathsheba, he attempted multiple sequential maneuvers to conceal his crime. What did David do FIRST before ordering Joab to have Uriah the Hittite killed in the front lines of battle?',
        '"David sent Uriah with a secret sealed death warrant directly to Joab","David recalled Uriah home and tried to get him to sleep with his wife","David confessed his sin immediately to Nathan the prophet","David commanded Bathsheba to flee to her father Eliam's estate"'::text[],
        'David recalled Uriah home and tried to get him to sleep with his wife',
        'David first recalled Uriah from the battlefield and tried repeatedly (even getting him drunk) to make him go home to Bathsheba to cover the pregnancy. Only when Uriah stubbornly slept at the palace door did David orchestrate his murder.',
        '2 Samuel 11:6–13',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Story Puzzle","clues":["David sent for Uriah from the siege of Rabbah.","David urged Uriah to go down to his house and wash his feet, sending a royal banquet portion after him.","Uriah refused to sleep in his house while the Ark and his fellow soldiers slept in open tents."],"hint":"David tried to make Uriah sleep at home so the child would appear to be Uriah''s.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Conditional Sequences","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l28-c4',
        'bible-puzzles',
        28,
        4,
        'CONDITIONAL SEQUENCES:
During King Solomon''s accession to the throne, his elder half-brother Adonijah made an initial grab for power. What specific action caused Solomon to ultimately execute Adonijah, ending his conditional clemency?',
        '"Adonijah formed an army with Joab to storm Jerusalem","Adonijah stole the royal crown of David from the palace","Adonijah requested David's concubine Abishag the Shunammite to be his wife","Adonijah sacrificed oxen at the high place of Gibeon without Solomon's consent"'::text[],
        'Adonijah requested David''s concubine Abishag the Shunammite to be his wife',
        'Adonijah asked Bathsheba to request Abishag the Shunammite as his wife. Solomon recognized this as a subtle claim on David''s royal rights (as claiming a king''s concubine was equivalent to claiming the throne) and ordered Benaiah to strike him down.',
        '1 Kings 2:13–25',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Story Puzzle","clues":["Solomon had previously told Adonijah: \"If he shows himself a worthy man, not one of his hairs shall fall to the earth.\"","Adonijah approached the queen mother Bathsheba with a dangerous request.","He asked for Abishag the Shunammite, King David''s attendant concubine, to be given to him as his wife."],"hint":"Asking for the former king''s maiden concubine Abishag signaled royal ambition.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Conditional Sequences","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l28-c5',
        'bible-puzzles',
        28,
        5,
        'CONDITIONAL SEQUENCES:
In the book of Acts, what crucial event happened immediately BEFORE the Jerusalem Council in Acts 15 met to debate whether Gentile believers had to be circumcised?',
        '"Peter had his vision of the unclean sheet of animals at Joppa","Judaizers came from Judea to Antioch demanding that Gentiles be circumcised","James the brother of John was executed with the sword by Herod Agrippa","Paul was stoned and dragged outside the gates of Lystra"'::text[],
        'Judaizers came from Judea to Antioch demanding that Gentiles be circumcised',
        'Acts 15:1–2 records that men came down from Judea to Antioch teaching that circumcision was necessary for salvation, sparking intense controversy that caused Paul and Barnabas to be sent to Jerusalem for the Council.',
        'Acts 15:1–2',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Story Puzzle","clues":["Paul and Barnabas had returned to Syrian Antioch and gathered the church to report all that God had done.","Certain men came down from Judea to Antioch teaching: \"Unless you are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you cannot be saved.\"","This ignited sharp dissension and debate in Antioch, leading the church to appoint Paul and Barnabas to go up to the apostles in Jerusalem."],"hint":"The arrival of strict legalists from Judea stirring controversy in Antioch.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Conditional Sequences","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l29-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        29,
        1,
        'LINEAGE LOGIC:
Zeruiah was King David''s sister. Her three famous warrior sons served in David''s military leadership. Who were the three sons of Zeruiah?',
        '"Joab, Abishai, and Asahel","Elhanan, Uriah, and Ittai","Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchi-shua","Benaiah, Eleazar, and Shammah"'::text[],
        'Joab, Abishai, and Asahel',
        '1 Chronicles 2:16 records David''s sisters Zeruiah and Abigail. The three sons of Zeruiah were Joab (the army commander), Abishai (the bold mighty man), and Asahel (swift runner slain by Abner).',
        '2 Samuel 2:18; 1 Chronicles 2:16',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["One was commander-in-chief of David''s army.","One was a fierce warrior who accompanied David into Saul''s camp by night and wanted to pin Saul with his spear.","One was as fleet of foot as a wild gazelle, but was killed by Abner with the butt of his spear at the pool of Gibeon."],"hint":"Joab and his two brothers; David''s nephews.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Lineage Logic","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l29-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        29,
        2,
        'LINEAGE LOGIC:
Timothy, the young pastoral protégé of the apostle Paul, was nurtured in sincere Christian faith by two women in his family. What were the names of Timothy''s grandmother and mother recorded by Paul in 2 Timothy 1:5?',
        '"Grandmother: Eunice; Mother: Lois","Grandmother: Lois; Mother: Eunice","Grandmother: Salome; Mother: Joanna","Grandmother: Martha; Mother: Mary"'::text[],
        'Grandmother: Lois; Mother: Eunice',
        '2 Timothy 1:5 states: "I am reminded of your sincere faith, a faith that dwelt first in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice and now, I am sure, dwells in you as well."',
        '2 Timothy 1:5; 3:15; Acts 16:1',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Paul remembered their unfeigned faith that first dwelt in his grandmother, then in his mother, and now in Timothy.","His mother was a Jewish believer, while his father was a Greek.","They taught Timothy the sacred Scriptures from infancy."],"hint":"Lois was the grandmother; Eunice was the mother.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Lineage Logic","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l29-c3',
        'bible-puzzles',
        29,
        3,
        'LINEAGE LOGIC:
Examine the genealogical relationship between King Saul and Abner, the commander-in-chief of Israel''s army:
- Saul was the son of Kish.
- Abner was the son of Ner.
- Kish and Ner were brothers, sons of Abiel.
What was the exact biological relationship between King Saul and General Abner?',
        '"Father and son","Uncle and nephew","First cousins","Brothers"'::text[],
        'First cousins',
        '1 Samuel 14:50–51 explains: "The name of the commander of his army was Abner the son of Ner, Saul''s uncle. Kish was the father of Saul, and Ner the father of Abner was the son of Abiel." Thus, Saul and Abner were first cousins.',
        '1 Samuel 14:50–51',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Their fathers (Kish and Ner) were full brothers.","Saul and Abner belonged to the same generation of the Benjaminite clan.","Abner was Saul''s cousin (or uncle''s son)."],"hint":"Their fathers were brothers, making Saul and Abner first cousins.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Lineage Logic","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l29-c4',
        'bible-puzzles',
        29,
        4,
        'LINEAGE LOGIC:
In the royal genealogy of the kingdom of Judah, Athaliah seized the throne of Jerusalem and slaughtered all royal heirs except baby Joash. Who was Athaliah''s father and who was her mother?',
        '"Father: King Baasha; Mother: Tirzah","Father: King Omri; Mother: Athaliah the elder","Father: King Ahab; Mother: Jezebel","Father: King Jeroboam; Mother: Zeruah"'::text[],
        'Father: King Ahab; Mother: Jezebel',
        'Athaliah was the daughter of King Ahab of Israel and Jezebel (called the granddaughter of Omri). She married Jehoram of Judah and brought the horrific corruptions of the house of Ahab to Jerusalem.',
        '2 Kings 8:18, 26; 2 Chronicles 22:2',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Her father was the notoriously wicked king of Israel who married a Sidonian princess.","Her mother introduced state-sponsored Baal and Asherah worship and killed God''s prophets.","Athaliah brought the murderous idolatry of the house of Omri into Judah through her marriage to King Jehoram."],"hint":"The infamous northern royal couple Ahab and Jezebel.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Lineage Logic","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l29-c5',
        'bible-puzzles',
        29,
        5,
        'LINEAGE LOGIC:
Aaron, the first high priest of Israel, had four sons consecrated to the priesthood. Two were struck dead before the Lord for offering unauthorized fire. What were the names of Aaron''s four sons, and which two survived to carry on the high priestly line?',
        '"All four: Hophni, Phinehas, Eleazar, Ithamar; Survivors: Hophni and Phinehas","All four: Nadab, Abihu, Phinehas, Zadok; Survivors: Phinehas and Zadok","All four: Gershon, Kohath, Merari, Eleazar; Survivors: Gershon and Kohath","All four: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, Ithamar; Survivors: Eleazar and Ithamar"'::text[],
        'All four: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, Ithamar; Survivors: Eleazar and Ithamar',
        'Aaron''s four sons were Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar. Nadab and Abihu died when they offered profane fire (Leviticus 10). Eleazar and Ithamar survived and served as priests under Aaron.',
        'Leviticus 10:1–2; Numbers 3:1–4; Exodus 6:23',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Nadab and Abihu died when fire came out from the Lord at the tabernacle.","The remaining two younger sons preserved the priestly lineage throughout Israel''s history."],"hint":"Eleazar and Ithamar were the two surviving sons.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Lineage Logic","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l30-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        30,
        1,
        'LOGIC CHAMBER BOSS:
MASTER LOGIC PUZZLE:
Three prominent kings of Israel and Judah experienced dramatic falls from grace involving disease, warfare, or madness. Deduce the correct match:
1. King Uzziah (Azariah) of Judah
2. King Asa of Judah
3. King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon',
        '"Uzziah: Grazed grass like an ox; Asa: Leprosy in temple; Nebuchadnezzar: Diseased in feet","Uzziah: Diseased in feet; Asa: Leprosy in temple; Nebuchadnezzar: Grazed grass like an ox","Uzziah: Leprosy in temple; Asa: Grazed grass like an ox; Nebuchadnezzar: Diseased in feet","Uzziah: Leprosy in temple; Asa: Diseased in feet; Nebuchadnezzar: Grazed grass like an ox"'::text[],
        'Uzziah: Leprosy in temple; Asa: Diseased in feet; Nebuchadnezzar: Grazed grass like an ox',
        'Uzziah was struck with leprosy when trying to burn incense (2 Chron 26). Asa suffered severe foot disease and sought only doctors (2 Chron 16:12). Nebuchadnezzar suffered divine madness eating grass (Daniel 4).',
        '2 Chronicles 26:16–21; 2 Chronicles 16:12; Daniel 4:28–33',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["One sought not the Lord but only physicians when severely diseased in his feet in his old age.","One became arrogant, entered the temple sanctuary to burn incense, and was struck on the forehead with leprosy.","One walked on the palace roof boasting of his majesty, lost his sanity, ate grass like an ox, and his hair grew like eagles'' feathers."],"hint":"Uzziah = forehead leprosy; Asa = foot disease; Nebuchadnezzar = lycanthropic madness.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Chamber Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l30-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        30,
        2,
        'LOGIC CHAMBER BOSS:
Three men in the New Testament bore the name James. Deduce which James matches which historical identity:
1. James the son of Zebedee
2. James the son of Alphaeus
3. James the brother of the Lord',
        '"Son of Zebedee: Jerusalem leader; Son of Alphaeus: Martyred by Herod; Brother of Lord: One of the 12","Son of Zebedee: One of the 12; Son of Alphaeus: Jerusalem leader; Brother of Lord: Martyred by Herod","Son of Zebedee: Inner circle martyred by Herod; Son of Alphaeus: One of the 12 (James the Less); Brother of Lord: Jerusalem church leader","Son of Zebedee: Author of epistle; Son of Alphaeus: Inner circle; Brother of Lord: Son of Zebedee"'::text[],
        'Son of Zebedee: Inner circle martyred by Herod; Son of Alphaeus: One of the 12 (James the Less); Brother of Lord: Jerusalem church leader',
        'James son of Zebedee was executed in Acts 12. James son of Alphaeus was one of the Twelve. James the Lord''s brother presided at the Jerusalem Council in Acts 15 and wrote the Epistle.',
        'Matthew 10:2–3; Acts 12:1–2; Acts 15:13; Galatians 1:19',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["One was brother of John, member of Jesus'' inner circle, and was executed with the sword by King Herod Agrippa I.","One was one of the Twelve apostles called \"James the Less\".","One was leader of the Jerusalem church, author of the Epistle of James, and had a resurrection appearance from Jesus."],"hint":"Zebedee''s son died first in Acts 12; the Lord''s brother led the Jerusalem church.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Chamber Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l30-c3',
        'bible-puzzles',
        30,
        3,
        'LOGIC CHAMBER BOSS:
Examine these four claims regarding the Ark of the Covenant''s journey after being captured by the Philistines. Which ONE claim contains an inaccurate biblical error?',
        '"The Ark was brought to Kiriath-jearim to the house of Abinadab on the hill, where Eleazar was consecrated to guard it","The Ark remained at the city of Jericho inside Rahab's house for twenty years","The Philistines sent a guilt offering of five golden tumors and five golden mice corresponding to their five lords","The men of Beth-shemesh were struck down because they looked inside the Ark of the Lord"'::text[],
        'The Ark remained at the city of Jericho inside Rahab''s house for twenty years',
        '1 Samuel 7:1–2 explicitly states the Ark stayed at Kiriath-jearim in the house of Abinadab for twenty years until David retrieved it. It was never kept in Rahab''s house in Jericho.',
        '1 Samuel 5:1–6:21; 7:1–2',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["The Philistines took the Ark from Ebenezer to Ashdod.","The idol Dagon fell face down and had its head and hands snapped off.","The Philistines returned the Ark on a new cart drawn by two milk cows with five golden tumors and five golden mice.","Examine where the Ark was kept for decades before David brought it to Jerusalem."],"hint":"The Ark was lodged at Kiriath-jearim, never in Jericho.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Chamber Boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l30-c4',
        'bible-puzzles',
        30,
        4,
        'LOGIC CHAMBER BOSS:
Which of the following events is an IMPOSSIBLE HISTORICAL ERROR regarding the ministry of the apostle Paul?',
        '"Paul was consenting to the death of Stephen when the witnesses laid their coats at his feet","Paul was present as an eyewitness disciple at the feeding of the five thousand in Galilee","Paul was let down over the city wall of Damascus in a basket through an opening in the wall","Paul was bitten by a viper on the island of Malta and suffered no harm"'::text[],
        'Paul was present as an eyewitness disciple at the feeding of the five thousand in Galilee',
        'Paul was not a disciple during Jesus'' earthly Galilean ministry; he first appears in Acts 7–8 persecuting the church. He was not present at the feeding of the 5,000.',
        'Galatians 1:13–17; Acts 7:58; Acts 9:25; Acts 28:3–5',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["Paul was born in Tarsus of Cilicia, a Roman citizen.","He was educated in Jerusalem at the feet of Gamaliel.","Examine his presence at early gospel events."],"hint":"Paul never followed Jesus during His earthly Galilean ministry before the crucifixion.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Chamber Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l30-c5',
        'bible-puzzles',
        30,
        5,
        'LOGIC CHAMBER BOSS:
ODD ONE OUT:
Which of these four men was NOT one of David''s famous "Three Mighty Men" (the elite top tier of heroes described in 2 Samuel 23)?',
        '"Josheb-basshebeth (Adino)","Abishai","Shammah son of Agee","Eleazar son of Dodo"'::text[],
        'Abishai',
        'The supreme "Three" were Josheb-basshebeth, Eleazar son of Dodo, and Shammah son of Agee (2 Samuel 23:8–12). Abishai was commander of "The Thirty" and most renowned of them, but 2 Samuel 23:19 explicitly states: "He did not attain to the Three."',
        '2 Samuel 23:8–19',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Odd One Out","clues":["Three formed the supreme trio of David''s warriors who broke through the Philistine camp to fetch David water from the well of Bethlehem.","One was Josheb-basshebeth the Tahchemonite (who killed 800 with his spear).","One was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite (who fought until his hand froze to his sword).","One was Shammah son of Agee the Hararite (who defended the field of lentils)."],"hint":"Scripture specifically notes that Abishai was chief of the Thirty, but did not attain to the elite Three.","stage":6,"category":"The Logic Chamber","level_theme":"Logic Chamber Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      )
