(
        'bible-puzzles-l31-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        31,
        1,
        'SPOT THE HISTORICAL TRAP:
Many popular traditions add non-biblical folklore to Genesis 3. According to the actual text of Genesis 3:6, what kind of fruit did Eve and Adam eat?',
        '"The text simply says \"the fruit of the tree\" without naming an apple or specific fruit","A fresh fig plucked from the surrounding grove","An apple from the garden orchard","A golden pomegranate of Eden"'::text[],
        'The text simply says "the fruit of the tree" without naming an apple or specific fruit',
        'Genesis 3:6 describes it simply as "the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil." The popular notion of an "apple" arose centuries later from Latin wordplay (malum = evil / apple), but is never named in Scripture.',
        'Genesis 3:1–6',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["The woman saw that the tree was good for food, a delight to the eyes, and desired to make one wise.","She took of its fruit and ate, and gave some to her husband.","Does the biblical text ever specify an apple, fig, or pomegranate?"],"hint":"Scripture leaves the botanical identity of the fruit completely unspecified.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Spot the Historical Trap","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l31-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        31,
        2,
        'SPOT THE HISTORICAL TRAP:
According to the exact biblical account in Judges 16, who actually shaved off the seven locks of Samson''s hair while he slept?',
        '"Samson shaved his own head in a delirious sleep","Delilah called a man to shave off the seven locks","A Philistine lord crept into the room with shears","Delilah herself took a razor and shaved his head"'::text[],
        'Delilah called a man to shave off the seven locks',
        'Judges 16:19 states: "She made him sleep on her knees. And she called a man and had him shave off the seven locks of his head." Delilah did not hold the razor herself; she summoned a man to do it.',
        'Judges 16:19',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Samson fell asleep on Delilah''s lap.","Delilah called for someone else to perform the physical shaving.","Identify the real actor who removed Samson''s hair."],"hint":"Delilah summoned a specialist into the room to cut the hair.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Spot the Historical Trap","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l31-c3',
        'bible-puzzles',
        31,
        3,
        'SPOT THE HISTORICAL TRAP:
Regarding the arrival of the Magi (wise men) in Matthew 2, which detail is an inaccurate popular tradition rather than what Matthew actually writes?',
        '"The Magi were warned in a dream not to return to Herod and left by another route","King Herod secretly summoned the Magi to ascertain the exact time the star appeared","The Magi arrived at a house where the child was, not at the manger","Matthew specifies that exactly three crowned kings named Gaspar, Melchior, and Balthasar visited"'::text[],
        'Matthew specifies that exactly three crowned kings named Gaspar, Melchior, and Balthasar visited',
        'Matthew never states there were "three kings" nor provides names like Gaspar, Melchior, and Balthasar. He only mentions three gifts (gold, frankincense, and myrrh). The Magi visited a house, not a stable.',
        'Matthew 2:1–12',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["They came from the east following His star.","They presented three gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.","Examine the number and title commonly assigned to them."],"hint":"Scripture mentions three gifts, but never specifies the number, titles, or names of the Magi.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Spot the Historical Trap","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l31-c4',
        'bible-puzzles',
        31,
        4,
        'SPOT THE HISTORICAL TRAP:
In Jonah 1:17, what creature did the Lord appoint to swallow Jonah when he was cast into the raging Mediterranean Sea?',
        '"A blue whale","A great fish (sea creature)","A prehistoric leviathan serpent","A giant sperm whale"'::text[],
        'A great fish (sea creature)',
        'Jonah 1:17 states: "And the Lord appointed a great fish to swallow up Jonah." It does not specify a biological "whale", but a specially prepared great aquatic creature.',
        'Jonah 1:17; Matthew 12:40',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["The Hebrew text uses ''dag gadol''.","Jesus refers to it in Matthew 12:40 as ''ketos'' (a great sea monster or large sea creature).","Popular nursery rhymes often use an anachronistic mammal name."],"hint":"Scripture specifically designates a \"great fish\" appointed by God.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Spot the Historical Trap","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l31-c5',
        'bible-puzzles',
        31,
        5,
        'SPOT THE HISTORICAL TRAP:
At Noah''s Ark, popular storybooks often claim animals went in strictly "two by two" across the board. What was God''s actual command regarding CLEAN animals in Genesis 7:2?',
        '"Only two of every animal, clean and unclean alike","Seven pairs (or seven individuals) of every clean animal","Twelve of every clean animal representing the tribes","Four pairs of every domestic beast"'::text[],
        'Seven pairs (or seven individuals) of every clean animal',
        'Genesis 7:2 commands: "Take with you seven pairs of all clean animals, the male and his mate, and a pair of the animals that are not clean." This provided for the burnt offering Noah offered in Genesis 8:20.',
        'Genesis 7:2–3; 8:20',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Unclean animals entered as a single pair (two by two, male and female).","Clean animals and birds were taken in larger quantities for food and post-flood sacrifices.","How many of each clean animal was Noah commanded to take?"],"hint":"Clean animals were taken by sevens, not merely by twos.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Spot the Historical Trap","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l32-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        32,
        1,
        'NAME CONFUSION TRAPS:
Three distinct women in the Gospels were named Mary. Match each Mary to her distinct biblical description:
1. Mary of Bethany
2. Mary Magdalene
3. Mary the mother of James and Joseph',
        '"Mary of Bethany: 7 demons cast out; Mary Magdalene: Sat at feet; Mother of James: Stood by cross","Mary of Bethany: Sat at Jesus' feet & anointed Him; Mary Magdalene: 7 demons cast out & garden tomb; Mother of James: Stood by cross","Mary of Bethany: Sister of Martha at cross; Mary Magdalene: Mother of James; Mother of James: Garden tomb","Mary of Bethany: Stood by cross; Mary Magdalene: 7 demons; Mother of James: Anointed Jesus"'::text[],
        'Mary of Bethany: Sat at Jesus'' feet & anointed Him; Mary Magdalene: 7 demons cast out & garden tomb; Mother of James: Stood by cross',
        'Mary of Bethany was Lazarus and Martha''s sister who anointed Jesus (John 11–12). Mary Magdalene was cleansed of 7 demons and met the risen Christ (Luke 8:2, John 20). Mary the mother of James the younger and Joses stood by the cross (Mark 15:40).',
        'Luke 8:2; John 11:1–2; 12:3; 20:11–18; Matthew 27:56',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["One was delivered from seven demons and was the first to see the risen Lord at the garden tomb.","One sat at Jesus'' feet listening to His teaching and anointed His feet with pure nard, wiping them with her hair.","One stood near the cross and witnessed where Jesus'' body was laid."],"hint":"Bethany Mary sat at His feet; Magdalene had seven demons cast out.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Name Confusion Traps","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l32-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        32,
        2,
        'NAME CONFUSION TRAPS:
Two prominent figures named Saul appear in Scripture: King Saul of the Old Testament and Saul of Tarsus (the Apostle Paul) in the New Testament. What common tribal heritage did BOTH Sauls share?',
        '"Tribe of Benjamin","Tribe of Ephraim","Tribe of Levi","Tribe of Judah"'::text[],
        'Tribe of Benjamin',
        'Both King Saul (son of Kish) and Saul of Tarsus were from the tribe of Benjamin. Paul explicitly writes: "circumcised on the eighth day, of the people of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin" (Philippians 3:5).',
        '1 Samuel 9:1–2; Philippians 3:5; Romans 11:1',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["King Saul was the first anointed monarch of Israel.","Saul of Tarsus described his pedigree in Philippians 3:5 and Romans 11:1.","Which of the twelve tribes of Israel did both men descend from?"],"hint":"The smallest yet fierce tribe that gave Israel its first king.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Name Confusion Traps","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
