Match each to his distinct scriptural record:',
        '"John the Baptist: Wilderness preacher; John the Apostle: Cousin of Barnabas; John Mark: Son of Zebedee","John the Baptist: Wilderness preacher; John the Apostle: Son of Zebedee; John Mark: Cousin of Barnabas & Gospel author","John the Baptist: Cousin of Barnabas; John the Apostle: Wilderness preacher; John Mark: Son of Zebedee","John the Baptist: Son of Zebedee; John the Apostle: Gospel of Mark author; John Mark: Wilderness preacher"'::text[],
        'John the Baptist: Wilderness preacher; John the Apostle: Son of Zebedee; John Mark: Cousin of Barnabas & Gospel author',
        'John the Baptist was the forerunner. John the Apostle was the son of Zebedee. John Mark was Mary''s son and Barnabas'' cousin who accompanied Paul and wrote Mark''s Gospel.',
        'Matthew 3:1; Matthew 4:21; Acts 12:25; Colossians 4:10',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["Preached repentance in the wilderness of Judea and was beheaded by Herod Antipas.","Son of Zebedee, author of the fourth Gospel, three epistles, and Revelation.","Cousin of Barnabas who departed during Paul''s first missionary journey, but later wrote the second Gospel."],"hint":"Zebedee''s son was the Apostle; Barnabas'' cousin was John Mark.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Name Confusion Traps","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
