1. Herod the Great
2. Herod Antipas (Tetrarch)
3. Herod Agrippa I',
        '"Herod the Great: Bethlehem infants; Herod Antipas: Beheaded John the Baptist; Herod Agrippa I: Executed James","Herod the Great: Beheaded John; Herod Antipas: Executed James; Herod Agrippa I: Bethlehem infants","Herod the Great: Executed James; Herod Antipas: Bethlehem infants; Herod Agrippa I: Beheaded John","Herod the Great: Bethlehem infants; Herod Antipas: Executed James; Herod Agrippa I: Beheaded John"'::text[],
        'Herod the Great: Bethlehem infants; Herod Antipas: Beheaded John the Baptist; Herod Agrippa I: Executed James',
        'Herod the Great slaughtered the infants (Matthew 2). His son Herod Antipas beheaded John and mocked Jesus (Luke 23). His grandson Herod Agrippa I killed James and was eaten by worms (Acts 12).',
        'Matthew 2:16; Mark 6:27; Luke 23:7–11; Acts 12:1–23',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["Ordered the massacre of male infants in Bethlehem.","Beheaded John the Baptist and questioned Jesus during His trial.","Executed James the brother of John with the sword and was struck down by an angel at Caesarea."],"hint":"The Great = Nativity; Antipas = John & Passion; Agrippa I = Acts 12 martyr of James.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Name Confusion Traps","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
