        32,
        5,
        'NAME CONFUSION TRAPS:
In the Old Testament, two prominent kings of the northern kingdom of Israel were named Jeroboam: Jeroboam I (son of Nebat) and Jeroboam II (son of Jehoash). What notorious legacy characterized Jeroboam I?',
        '"He captured the city of Damascus and brought it under northern tribute","He restored the border of Israel from Lebo-hamath as far as the Sea of the Arabah","He was contemporary with the prophets Amos and Hosea during economic prosperity","He erected golden calves at Bethel and Dan and instituted a counterfeit priesthood"'::text[],
        'He erected golden calves at Bethel and Dan and instituted a counterfeit priesthood',
        'Jeroboam I set up the golden calves at Bethel and Dan to prevent Israel from worshiping in Jerusalem (1 Kings 12). Jeroboam II expanded borders centuries later (2 Kings 14).',
        '1 Kings 12:26–33; 2 Kings 14:23–28',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["He led the ten northern tribes to rebel against Solomon''s son Rehoboam.","He made two golden calves, setting one in Bethel and one in Dan.","He became the proverbial standard of northern apostasy: \"who made Israel to sin.\""],"hint":"Jeroboam I invented the golden calf shrines at Dan and Bethel.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Name Confusion Traps","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
