        'bible-puzzles',
        33,
        1,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DETAIL:
Examine the life of Moses. Which of the following statements contains an IMPOSSIBLE HISTORICAL ERROR?',
        '"Moses crossed the Jordan River and personally led the conquest of Jericho","Moses married Zipporah the daughter of Jethro priest of Midian","Moses was placed by his mother in a papyrus basket among the reeds of the Nile","Moses saw the Promised Land from the summit of Mount Pisgah before he died"'::text[],
        'Moses crossed the Jordan River and personally led the conquest of Jericho',
        'Moses was forbidden by God from crossing the Jordan because of his disobedience at Meribah (Numbers 20:12, Deuteronomy 34:4). Joshua led Israel across the Jordan and captured Jericho.',
        'Deuteronomy 3:25–27; 34:4–5; Joshua 1:1–2',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["Moses led Israel out of Egypt and through the Red Sea.","He struck the rock at Meribah in anger instead of speaking to it.","Examine whether he crossed the Jordan River into the Promised Land."],"hint":"Moses died on the east side of the Jordan and never set foot in Canaan.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"The Impossible Detail","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
