        'bible-puzzles',
        33,
        2,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DETAIL:
Which of these statements regarding King David contains an IMPOSSIBLE HISTORICAL ERROR?',
        '"David laid the foundation stones and built the roof of the temple in Jerusalem","David wrote numerous psalms including Psalm 23 and Psalm 51","David was anointed by Samuel at Bethlehem while tending his father's sheep","David was forbidden by God to build the temple because he had shed much blood in warfare"'::text[],
        'David laid the foundation stones and built the roof of the temple in Jerusalem',
        'David was not permitted to build the temple because he was a man of war who shed blood. God reserved the actual building for his son Solomon (1 Chronicles 22:8).',
        '1 Chronicles 22:6–10; 28:2–3; 1 Kings 6:1',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["David purchased the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite.","He gathered vast quantities of gold, silver, bronze, and cedar for the temple.","Did David personally build the stone sanctuary of the temple?"],"hint":"Solomon built the temple, not David.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"The Impossible Detail","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
