        'bible-puzzles',
        33,
        3,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DETAIL:
Which of the following claims about the Day of Pentecost in Acts 2 is an IMPOSSIBLE HISTORICAL ERROR?',
        '"Paul preached alongside Peter to the crowd on the Day of Pentecost","Some mockers said: \"They are filled with new wine\"","About three thousand souls were baptized and added to the church that day","Visitors from Parthia, Media, Elam, Mesopotamia, and Rome heard them in their own languages"'::text[],
        'Paul preached alongside Peter to the crowd on the Day of Pentecost',
        'Paul (Saul) was not a believer or present as a preacher on Pentecost in Acts 2; he was still an unconverted Pharisee persecuting believers until his Damascus road vision in Acts 9.',
        'Acts 2:1–41; Acts 9:1–6',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["The Holy Spirit descended with the sound of a rushing wind and divided tongues of fire.","Peter stood up with the Eleven and addressed the gathered pilgrims.","Examine the presence of Saul of Tarsus (Paul)."],"hint":"Paul was not yet converted on the Day of Pentecost in Acts 2.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"The Impossible Detail","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
