        'bible-puzzles',
        33,
        4,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DETAIL:
Examine the life and miracles of Jesus in the Gospels. Which statement contains an IMPOSSIBLE SCRIPTURAL ERROR?',
        '"Jesus turned water into wine at the wedding feast of Cana in Galilee","Jesus walked on the stormy waters of the Sea of Galilee in the fourth watch of the night","Jesus fed five thousand men besides women and children with five loaves and two fish","Jesus struck down Pontius Pilate with fire from heaven when Pilate sentenced Him"'::text[],
        'Jesus struck down Pontius Pilate with fire from heaven when Pilate sentenced Him',
        'Jesus never called down fire on Pilate or His persecutors. As 1 Peter 2:23 says: "When he was reviled, he did not revile in return; when he suffered, he did not threaten, but continued entrusting himself to him who judges justly."',
        'Matthew 27:11–26; John 19:10–11; 1 Peter 2:23',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["Jesus performed miracles over nature, disease, demons, and death.","Examine whether Jesus ever used His divine power for selfish enrichment or political coercion."],"hint":"Jesus willingly yielded to the cross without striking Pilate.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"The Impossible Detail","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
