        'bible-puzzles',
        33,
        5,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DETAIL:
Which of these accounts regarding the Hebrew patriarch Abraham contains an IMPOSSIBLE FACTUAL CONTRADICTION?',
        '"Abraham interceded for the righteous in Sodom, pleading down from fifty to ten","Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine and blessed Abraham","Isaac offered his father Abraham as a sacrifice on Mount Moriah","Abraham bought the cave of Machpelah from Ephron the Hittite to bury Sarah"'::text[],
        'Isaac offered his father Abraham as a sacrifice on Mount Moriah',
        'Genesis 22 explicitly records that God tested Abraham, commanding him to offer his son Isaac, not the reverse. Abraham bound Isaac and laid him upon the altar.',
        'Genesis 22:1–14; Hebrews 11:17–19',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Impossible Detail","clues":["Abraham journeyed from Ur of the Chaldeans to Haran, then to Canaan.","He had two primary sons: Ishmael and Isaac.","Examine who actually offered whom on Mount Moriah."],"hint":"Abraham was the father offering his son Isaac on the altar.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"The Impossible Detail","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
