(
        'bible-puzzles-l34-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        34,
        1,
        'PLAUSIBLE COUNTERFEITS:
Which of the following popular sayings is frequently mistaken for a Bible verse, but is NEVER found anywhere in the Bible?',
        '"\"God helps those who help themselves\"","\"Trust in the Lord with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding\"","\"A soft answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger\"","\"Pride goes before destruction, and a haughty spirit before a fall\""'::text[],
        '"God helps those who help themselves"',
        '"God helps those who help themselves" is an ancient proverb popularized by Algernon Sidney and Benjamin Franklin, not Scripture. The Bible teaches that God justifies the ungodly and saves the helpless (Romans 5:6).',
        'Proverbs 3:5; Proverbs 15:1; Proverbs 16:18; Romans 5:6',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Often attributed to Proverbs or Benjamin Franklin.","Popular folk wisdom concerning personal self-reliance.","God actually emphasizes helping the helpless and destitute."],"hint":"A famous quote coined by English philosopher Algernon Sidney, not Solomon.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Plausible Counterfeits","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l34-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        34,
        2,
        'PLAUSIBLE COUNTERFEITS:
What is the EXACT wording of the biblical warning regarding wealth in 1 Timothy 6:10?',
        '"\"Money itself is the root of every evil on earth\"","\"For the love of money is a root of all kinds of evils\"","\"Whoever touches gold shall fall into spiritual ruin\"","\"Possessing wealth is an abomination before the Lord\""'::text[],
        '"For the love of money is a root of all kinds of evils"',
        '1 Timothy 6:10 reads: "For the love of money is a root of all kinds of evils. It is through this craving that some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many pangs." Money itself is not evil; loving money is.',
        '1 Timothy 6:10',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Many people misquote it as \"Money is the root of all evil.\"","Paul specifies an attitude of the heart toward money.","Notice the precise qualification regarding what kind of evils spring from it."],"hint":"It is the \"love of money\" (greed), not money itself, that is the root.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Plausible Counterfeits","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
