        3,
        'PLAUSIBLE COUNTERFEITS:
Which common modern cliché is often attributed to the Bible, but was actually coined in a sermon by John Wesley in 1778?',
        '"\"Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin\"","\"Be holy, for I the Lord your God am holy\"","\"Create in me a clean heart, O God\"","\"Cleanliness is next to godliness\""'::text[],
        '"Cleanliness is next to godliness"',
        '"Cleanliness is next to godliness" was coined in an 1778 sermon by John Wesley, though reminiscent of ancient rabbinic adages. It is not found in the text of Scripture.',
        'Leviticus 19:2; Psalm 51:2, 10',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Deals with personal hygiene and sanctification.","Popularly quoted as if it were a commandment in Leviticus.","Connects cleanliness to holiness."],"hint":"Connects keeping clean with being godly; popularized by Methodist John Wesley.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Plausible Counterfeits","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
