        34,
        4,
        'PLAUSIBLE COUNTERFEITS:
People often claim the Bible promises: "God won''t give you more than you can handle." What does 1 Corinthians 10:13 ACTUALLY state regarding temptation?',
        '"He will also provide the way of escape, that you may be able to endure it","He will remove every trial before it causes you sorrow or burden","He guarantees that life's problems will never exceed your natural strength","He promises that believers will never face overwhelming grief"'::text[],
        'He will also provide the way of escape, that you may be able to endure it',
        '1 Corinthians 10:13 promises that God will not allow you to be tempted beyond what you can bear, but will provide "the way of escape" to endure it. Paul later notes in 2 Corinthians 1:8 that he was burdened "beyond our strength" so they would rely on God.',
        '1 Corinthians 10:13; 2 Corinthians 1:8–9',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["God is faithful.","He will not let you be tempted beyond your ability.","What does God provide along with the temptation so that you may endure it?"],"hint":"God provides \"the way of escape\" to endure temptation.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Plausible Counterfeits","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
