        'bible-puzzles',
        35,
        2,
        'SCRIPTURE TRAP BOSS:
Identify the factual scriptural error among these details of Jesus'' crucifixion:',
        '"One of the soldiers pierced His side with a spear, bringing forth blood and water","The Roman soldiers broke both of Jesus' legs to hasten His death before sunset","The soldiers divided His garments into four parts, one for each soldier","For His seamless tunic, they cast lots to decide whose it should be"'::text[],
        'The Roman soldiers broke both of Jesus'' legs to hasten His death before sunset',
        'John 19:33 states: "When they came to Jesus and saw that he was already dead, they did not break his legs." This fulfilled Scripture: "Not one of his bones will be broken."',
        'John 19:23–36; Exodus 12:46; Psalm 34:20',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["Two criminals were crucified with Him, one on His right and one on His left.","Pilate wrote an inscription: \"Jesus of Nazareth, the King of the Jews.\"","Examine whether the soldiers broke Jesus'' legs."],"hint":"Jesus'' bones were preserved unbroken to fulfill the Passover lamb typology.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Scripture Trap Boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
