        4,
        'SCRIPTURE TRAP BOSS:
ODD ONE OUT:
Which of these four men was NEVER an anointed king over any part of Israel or Judah?',
        '"Jehoiada","Jehoahaz","Jehoash (Joash)","Jehoiachin"'::text[],
        'Jehoiada',
        'Jehoiada was the venerable High Priest who guarded baby Joash from Athaliah and anointed Joash king (2 Kings 11). The other three (Jehoahaz, Jehoash, Jehoiachin) were all kings of Judah or Israel.',
        '2 Kings 11:4–12; 2 Chronicles 24:15–16',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Odd One Out","clues":["Three were crowned kings in Jerusalem or Samaria.","One was the faithful court priest who hid baby Joash and orchestrated Queen Athaliah''s overthrow."],"hint":"Jehoiada was the righteous High Priest, not a king, though honored with burial among the kings.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Scripture Trap Boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
