(
        'bible-puzzles-l35-c5',
        'bible-puzzles',
        35,
        5,
        'SCRIPTURE TRAP BOSS:
In 2 Samuel 12, the prophet Nathan confronted David with a parable of a rich man who spared his own flocks and took a poor man''s single beloved pet ewe lamb. When David furiously proclaimed, "The man who has done this deserves to die, and he shall restore the lamb fourfold," what four tragic deaths in David''s own family fulfilled this fourfold judgment?',
        '"Solomon, Rehoboam, Jeroboam, and Abijah","Kileab, Shephatiah, Ithream, and Nathan","Bathsheba's first infant son, Amnon, Absalom, and Adonijah","Jonathan, Ish-bosheth, Saul, and Mephibosheth"'::text[],
        'Bathsheba''s first infant son, Amnon, Absalom, and Adonijah',
        'David pronounced a fourfold restitution (2 Samuel 12:6). Consequently, four of his sons died prematurely: 1. Bathsheba''s first baby (2 Sam 12:18); 2. Amnon (slain by Absalom, 2 Sam 13:29); 3. Absalom (slain by Joab, 2 Sam 18:14); 4. Adonijah (executed by Solomon, 1 Kings 2:25).',
        '2 Samuel 12:6, 14–19; 13:28–29; 18:14–15; 1 Kings 2:24–25',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["David decreed a fourfold restitution.","God said: \"The sword shall never depart from your house.\"","Four of David''s sons died untimely, violent deaths."],"hint":"Four of David''s sons died as a consequence of his judgment.","stage":7,"category":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Scripture Trap Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l36-c1',
        'bible-puzzles',
        36,
        1,
        'TYPOLOGY LINKS:
In Genesis 14:18, Melchizedek king of Salem brought out two specific items to bless Abraham after the rescue of Lot. These items prefigure Christ''s Last Supper with His disciples. What two items did Melchizedek bring out?',
        '"Roasted grain and bitter herbs","Milk and honey","Bread and wine","Water and oil"'::text[],
        'Bread and wine',
        'Genesis 14:18 states: "And Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine. (He was priest of God Most High.)" This foreshadowed Christ, our eternal High Priest, instituting bread and wine.',
        'Genesis 14:18; Matthew 26:26–28; Hebrews 7:1–3',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["He was priest of God Most High (El Elyon).","He refreshed Abraham''s weary army with these sacramental elements.","Identical to the elements instituted by Jesus at the Passover meal."],"hint":"The two foundational elements of the Lord''s Supper.","stage":8,"category":"The Hidden Connection","level_theme":"Typology Links","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l36-c2',
        'bible-puzzles',
        36,
        2,
        'TYPOLOGY LINKS:
In John 3:14, Jesus directly linked His upcoming crucifixion to an Old Testament event in Numbers 21: "And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, so must the Son of Man be lifted up." What was the material and form of the serpent Moses made?',
        '"A bronze (brass) serpent","A carved wooden serpent","A silver serpent","A golden serpent"'::text[],
        'A bronze (brass) serpent',
        'Numbers 21:9 states: "So Moses made a bronze serpent and set it on a pole. And if a serpent bit anyone, he would look at the bronze serpent and live." Jesus taught this was a direct type of His being lifted up on the cross.',
        'Numbers 21:8–9; John 3:14–15',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Find the Hidden Connection","clues":["Fiery serpents bit the murmuring Israelites.","God commanded Moses to make a serpent of this shiny metal and set it on a pole.","Whoever looked at the metal serpent lived."],"hint":"Made of reddish-brown polished bronze (Nehushtan).","stage":8,"category":"The Hidden Connection","level_theme":"Typology Links","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-puzzles-l36-c3',
        'bible-puzzles',
        36,
        3,
        'TYPOLOGY LINKS:
In 1 Corinthians 5:7, the apostle Paul writes: "Cleanse out the old leaven that you may be a new lump... For Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed." What requirement was mandated for the original Passover lamb in Exodus 12 that corresponds to Christ''s moral perfection?',
        '"Born in Bethlehem","White fleece without gray spots","Without blemish or defect","Fed exclusively on hyssop"'::text[],
        'Without blemish or defect',
        'Exodus 12:5 commands: "Your lamb shall be without blemish, a male a year old." 1 Peter 1:19 affirms that we were redeemed "with the precious blood of Christ, like that of a lamb without blemish or spot."',
        'Exodus 12:5; 1 Peter 1:19',
