        '"Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians, and Philemon","1 Thessalonians, 2 Thessalonians, 1 Timothy, and 2 Timothy","Romans, 1 Corinthians, 2 Corinthians, and Galatians","Titus, Hebrews, James, and 1 Peter"'::text[],
        'Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians, and Philemon',
        'Paul''s four classic Prison Epistles written during his first Roman imprisonment are Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians, and Philemon.',
        'Ephesians 6:20; Philippians 1:7, 13; Colossians 4:18; Philemon 1, 9',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["All written from imprisonment where Paul refers to himself as an \"ambassador in chains\".","Carried to Asia Minor and Macedonia by Tychicus, Onesimus, and Epaphroditus.","Includes two letters addressing cities in the Lycus Valley."],"hint":"Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians, and Philemon.","stage":9,"category":"The Expert Puzzle Room","level_theme":"Expert Puzzle Boss","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
