Examine these four complex details of Old Testament Levitical and High Priestly ritual. Which ONE statement contains an explicit FACTUAL ERROR?',
        '"Incense was put on burning coals before the Lord so that the cloud of incense covered the mercy seat, lest the High Priest die","The High Priest wore pure white linen garments (tunic, sash, turban) when entering the Most Holy Place on Yom Kippur","Two goats were presented: one was slaughtered as a sin offering; the other was sent into the wilderness as the scapegoat (Azazel)","On the Day of Atonement, the High Priest entered the Most Holy Place wearing his dazzling golden garments with the breastpiece of twelve jewels"'::text[],
        'On the Day of Atonement, the High Priest entered the Most Holy Place wearing his dazzling golden garments with the breastpiece of twelve jewels',
        'Leviticus 16:4 explicitly specifies that on the Day of Atonement, the High Priest stripped off his ornate golden garments and wore only simple holy linen garments (tunic, undergarments, sash, turban) to make atonement. He put the golden garments back on only after atonement was complete.',
        'Leviticus 16:4, 23–24',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Spot the Biblical Mistake","clues":["The High Priest wore the breastpiece with twelve precious stones and the Urim and Thummim.","Pomegranates and golden bells hung from the hem of the robe of the ephod.","Examine the Day of Atonement (Yom Kippur) animal sacrifices in Leviticus 16."],"hint":"On Yom Kippur, the High Priest entered in humble, plain white linen, not his ornate golden robes.","stage":9,"category":"The Expert Puzzle Room","level_theme":"Expert Puzzle Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
