        1,
        'FORENSIC CLUES GRANDMASTER:
DOSSIER:
- I was an exile in Babylon living among the captives by the Chebar canal.
- In the thirtieth year, on the fifth day of the fourth month, the heavens were opened and I saw visions of God.
- I was a priest, the son of Buzi.
- I was shown four living creatures with wheels within wheels, full of eyes around their rims, and an expanse like gleaming crystal.
- I was commanded to eat a scroll sweet as honey and was appointed a watchman for the house of Israel.
Who am I?',
        '"Zechariah","Ezekiel","Jeremiah","Daniel"'::text[],
        'Ezekiel',
        'Ezekiel 1:1–3 explicitly introduces Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, by the river Chebar in Babylon, who saw visions of God and was appointed watchman.',
        'Ezekiel 1:1–3; 2:8–3:3, 17',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Priest and prophet by the Chebar canal in Babylon.","Son of Buzi.","Saw the vision of the fiery chariot-throne and the valley of dry bones."],"hint":"Prophet of the Chebar canal, son of Buzi.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Forensic Clues Grandmaster","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
