        46,
        2,
        'FORENSIC CLUES GRANDMASTER:
DOSSIER:
- I was a native of Pontus, a tentmaker by trade, who fled Rome with my wife when Claudius expelled all Jews.
- In Ephesus, my wife and I heard a brilliant Alexandrian orator named Apollos who spoke boldly in the synagogue, knowing only the baptism of John.
- We took Apollos aside and explained to him the way of God more accurately.
- Paul sends greetings from us and the church in our house in multiple epistles.
Who am I and who is my wife?',
        '"Ananias and Sapphira","Philemon and Apphia","Andronicus and Junia","Aquila and Priscilla (Prisca)"'::text[],
        'Aquila and Priscilla (Prisca)',
        'Aquila and Priscilla took Apollos aside in Ephesus and explained the way of God more accurately (Acts 18:26). They were Paul''s trusted fellow workers who risked their necks for his life.',
        'Acts 18:1–3, 24–26; Romans 16:3–5; 1 Corinthians 16:19',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Husband and wife ministry team.","Tentmakers in Corinth and Ephesus.","Instructed Apollos in deeper Christian doctrine."],"hint":"Aquila and his wife Priscilla.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Forensic Clues Grandmaster","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
