        'bible-puzzles',
        46,
        3,
        'FORENSIC CLUES GRANDMASTER:
DOSSIER:
- I was a wealthy chief tax collector (architelones) in the ancient city of Jericho.
- Because I was small of stature and the crowd was dense, I ran ahead and climbed up into a sycamore tree to see Jesus.
- Jesus looked up and called me by name: "Hurry and come down, for I must stay at your house today."
- I joyfully pledged to give half my goods to the poor and restore fourfold anything defrauded.
Who am I?',
        '"Cornelius","Levi (Matthew)","Bartimaeus","Zacchaeus"'::text[],
        'Zacchaeus',
        'Zacchaeus was a chief tax collector in Jericho, small in stature, who climbed a sycamore-fig tree to see Jesus. Jesus announced: "Today salvation has come to this house."',
        'Luke 19:1–10',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Chief tax collector in Jericho.","Small in physical height.","Climbed a sycamore tree to see Jesus."],"hint":"Zacchaeus, the short tax collector of Jericho.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Forensic Clues Grandmaster","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
