        46,
        4,
        'FORENSIC CLUES GRANDMASTER:
DOSSIER:
- I was a runaway slave from the city of Colossae.
- I had apparently defrauded or stolen from my Christian master and fled all the way to Rome.
- There in Rome I met the apostle Paul while he was in chains, and through his gospel I became his spiritual child in the faith.
- Paul sent me back to my master carrying a personal letter, urging my master to receive me no longer as a slave, but as a beloved brother.
Who am I and who was my master?',
        '"Slave: Tychicus; Master: Gaius","Slave: Aristarchus; Master: Theophilus","Slave: Onesimus; Master: Philemon","Slave: Epaphras; Master: Archippus"'::text[],
        'Slave: Onesimus; Master: Philemon',
        'Onesimus was Philemon''s runaway slave who became a believer under Paul''s ministry in Rome. Paul returned him to Philemon, asking Philemon to receive him as a beloved brother.',
        'Philemon 1:10–18; Colossians 4:9',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Runaway slave whose Greek name means \"Useful\" or \"Profitable\".","Converted in prison through Paul''s ministry in Rome.","Sent back to his master with a tender letter of reconciliation."],"hint":"Onesimus was the slave; Philemon was the master.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Forensic Clues Grandmaster","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
