        46,
        5,
        'FORENSIC CLUES GRANDMASTER:
DOSSIER:
- I was an Ethiopian court dignitary, a eunuch of great authority under Candace, queen of the Ethiopians, in charge of all her treasure.
- I had traveled more than a thousand miles to Jerusalem to worship.
- On my return journey on the desert road to Gaza, I sat in my chariot reading the scroll of the prophet Isaiah.
- An evangelist was miraculously directed by the Spirit to run up to my chariot and explain the gospel to me, whereupon I was baptized in roadside water.
Who was the evangelist who baptized me?',
        '"Stephen the Deacon","Peter the Apostle","Barnabas of Cyprus","Philip the Evangelist"'::text[],
        'Philip the Evangelist',
        'Philip the Evangelist was told by an angel to go toward the south on the road from Jerusalem to Gaza. He met the Ethiopian treasurer, preached Jesus from Isaiah 53, and baptized him in water.',
        'Acts 8:26–40',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["One of the Seven deacons chosen in Acts 6.","Had previously sparked a great revival in Samaria.","The Spirit caught him away to Azotus immediately after baptizing me."],"hint":"Philip the Evangelist on the desert road to Gaza.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Forensic Clues Grandmaster","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
