        '"Pharaoh: Ten plagues & Red Sea; Nebuchadnezzar: Golden image & lycanthropic humbling; Cyrus: Decree to rebuild Jerusalem","Pharaoh: Ten plagues; Nebuchadnezzar: Decree to rebuild Jerusalem; Cyrus: Golden image","Pharaoh: Golden image; Nebuchadnezzar: Ten plagues; Cyrus: Red Sea","Pharaoh: Decree to rebuild Jerusalem; Nebuchadnezzar: Red Sea; Cyrus: Golden image"'::text[],
        'Pharaoh: Ten plagues & Red Sea; Nebuchadnezzar: Golden image & lycanthropic humbling; Cyrus: Decree to rebuild Jerusalem',
        'Pharaoh was judged by the plagues and Red Sea. Nebuchadnezzar erected the Dura image and was humbled to eat grass. Cyrus issued the edict for the Jews to rebuild the temple in Ezra 1.',
        'Exodus 7–14; Daniel 3–4; Ezra 1:1–4; Isaiah 44:28; 45:1',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["One endured ten devastating plagues and had his chariots swallowed in the Red Sea.","One built a 90-foot golden image on the plain of Dura and was later humbled by living like a beast for seven seasons.","One was named by Isaiah over a century before his birth and issued the historic decree allowing the Jews to return and rebuild Jerusalem."],"hint":"Pharaoh = Exodus plagues; Nebuchadnezzar = golden image & madness; Cyrus = rebuilding edict.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Ultimate Logic Grid","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
