        49,
        1,
        'BIBLE PUZZLE MASTER:
FORENSIC MASTER INVESTIGATION:
- I was a wealthy merchant woman from the city of Thyatira, a seller of purple fabrics.
- I was living in the Macedonian Roman colony of Philippi.
- On the Sabbath day, Paul and Silas found me and other women praying by the riverside outside the city gate.
- The Lord opened my heart to pay attention to what was said by Paul.
- I and my household were baptized, and I persuaded Paul''s mission team to lodge at my house: "If you have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, come to my house and stay."
Who am I?',
        '"Damaris","Phoebe","Priscilla","Lydia"'::text[],
        'Lydia',
        'Acts 16:14 tells of Lydia from Thyatira, a seller of purple cloth in Philippi, whose heart the Lord opened. She became the first convert in Europe and opened her home as the base for the Philippian church.',
        'Acts 16:14–15, 40',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Seller of expensive purple goods from Thyatira.","Converted by the riverside in Philippi.","First recorded Christian convert on the continent of Europe."],"hint":"Lydia of Philippi, seller of purple.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Bible Puzzle Master","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
