        'Cornelius was the Roman centurion in Caesarea who summoned Peter from Joppa. When Peter preached Christ, the Holy Spirit was poured out on the Gentiles, settling the apostolic admission of Gentiles into the church.',
        'Acts 10:1–48; 11:1–18',
        '{"puzzle_type":"The Bible Detective","clues":["Centurion of the Italian Cohort at Caesarea.","Devout God-fearer whose alms and prayers were remembered by God.","The first uncircumcised Gentile convert with his household in Acts 10."],"hint":"Centurion Cornelius of Caesarea.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Bible Puzzle Master","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
