Match each to his distinct biblical testimony:',
        '"Enoch: Chariot of fire; Elijah: Walked with God; Moses: Without genealogy; Melchizedek: Buried by God","Enoch: Walked with God & was taken; Elijah: Chariot of fire whirlwind; Moses: Buried by God with unknown grave; Melchizedek: Without genealogy continuing forever","Enoch: Walked with God; Elijah: Buried by God; Moses: Chariot of fire; Melchizedek: Without genealogy","Enoch: Buried by God; Elijah: Without genealogy; Moses: Chariot of fire; Melchizedek: Walked with God"'::text[],
        'Enoch: Walked with God & was taken; Elijah: Chariot of fire whirlwind; Moses: Buried by God with unknown grave; Melchizedek: Without genealogy continuing forever',
        'Enoch was translated because he walked with God (Gen 5). Elijah ascended in a fiery whirlwind (2 Kings 2). Moses was personally buried by God on Nebo (Deut 34). Melchizedek is presented without recorded genealogy as an eternal priestly type (Hebrews 7).',
        'Genesis 5:24; 2 Kings 2:11; Deuteronomy 34:5–6; Hebrews 7:3',
        '{"puzzle_type":"Bible Logic Grid","clues":["Enoch: \"Walked with God, and he was not, for God took him\" (Genesis 5:24).","Elijah: \"Ascended by a whirlwind into heaven in a chariot of fire\" (2 Kings 2:11).","Moses: \"Died on Mount Nebo; the Lord buried him in the valley in Moab, and no man knows his grave to this day\" (Deuteronomy 34:5–6).","Melchizedek: \"Without father or mother or genealogy, having neither beginning of days nor end of life, resembling the Son of God he continues a priest forever\" (Hebrews 7:3)."],"hint":"Enoch walked with God; Elijah took the fiery chariot; Moses was buried by God; Melchizedek is the eternal priest type.","stage":10,"category":"The Ultimate Bible Puzzle","level_theme":"Puzzle Grandmaster Finale","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":20,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
