        8,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I am the amanuensis (scribe) who physically put pen to parchment to write down Paul’s grand theological masterpiece to the church in the capital of the empire. Right before the final doxology, I inserted my own personal greeting: "I, [...], who wrote down this letter, greet you in the Lord." Who am I?',
        '"Tertius","Tychicus","Quartus","Silvanus"'::text[],
        'Tertius',
        'Tertius was Paul’s secretary/amanuensis who wrote down the Epistle to the Romans and added his own greeting in 16:22.',
        'Romans 16:22',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Recorded in Romans 16:22.","Name is a Latin ordinal meaning \"third.\"","Greeted the church alongside Gaius, Erastus, and Quartus."],"hint":"Paul’s amanuensis who wrote down the Epistle to the Romans.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Tertius of Iconium"],"stage":2,"stage_title":"Mystery of the People","level_theme":"Forgotten Epistolary Figures","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
