        'bible-riddles',
        8,
        2,
        'WHO AM I?
When all the believers in the Roman province of Asia turned away from Paul during his second imprisonment in Rome, I was not ashamed of his chains. I searched for him diligently in the imperial capital until I found him in his cold dungeon and frequently refreshed his spirit. Paul prayed that the Lord would grant mercy to my household and that I might find mercy from the Lord on that Day. Who am I?',
        '"Onesiphorus","Tychicus","Epaphras","Philemon"'::text[],
        'Onesiphorus',
        'Onesiphorus searched diligently for Paul in Rome, refreshed him in prison, and was not ashamed of his chains.',
        '2 Timothy 1:16–18; 4:19',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Contrasted with Phygelus and Hermogenes who deserted Paul.","Faithful resident of Ephesus whose household was repeatedly blessed.","Mentioned in 2 Timothy 1:16–18 and 4:19."],"hint":"Faithful disciple who searched Rome to refresh imprisoned Paul.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Onesiforos"],"stage":2,"stage_title":"Mystery of the People","level_theme":"Forgotten Epistolary Figures","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
