        'bible-riddles',
        8,
        3,
        'THE BIBLICAL RELATIONSHIP RIDDLE:
I was a runaway bondservant who robbed my wealthy Christian master in Colossae and fled across the Mediterranean to Rome. There in prison, I encountered the Apostle Paul, who led me to Christ and referred to me as "my child, whom I have begotten in my chains." Paul sent me back to my master carrying a personal letter that pleaded for me to be received no longer as a slave, but as a beloved brother. Who am I?',
        '"Trophimus","Onesimus","Archippus","Epaphras"'::text[],
        'Onesimus',
        'Onesimus was the runaway slave of Philemon who was converted under Paul’s imprisonment and returned as a beloved Christian brother.',
