        'TYPE TWO ANSWERS — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
In Romans 16:12, the Apostle Paul sends affectionate greetings to two Christian women in the Roman church whose names sound remarkably alike—both derived from a Greek root meaning "delicate" or "luxurious"—and notes that they "work hard in the Lord." What are the names of these two hardworking women?',
