        9,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a prophetess who lived in Jerusalem in the Second Quarter (Mishneh) of the city, wife of Shallum keeper of the royal wardrobe. When King Josiah’s high priest Hilkiah discovered the lost Book of the Law in the temple, the king sent an official delegation not to Jeremiah or Zephaniah, but to me, to inquire of Yahweh concerning the impending wrath against Judah. Who am I?',
        '"Huldah","Deborah","Miriam","Anna"'::text[],
        'Huldah',
        'Huldah was the revered prophetess in Jerusalem consulted by King Josiah’s delegation upon finding the Book of the Law.',
