        'bible-riddles',
        9,
        2,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DESCRIPTION:
I was a non-Israelite diviner from Pethor near the Euphrates River, hired by Balak king of Moab with fees of divination to place an inescapable curse upon the advancing Israelites. Yet three times on mountain heights, as the Spirit of God overtook me, I opened my mouth to curse them, and only sublime poetic blessings poured forth from my lips, concluding with a vision of a Star rising from Jacob and a Scepter out of Israel. Who am I?',
        '"Balaam","Balak","Jethro","Melchizedek"'::text[],
        'Balaam',
        'Balaam son of Beor was hired by Balak to curse Israel, but God compelled him to pronounce blessings and prophecies of the Messiah.',
        'Numbers 22:1–24:25; 31:16; 2 Peter 2:15–16',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Impossible Description","is_typed":false,"clues":["Rode a donkey that spoke with a man’s voice to rebuke my madness.","Encountered the Angel of the Lord with a drawn sword in a narrow path between vineyards.","Later counseled the Midianites to seduce Israel with the daughters of Moab at Baal-peor."],"hint":"Pagan prophet whose donkey rebuked him before he blessed Israel.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Balaam son of Beor","Bileam"],"stage":2,"stage_title":"Mystery of the People","level_theme":"Unusual Prophets & Ancient Seers","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
