        10,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a wealthy member of the Jewish Sanhedrin from a town in Judea, an honorable counselor who was secretly a disciple of Jesus for fear of the Jews and had not consented to their counsel and deed. After the crucifixion, I boldly approached Pontius Pilate to request the body of Jesus, wrapped Him in clean linen, and laid Him in my own newly hewn rock tomb where no one had ever been laid. Who am I?',
        '"Simon of Cyrene","Jairus","Joseph of Arimathea","Nicodemus"'::text[],
        'Joseph of Arimathea',
        'Joseph of Arimathea, a rich Sanhedrin member and secret disciple, claimed Jesus’ body from Pilate and buried Him in his private garden tomb.',
        'Matthew 27:57–60; John 19:38–42',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["A native of Arimathea.","Fulfilled Isaiah 53:9: \"He made his grave with the wicked, and with a rich man in his death.\"","Joined by Nicodemus bearing seventy-five pounds of myrrh and aloes."],"hint":"Wealthy council member who donated his new rock tomb for Jesus.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Joseph of Arimathea","Joseph from Arimathea"],"stage":2,"stage_title":"Mystery of the People","level_theme":"Enigmas of the Gospels & Passion Week","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
