        'WHAT AM I?
I was the massive, nine-foot-long weapon of a Philistine giant from Gath whose iron head weighed six hundred shekels (about fifteen pounds), and whose shaft was described as being like a weaver’s beam. Later, after my owner was beheaded, my blade was wrapped in a cloth behind the priestly ephod at Nob until David claimed me, declaring: "There is none like that; give it to me." What am I?',
        '"Joab’s Dagger","Benaiah’s Spear","Goliath’s Sword","Saul’s Spear"'::text[],
        'Goliath’s Sword',
        'The sword of Goliath was kept wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod at Nob until Ahimelech gave it to David.',
        '1 Samuel 17:7, 51; 21:8–9',
        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Weapon of Goliath the Philistine champion.","David took Goliath’s own sword from its sheath to cut off his head.","Given to David by the priest Ahimelech at Nob."],"hint":"Giant’s blade kept at Nob and claimed by David.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Sword of Goliath","Goliaths Sword"],"stage":3,"stage_title":"Objects and Symbols","level_theme":"Instruments of War & Deliverance","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
