I was a linen waistband (girdle) that the prophet Jeremiah was instructed to buy, wear on his loins without putting into water, and then take on a long journey to the river Euphrates (Perath) to bury in a cleft of the rock. When Jeremiah returned many days later to dig me up, I was ruined, spoiled, and completely profitable for nothing—symbolizing how God would ruin the pride of Judah. What am I?',
        '"Jeremiah’s Linen Belt","Aaron’s Sash","John the Baptist’s Girdle","Elijah’s Leather Belt"'::text[],
