I was a common construction brick (clay tablet) upon which the prophet Ezekiel was commanded to engrave a detailed diagram of the city of Jerusalem. The prophet then built miniature siege works, threw up an assault ramp, set camps around it, placed battering rams against it on all sides, and held an iron griddle (plate) between himself and the brick as an iron wall—serving as a dramatic prophetic sign to the house of Israel. What am I?',
