I was an exquisite vessel made of soft white stone, filled with a pound of pure nard of extraordinary value—worth more than three hundred denarii (a full year’s wages for a laborer). Brought into a banquet in Bethany, my owner broke my neck and poured my fragrant contents upon the head and feet of Jesus, wiping His feet with her hair until the entire house was filled with the fragrance. What am I?',
        '"The Alabaster Flask of Nard","The Water Jar of Cana","The Golden Censer","The Cup of Blessing"'::text[],
