        'WHAT AM I?
We were thirty silver coins paid from the temple treasury to an apostle who agreed to betray his Master in a secluded olive grove. Consumed with remorse after Jesus was condemned, the traitor flung us across the sanctuary floor before hanging himself. Because we were blood money, the chief priests refused to put us into the treasury and used us to buy the Potter’s Field as a burial place for foreigners. What are we?',
        '"The Temple Shekel","The Thirty Pieces of Silver","The Widow’s Two Mites","The Stater in the Fish’s Mouth"'::text[],
        'The Thirty Pieces of Silver',
        'Judas Iscariot betrayed Jesus for thirty pieces of silver; cast into the temple, the money purchased the Potter’s Field.',
        'Matthew 26:14–16; 27:3–10; Zechariah 11:12–13',
        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Thirty pieces of silver (Tyrian shekels/tetradrachms).","Fulfilled Zechariah 11:12–13: \"They weighed out as my price thirty pieces of silver.\"","Bought the field called Akeldama, the Field of Blood."],"hint":"Thirty silver coins paid to Judas to betray Christ.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Thirty Pieces of Silver","30 Pieces of Silver","The Blood Money"],"stage":3,"stage_title":"Objects and Symbols","level_theme":"New Testament Sacred Objects","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
