        3,
        'WHAT AM I?
I was an inner undergarment (chiton) worn by Jesus on the day of His crucifixion. Woven in one piece from the top down without any seam, the four Roman executioners chose not to tear me into four pieces like His other garments, but cast lots for me, fulfilling the ancient prophecy of Psalm 22:18: "They divided my garments among them, and for my clothing they cast lots." What am I?',
        '"The Seamless Tunic of Christ","The Linen Shroud","The Purple Robe","The Veil of the Temple"'::text[],
        'The Seamless Tunic of Christ',
        'Jesus’ seamless tunic was not torn by the soldiers at the cross; they cast lots to decide who would get it.',
        'John 19:23–24; Psalm 22:18',
        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Woven seamless throughout.","Sought intact by the Roman quaternion of soldiers at Golgotha.","Regarded as a symbol of the undivided unity of Christ’s church."],"hint":"Seamless woven tunic of Jesus for which Roman soldiers cast lots.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Seamless Tunic","Seamless Robe","Seamless Garment","Seamless Tunic"],"stage":3,"stage_title":"Objects and Symbols","level_theme":"New Testament Sacred Objects","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
