        'WHAT AM I?
I was a massive, sixty-foot-high, beautifully woven curtain of blue, purple, and scarlet yarns that hung inside the Jerusalem Temple, dividing the Holy Place from the Holy of Holies. At the exact moment Jesus breathed His last on the cross and cried, "It is finished!", an invisible power tore me in two from top to bottom, demonstrating that the way into God’s presence was now thrown wide open to all believers. What am I?',
        '"The Linen Shroud","The Veil of the Temple","The Tabernacle Curtains","The High Priest’s Robe"'::text[],
        'The Veil of the Temple',
        'The veil of the temple separating the Holy of Holies was torn in two from top to bottom when Jesus died, opening access to God.',
        'Matthew 27:51; Mark 15:38; Hebrews 10:19–20',
        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The veil of the temple (katapetasma).","Torn from top to bottom (indicating divine action, not human hands).","Hebrews 10:19–20 describes Jesus’ flesh as this veil opened for us."],"hint":"Temple curtain torn in two from top to bottom at Jesus’ death.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Temple Veil","Veil of the Temple","The Veil"],"stage":3,"stage_title":"Objects and Symbols","level_theme":"New Testament Sacred Objects","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
