        16,
        2,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a remote, steep ravine east of the Jordan River where the prophet Elijah was commanded to hide during the three-and-a-half-year drought he had declared over Israel. There, ravens brought the prophet bread and meat every morning and evening, and he drank from my bubbling brook until the water dried up because there was no rain in the land. What brook am I?',
        '"Brook Kishon","Brook Kidron","River Jabbok","Brook Cherith"'::text[],
        'Brook Cherith',
        'Brook Cherith was the secluded wadi where Elijah was sustained by ravens and brook water until the stream dried up.',
        '1 Kings 17:2–7',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Brook that flows into the Jordan from the east.","Elijah hid here before being directed to the widow of Zarephath in Sidon.","Miraculous ravens served as God’s couriers here."],"hint":"Secluded brook where ravens fed Elijah bread and meat.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Cherith","The Brook Cherith","Wadi Cherith"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Ancient Waters & Wilderness Waypoints","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
