        16,
        3,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a freshwater spring and pool in lower Jerusalem fed by the waters of the Gihon Spring via King Hezekiah’s underground tunnel. Jesus spat on the ground, made clay with the saliva, anointed the eyes of a man blind from birth, and said to him: "Go, wash in the pool of [...]." The man went, washed, and came back seeing. What pool am I?',
        '"Pool of Samaria","Pool of Bethesda","Pool of Siloam","Pool of Gibeon"'::text[],
        'Pool of Siloam',
