        'THE THREE-CLUE RIDDLE:
Clue 1: I was a spring at the foot of Mount Gilboa where Gideon and his army camped.
Clue 2: My name in Hebrew translates to "Trembling" or "Spring of Trembling."
Clue 3: At my waters, Gideon tested his men by watching how they drank—twenty-two thousand left because they were afraid, and from the remaining ten thousand, only three hundred who lapped water like a dog were selected. What spring am I?',
        '"Spring of Harod","Brook Kishon","Well of Beersheba","Waters of Megiddo"'::text[],
