        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Place","is_typed":true,"clues":["Aramaic name means \"House of Mercy\" (Bethesda) or \"House of Olives\" (Bethzatha).","Excavations near St. Anne’s Church in Jerusalem confirmed its five porticoes.","Contrasted with the Pool of Siloam in John’s Gospel."],"hint":"Five-porched pool by the Sheep Gate in Jerusalem where Jesus healed a 38-year invalid.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Bethesda","Pool of Bethzatha","Bethzatha","The Pool of Bethesda"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Ancient Waters & Wilderness Waypoints","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
