        'bible-riddles',
        17,
        1,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was the mountain ridge in the land of Moriah where Abraham was directed by God to journey for three days to offer his only beloved son Isaac as a burnt offering. On my summit, the angel of the Lord halted the raised knife, a ram caught in a thicket by its horns was sacrificed instead, and Abraham named me Yahweh-Jireh ("The Lord will provide"). A millennium later, Solomon built the Temple upon my threshing floor. What mountain am I?',
        '"Mount Zion","Mount Moriah","Mount Carmel","Mount Sinai"'::text[],
        'Mount Moriah',
        'Mount Moriah was where Abraham prepared to sacrifice Isaac, God provided the ram, and Solomon later constructed the Temple.',
        'Genesis 22:1–14; 2 Chronicles 3:1',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Site of the Akedah (binding of Isaac).","Purchased by David as the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite.","Site of Solomon’s Temple (2 Chronicles 3:1)."],"hint":"Mountain where Abraham offered Isaac and Solomon built the Temple.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Moriah","Mount of the Lord"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Sacred Mountains & Heights","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
