        3,
        'THE DOUBLE-MEANING RIDDLE:
We were two facing mountains in central Canaan framing the ancient city of Shechem. Six tribes stood on one mountain to pronounce blessings for obedience, while six tribes stood on the other to shout solemn curses for disobedience. Joshua built an altar of unhewn stones and wrote a copy of the Law on the mountain of the curse. What are the names of these twin covenant mountains?',
        '"Mount Zion and Mount Moriah","Mount Sinai and Mount Horeb","Mount Carmel and Mount Tabor","Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal"'::text[],
        'Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal',
        'Mount Gerizim was designated for blessings and Mount Ebal for curses as Israel entered the Promised Land.',
        'Deuteronomy 11:29; 27:11–13; Joshua 8:30–35',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Double-Meaning Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Mount Gerizim for blessing (Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Joseph, Benjamin).","Mount Ebal for cursing (Reuben, Gad, Asher, Zebulun, Dan, Naphtali).","Located in the heart of Samaria."],"hint":"Twin mountains of blessing and curse framing Shechem.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Gerizim and Ebal","Mount Ebal and Mount Gerizim","Ebal and Gerizim","Gerizim & Ebal"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Sacred Mountains & Heights","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
