        4,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was an olive-tree-covered ridge east of Jerusalem, separated from the Temple Mount by the steep Kidron Valley. David wept barefoot with his head covered as he climbed me while fleeing Absalom. Jesus wept over Jerusalem from my crest during His triumphal entry, agonized in Gethsemane at my base, ascended into heaven from my slopes, and Zechariah prophesies that His feet will stand on me in the day of the Lord, splitting me in two from east to west. What ridge am I?',
        '"Mount Moriah","Mount of Offense","Mount Zion","Mount of Olives"'::text[],
        'Mount of Olives',
        'The Mount of Olives overlooks Jerusalem, witnessed David’s flight, Christ’s agony and ascension, and is prophesied to split at His return.',
        '2 Samuel 15:30; Zechariah 14:4; Luke 19:37–41; Acts 1:9–12',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The Mount of Olives (Olivet).","Site of the Olivet Discourse (Matthew 24).","Zechariah 14:4 foretells it will split in two creating a great valley."],"hint":"Olive-covered ridge east of Jerusalem where Jesus ascended.","testament":"Both","acceptedAlternatives":["Mount Olivet","The Mount of Olives","Olivet"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Sacred Mountains & Heights","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
