        5,
        'TYPE THE PLACE — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was the highest snow-capped mountain ridge in the far north of Israel, towering over nine thousand feet above sea level at the headwaters of the Jordan River. Psalm 133 compares fraternal unity among brethren to my sweet, heavy morning dew descending upon the mountains of Zion. Christian tradition often identifies my majestic heights as the probable location of the Transfiguration of Jesus Christ. What mountain am I?',
        '"Mount Lebanon","Mount Hermon","Mount Carmel","Mount Tabor"'::text[],
        'Mount Hermon',
        'Mount Hermon is the northern snow-capped mountain famed for its heavy dew in Psalm 133:3 and the probable site of the Transfiguration.',
        'Deuteronomy 3:8–9; Psalm 133:3; Matthew 17:1–2',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Place","is_typed":true,"clues":["Known as Sirion by the Sidonians and Senir by the Amorites (Deuteronomy 3:9).","Northern boundary of the Promised Land conquered by Joshua.","Snowy peaks visible throughout Galilee and the Decapolis."],"hint":"Snowy northern mountain famed in Psalm 133 for its refreshing dew.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Hermon","The Mount Hermon"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Sacred Mountains & Heights","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
