        'bible-riddles',
        18,
        1,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a small Canaanite hill town east of Bethel whose name literally means "The Ruin." When Joshua sent only three thousand men to capture me after the fall of Jericho, my defenders routed them and killed thirty-six Israelites, because Achan had stolen devoted treasures in secret. After Achan was stoned in the valley of Achor, Joshua set an ambush behind me, burned me to the ground, and turned me into a permanent heap of ruins. What city am I?',
        '"Jericho","Bethel","Ai","Gibeon"'::text[],
        'Ai',
        'Ai was the city where Israel was initially defeated due to Achan’s sin, and subsequently conquered through an ambush strategy.',
        'Joshua 7:1–5; 8:1–29',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Joshua’s second military target in Canaan.","Capture involved setting five thousand men in ambush between Bethel and me.","City’s king was hanged on a tree until evening."],"hint":"Small city where Israel was defeated before Joshua ambushed and burned it.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The City of Ai","Hai"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Conquered Cities & Ruins","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
