        'bible-riddles',
        18,
        2,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was the city in Ephraim where the Tabernacle was pitched and the Ark of the Covenant rested for over three centuries after the conquest of Canaan. Hannah prayed silently here for a child, Samuel heard God’s call here at night while lying near the Ark, and Eli fell backward from his seat and broke his neck when news arrived that my Ark had been captured by Philistines. Jeremiah later warned Jerusalem: "Go now to my place that was in [...], and see what I did to it for the evil of my people Israel." What city am I?',
        '"Shiloh","Shechem","Bethel","Mizpah"'::text[],
        'Shiloh',
        'Shiloh was the sanctuary home of the Tabernacle during the Judges until the Ark was captured and God abandoned the city.',
        'Joshua 18:1; 1 Samuel 1:3; 3:1–21; 4:12–18; Jeremiah 7:12–14',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["First permanent religious center for the Tabernacle in the Promised Land.","Hophni and Phinehas corrupted the offerings here.","Destroyed by Philistines after the battle of Ebenezer."],"hint":"City where Samuel grew up in the Tabernacle and Eli died; later destroyed.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Silo"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Conquered Cities & Ruins","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
