        'bible-riddles',
        18,
        3,
        'WHERE AM I?
Originally called Luz, I was the place where Jacob slept on a stone pillow and dreamed of a ladder set up on earth with its top reaching to heaven, and the angels of God ascending and descending on it. Awaking in awe, Jacob exclaimed, "How awesome is this place! This is none other than the house of God, and this is the gate of heaven," and poured oil upon the stone. Centuries later, Jeroboam turned me into a center of apostasy by erecting one of his golden calves here. What city am I?',
        '"Bethel","Peniel","Beersheba","Shechem"'::text[],
        'Bethel',
        'Bethel ("House of God"), formerly Luz, was where Jacob saw the ladder to heaven and Jeroboam later erected a golden calf.',
        'Genesis 28:10–22; 35:1–7; 1 Kings 12:28–33',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Name means \"House of God\" in Hebrew.","Jacob returned here by God’s command in Genesis 35.","Condemned by the prophets as Beth-aven (\"House of Iniquity\") due to Jeroboam’s calf."],"hint":"City where Jacob saw the ladder to heaven, meaning \"House of God.\"","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Beth-el","House of God"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Conquered Cities & Ruins","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
