        'bible-riddles',
        18,
        4,
        'THE THREE-CLUE RIDDLE:
Clue 1: I was an ancient Hivite royal city whose inhabitants sent ambassadors to Joshua disguised in worn-out sacks, patched sandals, and moldy bread.
Clue 2: We tricked Israel into making a binding covenant of peace without inquiring of the Lord.
Clue 3: When the deception was discovered, Joshua spared our lives but made us woodcutters and water carriers for the house of God forever; later, the sun stood still over me during battle. What city am I?',
        '"Kiriath-jearim","Chephirah","Beeroth","Gibeon"'::text[],
        'Gibeon',
        'Gibeon tricked Joshua into a covenant of peace using moldy bread and worn sandals, and was the site where the sun stood still in battle.',
        'Joshua 9:3–27; 10:1–14',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["City of the crafty Gibeonites.","Five Amorite kings banded together to attack me for making peace with Joshua.","Site of the legendary miraculous long day when the sun stood still."],"hint":"City that deceived Joshua with moldy bread; where the sun stood still.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["City of Gibeon"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Conquered Cities & Ruins","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
