        18,
        5,
        'TYPE THE PLACE — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was the capital city of the ruthless Assyrian Empire on the east bank of the Tigris River, described by the prophet Nahum as "the bloody city, all full of lies and plunder." An ancient metropolis requiring three days to cross on foot, my king and people repented in sackcloth and ashes at the eight-word warning of a reluctant Hebrew prophet. However, a century later, Nahum and Zephaniah prophesied my final inundation and desolate ruin. What city am I?',
        '"Susa","Nineveh","Calneh","Babylon"'::text[],
        'Nineveh',
        'Nineveh was the Assyrian capital that repented under Jonah’s preaching, but was later completely destroyed as prophesied by Nahum.',
        'Jonah 3:1–10; Nahum 1:1; 3:1–7; Zephaniah 2:13–15',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Place","is_typed":true,"clues":["Spared in the book of Jonah when 120,000 who could not discern their right hand from their left repented.","Destroyed in 612 BC by a coalition of Medes and Babylonians fulfilling Nahum.","Located opposite modern Mosul, Iraq."],"hint":"Assyrian capital city that repented in sackcloth under Jonah’s preaching.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Nineve"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Conquered Cities & Ruins","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
