        'bible-riddles',
        19,
        1,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a Roman administrative city located at the foot of Mount Hermon near the headwaters of the Jordan River, rebuilt and renamed by the tetrarch Herod Philip in honor of Caesar. In our district, Jesus asked His disciples, "Who do people say that the Son of Man is?", prompting Simon Peter’s famous confession: "You are the Christ, the Son of the living God." What city am I?',
        '"Caesarea Philippi","Capernaum","Caesarea Maritima","Bethsaida"'::text[],
        'Caesarea Philippi',
        'Caesarea Philippi was the northern district where Peter confessed Jesus as the Christ, the Son of the Living God.',
        'Matthew 16:13–20; Mark 8:27–30',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Not to be confused with Caesarea Maritima on the Mediterranean coast.","Site where Jesus declared: \"On this rock I will build my church, and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.\"","Ancient center of Pan worship (Paneas)."],"hint":"Northern city where Peter declared: \"You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.\"","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Caesarea-Philippi","Cesarea Philippi"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"New Testament Waypoints & Ports","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
