        'bible-riddles',
        19,
        2,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a major port city on the Aegean Sea in northwest Asia Minor (Mysia) near ancient Troy. In this city, the Apostle Paul received his famous night vision of a man standing and urging him, "Come over to Macedonia and help us," prompting the first European missionary journey. On a later visit, Paul preached here until midnight and raised the young man Eutychus from the dead. What port am I?',
        '"Miletus","Pergamum","Troas","Ephesus"'::text[],
        'Troas',
        'Troas was the Aegean port where Paul saw the Macedonian vision and later raised Eutychus from the dead.',
        'Acts 16:8–10; 20:5–12; 2 Timothy 4:13',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Full name: Alexandria Troas.","Luke joins the narrative here as indicated by the \"we\" passage in Acts 16:10.","Paul left his winter cloak and parchments here with Carpus (2 Timothy 4:13)."],"hint":"Aegean seaport where Paul saw the vision of the Macedonian man calling for help.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Alexandria Troas"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"New Testament Waypoints & Ports","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
