        'bible-riddles',
        19,
        3,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a rocky hill northwest of the Acropolis in Athens where the supreme judicial council of the city convened. Epicurean and Stoic philosophers brought Paul to me, asking, "May we know what this new teaching is that you are presenting?" Standing in my midst, Paul addressed the council, declaring that he had found an altar with the inscription: "TO THE UNKNOWN GOD." What place am I?',
        '"The Areopagus / Mars Hill","The Acropolis","The Pnyx","The Agora"'::text[],
        'The Areopagus / Mars Hill',
        'The Areopagus (Mars Hill) in Athens was the council where Paul preached about the "Unknown God" and the resurrection of Christ.',
        'Acts 17:19–34',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Known in Greek as the Areopagus (Hill of Ares) and in Latin as Mars Hill.","Paul quoted Greek poets here: \"In him we live and move and have our being.\"","Dionysius the Areopagite and a woman named Damaris were converted here."],"hint":"Athenian council hill where Paul preached concerning the \"Unknown God.\"","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Areopagus","Mars Hill","Mars’ Hill","The Areopagus"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"New Testament Waypoints & Ports","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
