        'bible-riddles',
        19,
        4,
        'THE THREE-CLUE RIDDLE:
Clue 1: I was an island in the central Mediterranean south of Sicily where a grain ship carrying 276 passengers was shipwrecked in a violent northeastern storm (Euroclydon).
Clue 2: My native inhabitants showed extraordinary kindness by kindling a fire in the rain and cold.
Clue 3: When a deadly viper latched onto Paul’s hand as he gathered sticks, he shook it into the fire unharmed; Paul then healed the father of Publius, the chief man of our island. What island am I?',
        '"Patmos","Malta / Melita","Crete","Cyprus"'::text[],
        'Malta / Melita',
        'Melita (modern Malta) was the island where Paul was shipwrecked, shook off a poisonous viper into the fire, and healed Publius’ father.',
        'Acts 27:39–44; 28:1–11',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Known in Acts as Melita (modern Malta).","Island inhabitants first thought Paul was a murderer, then decided he was a god.","Ship spent three months wintering here before boarding the Castor and Pollux."],"hint":"Island where Paul was shipwrecked and shook off a viper into the fire.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Malta","Melita","Island of Malta","Island of Melita"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"New Testament Waypoints & Ports","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l19-c5',
        'bible-riddles',
        19,
        5,
        'TYPE THE PLACE — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was a prominent Greco-Roman metropolis on the Orontes River in Syria, the third largest city of the Roman Empire. When believers scattered after Stephen’s martyrdom began preaching the Lord Jesus to Greek-speaking Gentiles here, a great number believed. Barnabas brought Saul from Tarsus to teach the church for a whole year. In this city, the disciples were for the very first time called "Christians." What city am I?',
        '"Antioch in Syria","Alexandria","Damascus","Antioch of Pisidia"'::text[],
        'Antioch in Syria',
