        1,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a valley near Jericho whose name means "Trouble." Here, Achan, who took devoted gold, silver, and a beautiful mantle from Shinar from Jericho, was stoned and burned with his household under a great heap of stones. In Hosea 2:15, God promises a future redemption, transforming me from a place of judgment into "a door of hope." What valley am I?',
        '"Valley of Elah","Valley of Jezreel","Valley of Hinnom","Valley of Achor"'::text[],
        'Valley of Achor',
        'The Valley of Achor ("Valley of Trouble") was where Achan was stoned, and which Hosea prophesied would become a "door of hope."',
        'Joshua 7:24–26; Hosea 2:15; Isaiah 65:10',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Joshua said to Achan: \"Why have you brought trouble on us? The Lord will trouble you today.\"","Named the Valley of Achor.","Isaiah 65:10 promises it will become a resting place for herds."],"hint":"Valley of Trouble where Achan was stoned, prophesied as a \"door of hope.\"","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Achor","The Valley of Achor"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Mysterious Valleys & Graves","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
