        'WHERE AM I?
I was an ominous valley in exile into which the hand of the Lord transported the prophet Ezekiel in the Spirit. The valley floor was covered with a vast multitude of skeletal bones that were "very dry." When the prophet was commanded to prophesy to the dry bones and then to the four winds, breath entered them, and they came to life, standing on their feet as an exceedingly great army symbolizing the restoration of the house of Israel. What valley am I?',
        '"Valley of the Shadow of Death","Valley of Vision","Valley of Dry Bones","Valley of Decision"'::text[],
        'Valley of Dry Bones',
        'The Valley of Dry Bones was where Ezekiel prophesied life and the Spirit of God into a field of dry bones representing dead Israel.',
        'Ezekiel 37:1–14',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The valley of dry bones in Ezekiel 37.","The bones cried: \"Our bones are dried up, and our hope is lost; we are indeed cut off.\"","God promised: \"I will open your graves and raise you from your graves, O my people.\""],"hint":"Valley where Ezekiel saw dry skeletal bones come together and revive.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Valley of Dry Bones","Valley of the Dry Bones"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Mysterious Valleys & Graves","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
