        3,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was a broad valley in the desert of Tekoa where King Jehoshaphat and the people of Judah gathered after God miraculously threw the invading confederacy of Moab, Ammon, and Mount Seir into mutual self-destruction before a choir singing praises. It took three days to collect all the plunder of jewels, clothing, and precious vessels, and on the fourth day they assembled in me to bless Yahweh, giving me a name that means "The Valley of Blessing." What valley am I?',
        '"Valley of Rephaim","Valley of Beracah","Valley of Jehoshaphat","Valley of Achor"'::text[],
        'Valley of Beracah',
        'The Valley of Beracah ("Valley of Blessing") was named because Judah assembled there to bless the Lord after the miraculous defeat of Moab and Ammon.',
        '2 Chronicles 20:20–26',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The Valley of Beracah (Berakah).","The choir sang: \"Give thanks to the Lord, for his steadfast love endures forever.\"","Located in the Judean wilderness south of Bethlehem."],"hint":"Valley of Blessing where Jehoshaphat’s army praised God after three days of gathering spoil.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Beracah","Valley of Berakah","The Valley of Blessing"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Mysterious Valleys & Graves","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
