        4,
        'WHERE AM I?
I was an ominous ravine south and west of Jerusalem associated with child sacrifices by fire to Molech during the apostasy of Ahaz and Manasseh. King Josiah thoroughly defiled my high places of Topheth with human bones so no one could pass their child through the fire. Because perpetual fires burned city refuse and carcasses here, my Greek name Gehenna became the vivid New Testament metaphor used by Jesus for hellfire. What valley am I?',
        '"Valley of Hinnom / Gehenna","Valley of Kidron","Valley of Elah","Valley of Achor"'::text[],
        'Valley of Hinnom / Gehenna',
        'The Valley of the Son of Hinnom (Gehenna) was the site of Topheth and child sacrifice, which Jesus used to depict the final judgment.',
        'Joshua 15:8; 2 Kings 23:10; Jeremiah 7:31–32; Mark 9:43–48',
        '{"riddle_type":"Where Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The Valley of Hinnom (Gei-Hinnom / Gehenna).","Jeremiah prophesied it would be renamed the Valley of Slaughter.","Jesus spoke of Gehenna as a place where \"their worm does not die and the fire is not quenched.\""],"hint":"Jerusalem valley of child sacrifice to Molech whose name became Gehenna (hell).","testament":"Both","acceptedAlternatives":["Valley of Hinnom","Gehenna","Valley of Ben Hinnom","Valley of Ben-Hinnom"],"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places of Mystery","level_theme":"Mysterious Valleys & Graves","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
