I was a plot of clay land just outside Jerusalem originally known as the Potter’s Field. Purchased by the chief priests using the thirty pieces of silver that Judas Iscariot threw into the temple sanctuary, I was designated as a burial place for destitute strangers and foreigners who died in the holy city. What is my Aramaic name, explicitly recorded in Matthew 27:8 and Acts 1:19, which translates as "The Field of Blood"?',
        '"Gethsemane","Akeldama","Golgotha","Bethany"'::text[],
        'Akeldama',
