        'Genesis 5:21–24; Hebrews 11:5; Jude 1:14–15',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Father of Methuselah who lived 969 years.","Hebrews 11:5 commends me for having pleased God before being taken up.","Jude 14–15 quotes my ancient prophecy concerning the Lord coming with ten thousands of holy ones."],"hint":"Seventh from Adam who walked with God and did not see death.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Henoch"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Patriarchs & Matriarchs","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
