        'TYPE TWO ANSWERS — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
When dying Jacob blessed the two Egyptian-born sons of Joseph in Genesis 48, Joseph placed the firstborn on Jacob’s right hand and the younger on his left. However, Jacob deliberately crossed his hands, laying his right hand on the younger brother and his left on the firstborn, prophesying that the younger would become greater and his offspring a multitude of nations. What are the names of these two sons of Joseph (firstborn and younger)?',
        '"Perez and Zerah","Manasseh and Ephraim","Ephraim and Manasseh","Gershom and Eliezer"'::text[],
        'Manasseh and Ephraim',
        'Joseph’s two sons were Manasseh (firstborn) and Ephraim (younger); Jacob crossed his hands to bestow the firstborn blessing on Ephraim.',
        'Genesis 41:50–52; 48:1–20',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type Two Answers","is_typed":true,"clues":["Born in Egypt to Joseph by Asenath, daughter of Potiphera priest of On.","Older son’s name means \"God has made me forget all my hardship.\"","Younger son’s name means \"God has made me fruitful in the land of my affliction.\"","Their two names became major tribal territories in Israel replacing Joseph."],"hint":"Two sons of Joseph over whom Jacob crossed his hands to give the primary blessing to the younger.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Ephraim and Manasseh","Manasseh & Ephraim","Ephraim & Manasseh","Manasseh, Ephraim"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Patriarchs & Matriarchs","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
