        1,
        'THE THREE-CLUE CHALLENGE:
Clue 1: I was beating out wheat in a winepress in Ophrah to hide it from Midianite raiders when an angel greeted me: "The Lord is with you, O mighty man of valor!"
Clue 2: I tore down my father’s altar of Baal and the Asherah beside it by night, earning the nickname Jerubbaal ("Let Baal contend against him").
Clue 3: I confirmed God’s calling through a fleece of wool that was soaked while the ground was dry, and then dry while the ground was wet. Who am I?',
        '"Samson","Gideon","Jephthah","Barak"'::text[],
