        'THE THREE-CLUE CHALLENGE:
Clue 1: I was Solomon’s son who traveled to Shechem to be crowned king over all Israel.
Clue 2: When the northern tribes asked for relief from heavy taxes, I rejected the counsel of the older elders and listened to the young men who grew up with me, boasting: "My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add to your yoke; my father disciplined you with whips, but I will discipline you with scorpions."
