        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was the longest-reigning monarch in the history of Judah, ruling for fifty-five years in Jerusalem. I rebuilt the high places my father Hezekiah had torn down, erected altars for Baal, sacrificed my own son in the fire in the Valley of Ben-Hinnom, practiced sorcery, set up a carved idol in the house of the Lord, and shed very much innocent blood. Captured by the king of Assyria with hooks and bronze chains and dragged to Babylon, I humbled myself greatly before God in my distress, prayed, and was miraculously restored to my throne in Jerusalem, where I removed foreign gods from the temple. Who am I?',
        '"Manasseh","Ahaz","Jehoram","Amon"'::text[],
