        'THE THREE-CLUE CHALLENGE:
Clue 1: I served as cupbearer to King Artaxerxes in the Persian winter palace at Susa.
Clue 2: When I wept over news that the walls of Jerusalem were broken down and its gates burned with fire, the king granted me letters and timber to rebuild the city.
Clue 3: Despite armed threats and mockery from Sanballat, Tobiah, and Geshem, my builders labored with a trowel in one hand and a weapon in the other, completing the broken walls in just fifty-two days. Who am I?',
