        24,
        5,
        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was a descendant of Aaron the high priest and a priest-scribe skilled in the Law of Moses that Yahweh had given. In 458 BC, King Artaxerxes granted me a royal decree to lead a second return of Jewish exiles from Babylon to Jerusalem. Scripture records that I had set my heart to study the Law of the Lord, and to do it and to teach his statutes and rules in Israel. When I discovered pervasive intermarriage with foreign idolaters, I tore my tunic and mantle, pulled hair from my head and beard, and sat down appalled until the evening sacrifice. Who am I?',
        '"Zadok","Nehemiah","Hilkiah","Ezra"'::text[],
        'Ezra',
        'Ezra was the priestly scribe who led the second return from Babylon, instituted national repentance, and taught God’s Law.',
        'Ezra 7:1–10, 27–28; 8:21–23; 9:1–15; Nehemiah 8:1–8',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["Descendant of Phinehas and Zadok.","Refused a royal military escort across the desert, declaring: \"The hand of our God is for good on all who seek him.\"","Stood upon a wooden pulpit reading the Law of Moses to all the people from daybreak until midday (Nehemiah 8)."],"hint":"Priest and scribe who set his heart to study, practice, and teach the Law of God.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Esdras","Ezra the Scribe","Ezra the Priest"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Exilic & Post-Exilic Figures","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
