        25,
        2,
        'THE THREE-CLUE CHALLENGE:
Clue 1: I was a Levite from Cyprus whose original name was Joseph, but the Apostles renamed me with a title meaning "Son of Encouragement."
Clue 2: I sold a field I owned and brought the money and laid it at the Apostles’ feet, modeling radical generosity.
Clue 3: When the Jerusalem church feared the newly converted persecutor Saul, I vouched for him; later, I traveled to Antioch, retrieved Saul from Tarsus, and set off with him on the First Missionary Journey. Who am I?',
        '"Barnabas","Titus","Timothy","Silas"'::text[],
        'Barnabas',
        'Barnabas (Joseph of Cyprus, the Son of Encouragement) sponsored Paul before the apostles and partnered in the First Missionary Journey.',
        'Acts 4:36–37; 9:26–27; 11:22–26; 13:1–4; 15:36–40',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Cousin of John Mark.","Parted company with Paul over taking John Mark on the second journey.","Described in Acts 11:24 as \"a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and of faith.\""],"hint":"Levite from Cyprus nicknamed the \"Son of Encouragement.\"","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Joseph Barnabas"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Apostolic Witnesses & Martyrs","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
