        25,
        4,
        'THE THREE-CLUE CHALLENGE:
Clue 1: I was a native of Alexandria, Egypt, who arrived in Ephesus described as an eloquent man, mighty in the Scriptures.
Clue 2: Fervent in spirit, I taught accurately the things concerning Jesus, though I knew only the baptism of John.
Clue 3: Priscilla and Aquila heard me speaking boldly in the synagogue, took me aside, and explained to me the way of God more accurately; I then crossed to Corinth and powerfully refuted Jewish opponents in public, showing by the Scriptures that Jesus was the Christ. Who am I?',
        '"Tychicus","Barnabas","Apollos","Timothy"'::text[],
        'Apollos',
        'Apollos was the eloquent Alexandrian orator instructed more accurately by Priscilla and Aquila who watered the church in Corinth.',
        'Acts 18:24–28; 1 Corinthians 3:4–6; 4:6; Titus 3:13',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Believers in Corinth formed factions around Paul, Cephas, Christ, and me.","Paul wrote in 1 Corinthians 3:6: \"I planted, [...] watered, but God gave the growth.\"","Titus 3:13 urges believers to speed me on my journey."],"hint":"Eloquent Alexandrian preacher instructed more accurately by Priscilla and Aquila.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Apollo"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Apostolic Witnesses & Martyrs","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
