        25,
        5,
        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was an earthly half-brother of Jesus who did not believe in Him during His earthly ministry. Following His resurrection, Jesus appeared personally to me (1 Corinthians 15:7), and I became the foremost leader and pillar of the early church in Jerusalem. I presided over the historic Jerusalem Council in Acts 15, declaring the final consensus regarding Gentile converts, authored a practical New Testament epistle on living faith and trials, and was nicknamed "the Just" and "Camel Knees" for my ceaseless intercession. Who am I?',
        '"Jude","James the Lord’s Brother","James the Son of Zebedee","James the Son of Alphaeus"'::text[],
        'James the Lord’s Brother',
        'James the brother of Jesus was converted by the resurrected Christ, led the Jerusalem Council, and wrote the Epistle of James.',
        'Matthew 13:55; Acts 15:13–21; 1 Corinthians 15:7; Galatians 1:19; James 1:1',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["Referred to by Paul in Galatians 1:19 as \"James the Lord’s brother.\"","Referred to as a pillar alongside Cephas and John in Galatians 2:9.","Martyred in Jerusalem by high priest Ananus around 62 AD according to Josephus."],"hint":"Half-brother of Jesus who led the Jerusalem Council and wrote the Epistle of James.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["James","James the Just","James the Brother of Jesus","James the Brother of the Lord"],"stage":5,"stage_title":"The Three-Clue Challenge","level_theme":"Apostolic Witnesses & Martyrs","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
