        'bible-riddles',
        26,
        1,
        'TYPE TWO ANSWERS:
We were two Hebrew midwives operating in Egypt during the Pharaoh’s decree of genocide against infant Hebrew boys. Because we feared God more than the king of Egypt, we defied Pharaoh’s direct command and allowed the male babies to live, telling the king that Hebrew women were vigorous and gave birth before the midwife arrived. Scripture notes that God dealt well with us and gave us our own families. What are our two biblical names?',
        '"Jochebed and Miriam","Shiphrah and Puah","Leah and Rachel","Tryphena and Tryphosa"'::text[],
        'Shiphrah and Puah',
        'Shiphrah and Puah were the courageous Hebrew midwives who feared God and spared baby boys from Pharaoh’s murderous decree.',
        'Exodus 1:15–21',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type Two Answers","is_typed":true,"clues":["Names recorded in Exodus 1:15.","Hebrew names: שִׁפְרָה (meaning \"beautiful\") and פּוּעָה (meaning \"splendid/crying out\").","Exemplified godly civil disobedience against tyranny."],"hint":"Two courageous midwives in Exodus 1 who saved Hebrew male babies.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Shiphrah & Puah","Puah and Shiphrah","Shiphrah, Puah","Siphrah and Puah"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Forgotten Pentateuch & History Names","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
