        'bible-riddles',
        26,
        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was the spirited daughter of the great explorer Caleb who was offered as a bride to whoever would attack and capture the Canaanite fortress of Kiriath-sepher (Debir). When my cousin Othniel captured the city and married me, I dismounted from my donkey before my father and requested a wedding blessing: "You have given me the land of the Negeb; give me also springs of water." And Caleb gave me the upper and lower springs. Who am I?',
        '"Deborah","Jael","Achsah","Hoglah"'::text[],
        'Achsah',
        'Achsah was Caleb’s daughter who married Othniel and petitioned her father for upper and lower water springs in the dry Negeb.',
        'Joshua 15:16–19; Judges 1:12–15',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Daughter of Caleb son of Jephunneh.","Wife of Othniel, Israel’s first judge.","Secured both northern and southern freshwater springs."],"hint":"Caleb’s daughter who asked her father for springs of water.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Acsa"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Forgotten Pentateuch & History Names","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
