        'bible-riddles',
        26,
        4,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a valiant warrior from Kabzeel, son of Jehoiada the priest, who commanded David’s personal bodyguard of Cherethites and Pelethites. Among my legendary exploits: I struck down two royal champions of Moab, went down into a pit on a snowy day and killed a lion with my bare hands, and wrested a spear like a weaver’s beam out of an eight-foot Egyptian giant’s hand and killed him with his own spear. Under King Solomon, I executed Adonijah, Joab, and Shimei, becoming supreme commander of the royal army. Who am I?',
        '"Abishai","Ittai","Asahel","Benaiah"'::text[],
        'Benaiah',
        'Benaiah son of Jehoiada was David’s bodyguard commander who killed a lion in a snowy pit and became Solomon’s top general.',
        '2 Samuel 23:20–23; 1 Kings 2:25–46',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Jehoiada of Kabzeel.","Killed a lion in a pit on a snowy day.","Succeeded Joab as supreme commander of Solomon’s military."],"hint":"Warrior who killed a lion in a snowy pit and became Solomon’s army commander.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Benaiah son of Jehoiada"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Forgotten Pentateuch & History Names","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
