        'bible-riddles',
        26,
        5,
        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was a concubine of King Saul, daughter of Aiah, who bore him two sons, Armoni and Mephibosheth. When a three-year famine struck Israel because Saul had broken the ancient covenant by slaughtering the Gibeonites, David delivered seven sons of Saul to the Gibeonites, who hanged them on the mountain before the Lord. In an extraordinary vigil of maternal devotion, I spread sackcloth upon a rock from the beginning of harvest until the autumn rains poured from the sky, suffering neither the birds of the air to rest on their corpses by day nor the beasts of the field by night. Moved by my grief, David retrieved their bones and gave them honorable royal burial. Who am I?',
        '"Michal","Rizpah","Abigail","Merab"'::text[],
        'Rizpah',
        'Rizpah daughter of Aiah kept a heroic vigil over the exposed bodies of her sons and relatives, guarding them from vultures and wild beasts.',
        '2 Samuel 3:7; 21:8–14',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["Daughter of Aiah; Saul’s royal concubine.","Guarded seven hanging corpses from scavengers for nearly six months.","Her name is recorded in 2 Samuel 3:7 and 21:8–14."],"hint":"Saul’s concubine who kept a heroic vigil on sackcloth over her dead sons.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Rizpah daughter of Aiah","Rispa"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Forgotten Pentateuch & History Names","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
