        27,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was the devoted personal scribe and disciple of the prophet Jeremiah. When Jeremiah was barred from the temple, I wrote down all the words of the Lord from his dictation onto a leather scroll and read them aloud to all the people in the temple on a fast day. When King Jehoiakim cut the scroll with a penknife and threw it into his brazier fire, Jeremiah and I hid, and I penned an expanded second scroll at Jeremiah’s dictation. Who am I?',
        '"Baruch","Gedaliah","Seraiah","Ebed-Melech"'::text[],
        'Baruch',
        'Baruch son of Neriah was Jeremiah’s faithful scribe who penned the prophetic scroll that King Jehoiakim burned.',
        'Jeremiah 36:1–32; 45:1–5',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Neriah, grandson of Mahseiah.","Lamented: \"Woe is me! For the Lord has added sorrow to my pain\" (Jeremiah 45:3).","God gave him a personal promise that his life would be spared wherever he went."],"hint":"Jeremiah’s faithful scribe who wrote down his dictated scrolls.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Baruch son of Neriah"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Obscure Monarchy & Prophet Associates","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
