        'bible-riddles',
        27,
        2,
        'WHO AM I?
I was appointed governor of the destitute Jewish remnant remaining in Judah by Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon after the destruction of Jerusalem in 586 BC. Setting up my administrative capital at Mizpah, I encouraged the frightened people to stay, harvest summer fruits, and serve the king of Babylon in peace. Despite being warned by Johanan that Baalis king of the Ammonites had sent an assassin, I refused to believe it, and was murdered at a banquet in Mizpah by Ishmael son of Nethaniah. Who am I?',
        '"Gedaliah","Ishmael","Pashhur","Johanan"'::text[],
        'Gedaliah',
        'Gedaliah son of Ahikam was the Babylonian-appointed governor of Judah assassinated at Mizpah by Ishmael.',
        '2 Kings 25:22–25; Jeremiah 40:5–41:3',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Ahikam, son of Shaphan.","His father Ahikam had previously protected Jeremiah from execution (Jeremiah 26:24).","His assassination prompted the Fast of Gedaliah in the Jewish calendar."],"hint":"Governor of Judah after Jerusalem’s fall murdered at Mizpah by Ishmael.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Gedaliah son of Ahikam","Godolias"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Obscure Monarchy & Prophet Associates","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
