        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an ascetic nomad, son of Rechab, who met King Jehu riding in his chariot toward Samaria to purge the dynasty of Ahab. When Jehu asked, "Is your heart right with my heart, as my heart is with yours?", I answered, "It is." Jehu gave me his hand, pulled me up into his chariot, and said, "Come with me, and see my zeal for the Lord." Two centuries later, Jeremiah commended my descendants because they strictly obeyed my commands never to drink wine, build houses, sow seed, or plant vineyards. Who am I?',
        '"Rechab","Jehonadab","Obadiah","Jehu"'::text[],
        'Jehonadab',
        'Jehonadab son of Rechab joined Jehu in wiping out Baal worship, and his nomadic descendants the Rechabites were praised for steadfast fidelity.',
        '2 Kings 10:15–23; Jeremiah 35:1–19',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Jonadab (Jehonadab) son of Rechab.","Helped Jehu eradicate Baal worship from Samaria.","God promised that a descendant of Rechab would never lack a man to stand before Him forever."],"hint":"Founder of the wine-abstaining Rechabites who rode with King Jehu.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Jonadab","Jehonadab son of Rechab","Jonadab son of Rechab"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Obscure Monarchy & Prophet Associates","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
