        'bible-riddles',
        27,
        4,
        'THE BIBLICAL RELATIONSHIP RIDDLE:
I was the brother of the scribe Baruch and the royal quartermaster of King Zedekiah. When the last king of Judah traveled to Babylon in the fourth year of his reign, the prophet Jeremiah gave me a scroll containing all the divine judgments destined against Babylon. Jeremiah instructed me that upon arriving in Babylon, I must read the scroll aloud, tie a heavy stone to it, cast it into the midst of the Euphrates River, and declare: "Thus shall Babylon sink, and never rise again!" Who am I?',
        '"Pashhur","Hananiah","Baruch","Seraiah"'::text[],
        'Seraiah',
        'Seraiah, brother of Baruch, threw the scroll of doom into the Euphrates to enact Babylon’s permanent sinking.',
        'Jeremiah 51:59–64',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Biblical Relationship Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Neriah, son of Mahseiah.","Royal quartermaster (officer of the rest).","Enacted the prophetic sinking of Babylon in Jeremiah 51:59–64."],"hint":"Baruch’s brother who threw the prophecy scroll tied to a stone into the Euphrates.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Seraiah son of Neriah","Saraias"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Obscure Monarchy & Prophet Associates","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
