        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was not a professional prophet nor the son of a prophet, but a rural herdsman and a nipper (grower) of sycamore-fig trees from Tekoa in Judah. God called me to leave my sheep and travel north to the royal sanctuary of Bethel in Israel to proclaim divine judgment against economic injustice and empty religious ritual during the prosperous reign of Jeroboam II. Amaziah the priest of Bethel told me to flee back to Judah, but I prophesied the collapse of his house and the exile of Israel. Who am I?',
        '"Micah","Hosea","Habakkuk","Amos"'::text[],
        'Amos',
        'Amos was the shepherd and dresser of sycamore figs from Tekoa who denounced injustice at Bethel.',
        'Amos 1:1; 5:24; 7:10–17; 8:1–2',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Proclaimed: \"Let justice roll down like waters, and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream.\"","Saw five visions of judgment including a swarm of locusts, devouring fire, a plumb line, and a basket of summer fruit.","Third of the Twelve Minor Prophets."],"hint":"Herdsman and dresser of sycamore figs from Tekoa called to prophesy.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Prophet Amos"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Minor Prophets & Their Circumstances","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
