        2,
        'THE BIBLICAL RELATIONSHIP RIDDLE:
I was commanded by the Lord to take "a wife of whoredom and have children of whoredom," marrying a promiscuous woman named Gomer daughter of Diblaim, as a living parabolic dramatization of Israel’s spiritual adultery against Yahweh. Even after she deserted me for other lovers, God commanded me: "Go again, love a woman who is loved by another man and is an adulteress," and I bought her back for fifteen shekels of silver and a homer and a lethech of barley. Who am I?',
        '"Amos","Zechariah","Joel","Hosea"'::text[],
        'Hosea',
        'Hosea married unfaithful Gomer and later redeemed her from slavery to illustrate God’s unconditional covenant love for apostate Israel.',
        'Hosea 1:1–9; 3:1–3; 4:6',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Biblical Relationship Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Named my children Jezreel, Lo-ruhamah (\"No Mercy\"), and Lo-ammi (\"Not My People\").","Prophesied: \"My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge.\"","First of the Twelve Minor Prophets."],"hint":"Prophet commanded to marry an unfaithful wife named Gomer.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Osee"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Minor Prophets & Their Circumstances","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
