        28,
        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an introspective prophet of Judah who wrestled deeply with God concerning why the righteous suffer while the wicked flourish. Stationing myself upon my watchtower to see what God would speak to me, I was told: "Write the vision; make it plain on tablets, so he may run who reads it... the righteous shall live by his faith." My book concludes with a triumphant hymn of trust even if the fig tree does not blossom and there are no cattle in the stalls. Who am I?',
        '"Zephaniah","Habakkuk","Nahum","Malachi"'::text[],
        'Habakkuk',
        'Habakkuk stood on his watchtower questioning God’s providence, receiving the revelation that "the righteous shall live by his faith."',
        'Habakkuk 1:1–2:4; 3:17–19',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Wrestled with God’s use of the ruthless Babylonians (Chaldeans) as an instrument of judgment.","Key verse Habakkuk 2:4 quoted in Romans 1:17, Galatians 3:11, and Hebrews 10:38.","Concludes: \"God, the Lord, is my strength; he makes my feet like the deer’s.\""],"hint":"Prophet on the watchtower who declared \"the righteous shall live by faith.\"","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Habacuc"],"stage":6,"stage_title":"Forgotten Names","level_theme":"Minor Prophets & Their Circumstances","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
