        'WHO AM I?
I was a post-exilic prophet who arrived in Jerusalem in 520 BC when work on the Second Temple had been stalled for sixteen years while the returnees built their own paneled homes. I rebuked the nation: "Is it a time for you yourselves to dwell in your paneled houses, while this house lies in ruins? Consider your ways!" My four concise sermons inspired Zerubbabel and Joshua to resume construction within twenty-three days. Who am I?',
        '"Zechariah","Malachi","Haggai","Obadiah"'::text[],
        'Haggai',
