        'bible-riddles',
        29,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a righteous and devout elderly man living in Jerusalem waiting for the consolation of Israel, upon whom the Holy Spirit rested. It had been revealed to me by the Spirit that I would not see death before I had seen the Lord’s Christ. Guided by the Spirit into the temple when Mary and Joseph brought in the infant Jesus, I took the child into my arms, blessed God, and sang the Nunc Dimittis: "Lord, now you are letting your servant depart in peace." Who am I?',
        '"Simeon","Cleopas","Nicodemus","Zacharias"'::text[],
        'Simeon',
        'Simeon was the devout Jerusalem elder promised by the Holy Spirit that he would not die before holding the infant Messiah.',
