        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a blind beggar sitting by the roadside outside Jericho. When I heard the commotion that Jesus of Nazareth was passing by, I cried out loudly: "Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!" Though many strictly rebuked me to keep quiet, I cried out all the more. When Jesus stopped and summoned me, I threw off my cloak, sprang up, and came to Him; when He asked what I wanted, I replied: "Rabboni, let me recover my sight." Who am I?',
        '"Lazarus","Malchus","Bartimaeus","Zacchaeus"'::text[],
