        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was a prominent synagogue ruler in Corinth who, along with my entire household, believed in the Lord after hearing Paul preach. When Sosthenes succeeded me and an anti-Christian mob dragged Sosthenes before the Roman proconsul Gallio, Gallio refused to judge Jewish religious matters. Paul personally baptized me in Corinth, as he specifically recalls in 1 Corinthians 1:14: "I thank God that I baptized none of you except [...] and Gaius." Who am I?',
