        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a deaconess/servant of the church at Cenchreae, the eastern port of Corinth. In Romans 16:1–2, the Apostle Paul formally commends me to the Roman church, urging them to receive me in the Lord in a manner worthy of the saints and assist me in whatever matter I might need, for I had been a patron and helper of many, including Paul himself. Church tradition identifies me as the courier who carried Paul’s Epistle to the Romans across the sea to Rome. Who am I?',
