        'WHO AM I?
I am mentioned in Romans 16:23 alongside Erastus, the city treasurer of Corinth. While Tertius had just introduced himself as the scribe who wrote down the letter and Gaius as the host of the whole church, I am simply and tenderly described by Paul with a Latin name meaning "Fourth": "[...] a brother greets you." Who am I?',
        '"Tertius","Secundus","Quartus","Fortunatus"'::text[],
