        'bible-riddles-l31-c1',
        'bible-riddles',
        31,
        1,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DESCRIPTION:
I was an ancient riddle posed to thirty Philistine wedding companions in Timnah: "Out of the eater came something to eat. Out of the strong came something sweet." The companions could not solve me for three days until they threatened the bride with fire to entice her husband. What was the physical origin of this paradoxical riddle?',
        '"Honey in the Lion’s Carcass","Water from the Rock","The Bronze Serpent","Manna from Heaven"'::text[],
        'Honey in the Lion’s Carcass',
        'Samson’s riddle arose when he discovered a swarm of bees and sweet honey inside the carcass of the lion he had killed.',
        'Judges 14:5–18',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Impossible Description","is_typed":false,"clues":["Originated when Samson tore a young lion apart in the vineyards of Timnah.","A swarm of bees and honey were found inside the carcass of the lion.","Samson scraped honey into his hands and ate as he walked."],"hint":"Samson’s riddle based on sweet honey inside a lion’s dead carcass.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Honey in the Lion","Lion and Honey","Samson’s Riddle","Samsons Riddle"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Paradoxes & Impossible Puzzles","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l31-c2',
        'bible-riddles',
        31,
        2,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DESCRIPTION:
I was a deceased prophet whose dry skeletal bones possessed resurrection power even from beyond the grave. When an Israelite burial party was surprised by a band of invading Moabite raiders in the springtime, they hurriedly dumped a dead man’s corpse into my open tomb. As soon as the dead body touched my bones, the man revived, stood up on his feet, and walked out alive! Whose miracle-working bones were these?',
        '"Moses","Elisha","Samuel","Elijah"'::text[],
        'Elisha',
