        'WHAT AM I?
I was a sacred ritual sacrifice in Numbers 19 involving a female bovine without blemish or defect, upon which a yoke had never come. Slaughtered outside the camp before Eleazar the priest, my blood, hide, flesh, and dung were burned completely with cedarwood, hyssop, and scarlet yarn. My ashes were mixed with running water to create the "water for impurity" to cleanse those defiled by touching a corpse; yet paradoxically, the clean priest who burned me became ceremonially unclean until evening. What animal am I?',
        '"The Ram of Consecration","The Passover Lamb","The Scapegoat","The Red Heifer"'::text[],
        'The Red Heifer',
        'The ashes of the red heifer mixed with water purified those defiled by death, yet paradoxically defiled the clean priest who prepared it.',
        'Numbers 19:1–13; Hebrews 9:13',
        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The red heifer (Parah Adumah).","Ashes preserved outside the camp in a clean place.","Cited in Hebrews 9:13 as a type of the blood of Christ purifying the conscience."],"hint":"Flawless red cow burned outside the camp to create cleansing ash-water.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Red Heifer","The Red Cow","Ashes of the Red Heifer"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Paradoxes & Impossible Puzzles","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
