        4,
        'THE EVENT RIDDLE:
During the birth of twin sons to Tamar by Judah in Genesis 38, one baby put out his hand first. The midwife tied a scarlet thread around his wrist, declaring, "This one came out first." However, he drew back his hand, and his twin brother breached the birth canal first, earning a name meaning "Breach." The first baby then came out with the scarlet thread still on his wrist, and was named "Bright" or "Dawn." What are the names of these twin boys?',
        '"Jacob and Esau","Perez and Zerah","Gershom and Eliezer","Ephraim and Manasseh"'::text[],
        'Perez and Zerah',
        'Tamar bore twins Perez and Zerah; Zerah put his hand out first and received the scarlet cord, but Perez breached first to take the birthright.',
        'Genesis 38:27–30; Matthew 1:3',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Event Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Recorded in Genesis 38:27–30.","Perez (the breach) became the ancestor of King David and Jesus Christ (Matthew 1:3).","Zerah was the twin with the scarlet thread."],"hint":"Twin sons of Judah and Tamar where one put out a hand tied with a scarlet thread.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Perez & Zerah","Pharez and Zarah","Zerah and Perez","Perez, Zerah"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Paradoxes & Impossible Puzzles","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
