I was a wealthy, harsh, and ill-mannered Calebite pastoralist from Maon shearing three thousand sheep in Carmel. When David sent ten young men requesting customary hospitality during shearing festival for having protected my shepherds, I insolently replied: "Who is David? Who is the son of Jesse? There are many servants these days who are breaking away from their masters." Enraged, David strapped on his sword with four hundred armed men to annihilate every male in my household. When my wife later told me how close I had come to destruction, my heart died within me and I became like a stone, dying ten days later when the Lord struck me. Who am I?',
        '"Doeg","Nabal","Shimei","Ahithophel"'::text[],
        'Nabal',
        'Nabal was the wealthy fool whose insulting refusal of food to David nearly cost his entire house their lives until Abigail intervened.',
