        32,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a wise woman of the fortified city of Abel of Beth-maacah in northern Israel. When Joab besieged our city with siege ramps and battering rams pursuing the traitor Sheba son of Bichri, I called over the city wall: "Listen! Tell Joab, ‘Come here, that I may speak to you!’" I reminded Joab that our town was a peaceful and faithful mother in Israel, negotiated the preservation of the entire city, and convinced the townsfolk to cut off Sheba’s head and fling it over the wall to Joab, causing him to sound the trumpet and withdraw his troops. Who am I (by my biblical designation)?',
        '"The Wise Woman of Tekoa","The Wise Woman of Abel","Huldah the Prophetess","Abigail"'::text[],
        'The Wise Woman of Abel',
        'The wise woman of Abel of Beth-maacah saved her city from destruction by convincing the citizens to throw Sheba’s severed head over the wall to Joab.',
        '2 Samuel 20:14–22',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["A wise woman of Abel-beth-maacah.","Saved an entire city by negotiating with Joab.","Recorded in 2 Samuel 20:14–22."],"hint":"Wise woman who saved her besieged city by throwing the traitor’s head over the wall.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Wise Woman of Abel","The Wise Woman of Abel-beth-maacah","Wise Woman of Abel-beth-maacah"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Unlikely Interventions & Rescues","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
