        'WHO AM I?
I was a royal princess of Judah, daughter of King Jehoram, sister of King Ahaziah, and wife of Jehoiada the high priest. When the murderous Queen Mother Athaliah arose to butcher all the royal heirs of the house of David, I stole away one-year-old baby Joash from among the slaughtered princes and hid him with his nurse in a bedroom in the temple of the Lord for six years, preserving the messianic line of David from complete extinction. Who am I?',
        '"Jehosheba","Huldah","Maacah","Athaliah"'::text[],
        'Jehosheba',
        'Jehosheba, daughter of King Jehoram, courageously rescued infant Prince Joash from Athaliah’s royal massacre, hiding him in the temple.',
        '2 Kings 11:1–3; 2 Chronicles 22:11–12',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Jehosheba (or Jehoshabeath in 2 Chronicles 22:11).","Wife of Jehoiada the high priest.","Bravery preserved the Davidic lineage unbroken."],"hint":"Princess who hid infant King Joash in the temple for six years from Athaliah.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Jehoshabeath","Josaba"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Unlikely Interventions & Rescues","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
