        32,
        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an anonymous young Israelite girl abducted during a Syrian border raid and taken captive into a foreign land, where I was assigned as a domestic servant to the wife of Naaman, commander of the Syrian army. Witnessing my master’s tragic affliction with leprosy, I did not harbor bitterness or rejoice in his suffering, but boldly testified: "Would that my lord were with the prophet who is in Samaria! He would cure him of his leprosy." My simple testimony set in motion Naaman’s miraculous healing in the Jordan River. Who am I?',
        '"Achsah","The Captive Maid of Israel","The Widow of Zarephath","The Shunammite Woman"'::text[],
        'The Captive Maid of Israel',
        'The unnamed captive Israelite maid showed extraordinary faith and compassion by directing Naaman to Elisha for healing.',
