        32,
        4,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an innkeeper and harlot living in the fortified outer wall of Jericho. When two Hebrew spies sent by Joshua arrived, I hid them under stalks of flax laid out on my flat roof and misled the king’s search party. Having heard how the Lord dried up the Red Sea, I declared: "Yahweh your God, he is God in heaven above and on earth beneath." In return, the spies pledged my household’s safety on condition that I tie a scarlet cord in the window through which I lowered them by a rope. Who am I?',
        '"Rahab","Ruth","Tamar","Deborah"'::text[],
        'Rahab',
        'Rahab the harlot sheltered Joshua’s spies in Jericho, hung the scarlet cord from her window, and was grafted into the royal genealogy of Jesus.',
