        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
When the Apostle Paul was held under armed guard in the Antonia Fortress in Jerusalem, more than forty Jewish conspirators bound themselves under a solemn curse with an oath neither to eat nor to drink until they had killed Paul. However, a young unnamed family member of Paul heard of their ambush, entered the Roman barracks, and reported the plot directly to the tribune Claudius Lysias. Lysias immediately dispatched two hundred soldiers, seventy horsemen, and two hundred spearmen at the third hour of the night to escort Paul safely to Governor Felix in Caesarea. What family relation was this heroic young man to Paul?',
        '"Paul’s Son-in-law","Paul’s Brother","Paul’s Cousin","Paul’s Nephew"'::text[],
        'Paul’s Nephew',
        'Paul’s nephew (his sister’s son) uncovered the assassination plot of the forty conspirators and saved Paul’s life by informing the Roman commander.',
        'Acts 23:12–24',
