        1,
        'WHAT AM I?
I was an ancient legal custom in Israel regarding redemption and exchange to confirm a transaction, famously illustrated in Ruth 4. When a closer kinsman refused to redeem the land of Elimelech and marry Ruth the Moabitess lest he impair his own inheritance, he performed a symbolic act: he pulled off his leather sandal and handed it to Boaz before the ten elders of the town gate as a binding public testimony. What legal custom am I?',
        '"The Removal of the Sandal","The Cutting of the Covenant","The Year of Jubilee","The Cities of Refuge"'::text[],
        'The Removal of the Sandal',
