        '{"riddle_type":"What Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["The law of the kinsman-redeemer (Go’el).","In Deuteronomy 25:9, a brother’s widow pulls off the sandal of a man who refuses levirate marriage and spits in his face.","Symbolized transferring ownership and the right to tread upon the property."],"hint":"Legal custom where a man drew off his shoe to confirm a transaction at the gate.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Removal of the Sandal","Unloosing the Shoe","Removing the Shoe","Sandal Ceremony"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Obscure Legal Situations & Covenants","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
