        'WHAT AM I?
I was an ancient covenant vow described in Numbers 6 taken by a man or woman who consecrated themselves specially to the Lord for a period of time. During the days of separation, three strict prohibitions applied: eating or drinking anything produced by the grapevine (from seeds to skin, including wine and vinegar), letting a razor touch the head, and going near any dead body, even that of a father or mother. What vow am I?',
        '"The Nazirite Vow","The Levirate Vow","The Rechabite Vow","The Priestly Vow"'::text[],
        'The Nazirite Vow',
