When Abraham made his oldest household servant swear an oath to travel back to Mesopotamia to find a wife for his son Isaac, he commanded the servant to place his hand under Abraham’s thigh. Scripture does not name this servant in Genesis 24, but earlier in Genesis 15:2, before Isaac was born, Abraham lamented that his sole heir was a steward from Syria. What was the name of this head servant of Abraham’s household from Damascus?',
