        1,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an obscure biblical king mentioned only in the opening verse of Proverbs 31. My godly mother taught me solemn royal instructions: warning me against wasting strength on women, warning that wine and strong drink cause rulers to pervert justice, and commanding me to open my mouth for the mute and defend the rights of the poor and needy. She concluded by teaching me the celebrated acrostic poem of the virtuous wife (Eshet Chayil). Who am I?',
        '"King Lemuel","King Solomon","King Agur","King Hezekiah"'::text[],
