        'WHO AM I?
I was the author of Proverbs chapter 30, son of Jakeh, whose name means "gatherer." I opened my oracle by confessing my own human ignorance: "Surely I am too stupid to be a man. I have not the understanding of a man." I posed famous theological questions ("Who has ascended to heaven and come down? Who has gathered the wind in his fists? What is his name, and what is his son’s name?"), prayed for neither poverty nor riches, and observed sets of four mysterious things in nature. Who am I?',
        '"Lemuel","Agur","Asaph","Heman"'::text[],
