        'THE EVENT RIDDLE:
During a sleepless night in the royal palace of Susa, King Ahasuerus ordered the book of memorable deeds, the chronicles, to be brought and read before him. The reader happened upon the record where Mordecai had exposed the assassination plot of Bigthana and Teresh. When the king asked what honor or dignity had been bestowed on Mordecai, the servants replied, "Nothing has been done for him." At that exact moment, who walked into the outer court seeking the king’s permission to hang Mordecai on a seventy-five-foot gallows?',
        '"Harbona","Memucan","Hegai","Haman"'::text[],
