        'WHO AM I?
I was the desperate, rejected first king of Israel on the eve of the catastrophic battle of Mount Gilboa. Terrified by the vast Philistine army and receiving no answer from Yahweh by dreams, Urim, or prophets, I disguised myself, put on other garments, and traveled by night with two men to a necromancer (medium) at En-dor, asking her to conjure up the spirit of the deceased prophet Samuel. When an old man wrapped in a robe arose, I bowed to the earth, only to hear Samuel announce my death the following day. Who am I?',
        '"King Saul","King Ahab","King Ahaziah","King Jeroboam"'::text[],
