        1,
        'THE EVENT RIDDLE:
While the Babylonian army was actively besieging Jerusalem and the prophet Jeremiah was locked in the court of the guard, his cousin Hanamel son of Shallum came and said: "Buy my field at Anathoth in the land of Benjamin, for the right of redemption is yours." Jeremiah weighed out seventeen shekels of silver, signed and sealed the deed of purchase before witnesses, and placed both the sealed and open deeds into an earthenware jar to last a long time. What was the profound divine message of this seemingly foolish real estate investment during a siege?',
        '"The Vow of the Rechabites","The Purchase of the Potter’s Field","The Cleansing of the Temple","The Purchase of the Field of Anathoth"'::text[],
        'The Purchase of the Field of Anathoth',
        'Jeremiah purchased a field at Anathoth while imprisoned during the siege as a prophetic guarantee that Israel would return to buy fields again.',
        'Jeremiah 32:6–15, 42–44',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Event Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Jeremiah 32:6–15.","The Lord declared: \"Houses and fields and vineyards shall again be bought in this land.\"","A prophetic pledge that exile would not be permanent and Israel would return."],"hint":"Jeremiah bought a family field in Anathoth during the siege to prove Israel would return.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Buying the Field at Anathoth","Jeremiah’s Field","Field of Anathoth","Purchase of Anathoth"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Forensic Prophetic Dramas","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
