        'bible-riddles',
        35,
        2,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an 8th-century BC prophet of Jerusalem commanded by Yahweh to enact an astonishing, humiliating prophetic street pageant. For three full years, I walked through the streets of Jerusalem "naked and barefoot" as a living sign and portent against Egypt and Cush, symbolizing that the king of Assyria would lead away the captives of Egypt and the exiles of Cush, both young and old, naked and barefoot, with buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt. Who am I?',
        '"Micah","Isaiah","Jeremiah","Ezekiel"'::text[],
        'Isaiah',
        'Isaiah walked naked and barefoot for three years as a prophetic sign of the coming humiliation and captivity of Egypt and Cush by Assyria.',
        'Isaiah 20:1–6',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Amoz.","Also prophesied the Virgin Birth (7:14) and the Suffering Servant (53:1–12).","The dramatic pageant is recorded in Isaiah 20:1–6."],"hint":"Major prophet who walked naked and barefoot for three years as a sign against Egypt.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Prophet Isaiah","Esaias"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Forensic Prophetic Dramas","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
