        'bible-riddles',
        35,
        5,
        'TYPE THE BIBLE BOOK — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
In chapter 18 of this prophetic book, the prophet is directed to go down to the potter’s house. There, he watches the artisan working at his wheel. When the vessel he was making of clay was spoiled in the potter’s hand, he reworked it into another vessel, as seemed good to the potter to do. God then says: "O house of Israel, can I not do with you as this potter has done? Behold, like the clay in the potter’s hand, so are you in my hand." In which Old Testament prophetic book is this famous lesson recorded?',
        '"Ezekiel","Zechariah","Jeremiah","Isaiah"'::text[],
        'Jeremiah',
        'Jeremiah watched the potter rework spoiled clay on the wheel, illustrating God’s sovereign ability to reshape repenting nations.',
        'Jeremiah 18:1–10',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Book","is_typed":true,"clues":["Followed in chapter 19 by the breaking of an earthenware flask in Topheth.","Author was known as the Weeping Prophet.","Cited by Paul in Romans 9:20–21 concerning divine sovereignty."],"hint":"Prophetic book containing the visit to the potter’s house in chapter 18.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Book of Jeremiah","Jer"],"stage":7,"stage_title":"The Difficult Riddles","level_theme":"Forensic Prophetic Dramas","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
