        'bible-riddles',
        36,
        1,
        'WHO AM I?
Do not confuse me with the writing prophet of the same name or the father of John the Baptist. I was the son of Jehoiada the high priest during the reign of King Joash of Judah. When the Spirit of God clothed me, I stood above the people and rebuked the nation for forsaking Yahweh. By order of the king—who forgot the steadfast love my father Jehoiada had shown him—I was stoned to death with stones right in the sacred court of the house of the Lord, dying with the cry: "May the Lord see and avenge!" Jesus explicitly cited my martyrdom in Matthew 23:35. Who am I?',
        '"Uriah the Prophet","Zechariah the Prophet","Zechariah son of Jehoiada","Zechariah father of John"'::text[],
        'Zechariah son of Jehoiada',
        'Zechariah son of Jehoiada was stoned in the temple court by ungrateful King Joash, remembered by Jesus as the climactic Old Testament martyr.',
        '2 Chronicles 24:20–22; Matthew 23:35; Luke 11:51',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Jehoiada the high priest.","Stoned in the temple court by King Joash.","Jesus linked Abel (first martyr) with me (last martyr of the Hebrew canon)."],"hint":"Priest stoned in the temple court by King Joash; cited by Jesus in Matthew 23.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Zechariah","Zechariah ben Jehoiada","Zacharias son of Barachias"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Double Characters & Namesakes","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
