        'bible-riddles',
        36,
        2,
        'WHO AM I?
Do not confuse me with the Apostle Philip from Bethsaida. I was one of the Seven chosen to serve tables in Jerusalem who pioneered the gospel in Samaria with astonishing miracles, casting out unclean spirits and baptizing the magician Simon Magus. Led by an angel to the desert road of Gaza, I joined an Ethiopian official’s chariot, preached Jesus from Isaiah 53, and baptized him in water before being snatched away by the Spirit to Azotus. Who am I?',
        '"Philip the Evangelist","Stephen","Barnabas","Philip the Apostle"'::text[],
        'Philip the Evangelist',
        'Philip the Evangelist (one of the Seven) evangelized Samaria and the Ethiopian eunuch, distinct from Philip the Apostle.',
        'Acts 6:5; 8:4–40; 21:8–9',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Known specifically as Philip the Evangelist.","Hosted Paul in Caesarea years later with four unmarried daughters who prophesied (Acts 21:8–9).","One of the seven deacons of Acts 6."],"hint":"Deacon and evangelist who preached in Samaria and baptized the Ethiopian eunuch.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Philip the Deacon","Philip","Evangelist Philip"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Double Characters & Namesakes","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
