        'bible-riddles',
        36,
        3,
        'WHO AM I?
Do not confuse me with the James who authored the New Testament Epistle or James the brother of Jesus. I was a Galilean fisherman, son of Zebedee and brother of John, whom Jesus nicknamed Boanerges ("Sons of Thunder"). I was part of Jesus’ intimate inner circle on the Mount of Transfiguration, at the raising of Jairus’ daughter, and in Gethsemane. Under King Herod Agrippa I in Acts 12, I became the very first of the Twelve Apostles to be martyred, executed by the sword in Jerusalem. Who am I?',
        '"James the Lord’s Brother","James son of Alphaeus","James son of Zebedee","John the Apostle"'::text[],
        'James son of Zebedee',
        'James son of Zebedee (brother of John) was the first apostle martyred, beheaded by Herod Agrippa I in Acts 12.',
        'Matthew 4:21; Mark 3:17; Acts 12:1–2',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Zebedee, brother of the Apostle John.","Mother asked that my brother and I sit at Jesus’ right and left hands in His kingdom.","Beheaded by Herod Agrippa I around 44 AD (Acts 12:2)."],"hint":"Son of Zebedee and brother of John; the first apostle martyred by the sword.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["James the Apostle","James the Son of Zebedee","James the Greater"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Double Characters & Namesakes","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
