        'bible-riddles',
        36,
        4,
        'WHO AM I?
Do not confuse me with Simon Peter or Simon the Pharisee. I was one of the Twelve Apostles whose surname was the Zealot (or the Cananaean in Aramaic), reflecting my passionate former affiliation with the fiercely anti-Roman Jewish nationalist resistance movement. Remarkably, Jesus called me into the apostolic band to live and minister alongside Matthew, a former tax collector who had collected taxes for the Roman Empire! Who am I?',
        '"Simon the Magician","Simon the Zealot","Simon of Cyrene","Simon Peter"'::text[],
        'Simon the Zealot',
        'Simon the Zealot was the apostle from the Jewish patriotic faction who served alongside former Roman tax collector Matthew.',
        'Matthew 10:4; Mark 3:18; Luke 6:15; Acts 1:13',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Listed in Luke 6:15 and Acts 1:13 as \"Simon who was called the Zealot.\"","One of the Twelve Apostles.","Aramaic nickname \"Cananaean\" derives from qan’ana (zealous)."],"hint":"Apostle nicknamed the Zealot (or Cananaean) who served alongside Matthew.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Simon the Cananaean","Simon the Canaanite","Simon the Zealot/Cananaean"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Double Characters & Namesakes","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
