        36,
        5,
        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
Do not confuse me with King Saul of Israel who fell on his sword on Mount Gilboa. I was born in Tarsus of Cilicia, circumcised on the eighth day, of the people of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews; as to the law, a Pharisee; as to zeal, a persecutor of the church. I guarded the coats of those who stoned Stephen and breathed out threats and murder against the disciples of the Lord until a blinding light struck me down on the road to Damascus. What was my original Hebrew name before I was known universally as the Apostle Paul?',
        '"Saul","Shaul","Paul","Saul of Tarsus"'::text[],
        'Saul of Tarsus',
        'Saul of Tarsus, named after the Benjamite king Saul, was the fierce Pharisaic persecutor who became the Apostle Paul.',
        'Acts 7:58; 8:1–3; 9:1–19; Philippians 3:4–6',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["Shared the same tribe (Benjamin) as Israel’s first king Saul.","Studied at the feet of Gamaliel in Jerusalem.","Jesus addressed me twice by this name: \"Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me?\""],"hint":"Original Hebrew name of the Apostle Paul from the tribe of Benjamin.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Saul","Shaul","Saul of Tarsus (Paul)"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Double Characters & Namesakes","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
