        'bible-riddles',
        37,
        1,
        'THE IMPOSSIBLE DESCRIPTION:
Be careful not to confuse our two kingdoms: During the divided monarchy, two contemporary kings sharing the exact same name ruled at the same time—one over the northern kingdom of Israel (son of Ahab and Jezebel) and one over the southern kingdom of Judah (son of Jehoshaphat who married Ahab’s daughter Athaliah). What is this shared royal name?',
        '"Jehoahaz","Jehoram / Joram","Ahaziah","Joash"'::text[],
        'Jehoram / Joram',
        'Jehoram (Joram) was the identical name shared simultaneously by the king of Israel (Ahab’s son) and the king of Judah (Jehoshaphat’s son).',
        '2 Kings 1:17; 3:1; 8:16–25; 2 Chronicles 21:1–20',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Impossible Description","is_typed":false,"clues":["Both kings were named Jehoram (or Joram).","Jehoram of Israel was struck down by Jehu’s arrow at the vineyard of Naboth.","Jehoram of Judah died of an incurable disease of the bowels and departed with no one’s regret (2 Chronicles 21:18–20)."],"hint":"Shared name of two contemporary kings ruling over Judah and Israel simultaneously.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Jehoram","Joram","Jehoram or Joram"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Misleading Kings & Usurpers","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
