(
        'bible-riddles-l37-c2',
        'bible-riddles',
        37,
        2,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a chariot commander of King Elah of Israel who conspired against my royal master. While the king was getting drunk in the house of Arza in Tirzah, I entered, struck him down, and assassinated him, exterminating every single male of the house of Baasha. However, my reign was the shortest in the history of northern Israel—lasting only seven days! When the army made Omri king and besieged Tirzah, I retreated into the citadel of the royal palace, set the palace on fire over me, and burned to death. Who am I?',
        '"Zimri","Shallum","Baasha","Tibni"'::text[],
        'Zimri',
        'Zimri assassinated King Elah and reigned only seven days in Tirzah before committing suicide by burning the royal palace over himself.',
        '1 Kings 16:9–20; 2 Kings 9:31',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Reigned exactly seven days in Tirzah.","Jezebel later taunted Jehu: \"Is it peace, you Zimri, murderer of your master?\" (2 Kings 9:31).","Died in his own palace inferno."],"hint":"King of Israel who reigned only seven days and burned the palace over himself.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["King Zimri"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Misleading Kings & Usurpers","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
