(
        'bible-riddles-l37-c3',
        'bible-riddles',
        37,
        3,
        'WHO AM I?
I was a usurper, son of Jabesh, who conspired against King Zechariah (the last king of the dynasty of Jehu) and struck him down in public before the people in Samaria, bringing an end to Jehu’s four-generation dynasty. My reign over northern Israel lasted for exactly one full month. Menahem son of Gadi marched from Tirzah to Samaria, assassinated me, and seized the throne. Who am I?',
        '"Pekah","Zimri","Shallum","Pekahiah"'::text[],
        'Shallum',
        'Shallum son of Jabesh assassinated Zechariah of the house of Jehu and reigned only one full month before Menahem killed him.',
        '2 Kings 15:10–15',
        '{"riddle_type":"Who Am I?","is_typed":false,"clues":["Reigned one month in Samaria in 752 BC.","Son of Jabesh.","Recorded in 2 Kings 15:10–15."],"hint":"King of northern Israel who reigned for exactly one month.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Shallum son of Jabesh","Sellum"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Misleading Kings & Usurpers","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l37-c4',
        'bible-riddles',
        37,
        4,
        'THE THREE-CLUE RIDDLE:
Clue 1: I was the last reigning king of the northern ten-tribe kingdom of Israel (Samaria).
Clue 2: I conspired against Pekah son of Remaliah and assassinated him, reigning nine years.
Clue 3: When I stopped paying annual tribute to Shalmaneser king of Assyria and sent envoys to So, king of Egypt, the Assyrian king besieged Samaria for three years, captured the city, put me in prison bound in chains, and carried Israel into permanent exile to Assyria. Who am I?',
        '"Ahaz","Pekah","Menahem","Hoshea"'::text[],
        'Hoshea',
        'Hoshea was the nineteenth and final king of northern Israel whose alliance with Egypt led to the Assyrian siege and exile of the ten tribes.',
        '2 Kings 15:30; 17:1–6',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Three-Clue Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Elah.","Last monarch of the northern kingdom before its destruction in 722 BC.","The book of 2 Kings 17 details his downfall."],"hint":"Last king of the northern kingdom of Israel before the Assyrian exile.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Hoshea son of Elah","Osee"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Misleading Kings & Usurpers","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
