        'bible-riddles',
        37,
        5,
        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
I was an ambitious, third son of King David, born to Haggith in Hebron. After Absalom’s death, as David grew decrepit in his old age, I exalted myself, saying, "I will be king." I prepared chariots, horsemen, and fifty men to run before me, winning over Joab the army commander and Abiathar the high priest. I threw a royal coronation feast at the Serpent’s Stone (En-rogel). However, Nathan the prophet and Bathsheba intervened before David, who ordered Solomon to be anointed on the royal mule at Gihon. Terrified by the shouts, my guests fled, and I ran to the altar in the sanctuary to cling to its horns for mercy. Who am I?',
        '"Absalom","Shephatiah","Adonijah","Amnon"'::text[],
        'Adonijah',
        'Adonijah attempted to usurp David’s throne before Solomon’s coronation, but his coup collapsed and he clung to the altar horns.',
        '1 Kings 1:5–53; 2:13–25',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["David’s handsome son born after Absalom.","Clung to the horns of the altar to escape execution.","Later executed by Benaiah when he requested Abishag the Shunammite as wife."],"hint":"David’s handsome son who attempted a royal coup at En-rogel before Solomon.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Adonijah son of Haggith","Adonias"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Misleading Kings & Usurpers","difficulty":"hard","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
