        'bible-riddles',
        38,
        1,
        'THE EVENT RIDDLE:
When King David attempted to bring the Ark of the Covenant from Kiriath-jearim to Jerusalem on a new wooden ox cart, the oxen stumbled at the threshing floor of Nacon (Chidon). A man named [...] put out his hand to steady the Ark of God, and the anger of the Lord was kindled against him, and God struck him down dead on the spot for his irreverence beside the Ark. David was angry and terrified, naming the place Perez-uzzah. Who was the man struck dead for touching the Ark?',
        '"Ahio","Uzzah","Eleazar","Obed-edom"'::text[],
        'Uzzah',
        'Uzzah was struck dead for touching the Ark of God when the oxen stumbled, demonstrating God’s strict holiness regarding sacred items.',
        '2 Samuel 6:3–11; 1 Chronicles 13:7–14; Numbers 4:15',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Event Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Son of Abinadab, brother of Ahio.","Violated the law that only Kohathites could carry the Ark using golden poles, and that even they must not touch holy things lest they die (Numbers 4:15).","The Ark was detoured to the house of Obed-edom the Gittite for three months."],"hint":"Man struck dead by God for touching the Ark to steady it when the oxen stumbled.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Uzza"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Deceptive Theological & Narrative Traps","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
