        'bible-riddles',
        38,
        2,
        'TYPE TWO ANSWERS:
We were the two oldest sons of Aaron the high priest who were consecrated as priests in the wilderness sanctuary. In Leviticus 10, right after God’s glory fell on the altar, we each took our censers, put fire in them, laid incense on them, and offered "unauthorized fire" (strange fire) before the Lord, which God had not commanded. Fire came out from before the Lord and instantly consumed both of us, and we died before the Lord. What are our two biblical names?',
        '"Nadab and Abihu","Eleazar and Ithamar","Hophni and Phinehas","Korah and Dathan"'::text[],
        'Nadab and Abihu',
        'Nadab and Abihu were Aaron’s sons consumed by fire from the Lord for offering unauthorized (strange) fire on the altar.',
        'Leviticus 10:1–7; Numbers 3:4; 26:61',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type Two Answers","is_typed":true,"clues":["Oldest sons of Aaron; brothers of Eleazar and Ithamar.","Moses said to Aaron: \"This is what the Lord has said: ‘Among those who are near me I will be sanctified.’\" And Aaron held his peace.","Carried outside the camp in their tunics by Mishael and Elzaphan."],"hint":"Two sons of Aaron struck down by fire for offering strange fire in the sanctuary.","testament":"Old Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Nadab & Abihu","Abihu and Nadab","Nadab, Abihu"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Deceptive Theological & Narrative Traps","difficulty":"medium","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l38-c3',
        'bible-riddles',
        38,
        3,
        'THE EVENT RIDDLE:
In Acts 5, a husband and wife in the early church sold a piece of property and brought a portion of the proceeds to the Apostles’ feet, while secretly keeping back part of the price with full mutual conspiracy, pretending to give all. Peter confronted the husband: "Why has Satan filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit?" Hearing these words, the man fell down dead. Three hours later, his unaware wife repeated the lie and dropped dead instantly, being buried beside her husband. What are their two names?',
        '"Ananias and Sapphira","Aquila and Priscilla","Zacharias and Elizabeth","Simon and Rhoda"'::text[],
        'Ananias and Sapphira',
        'Ananias and Sapphira fell down dead for lying to the Holy Spirit about their financial offering in the early Jerusalem church.',
        'Acts 5:1–11',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Event Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Peter told the wife: \"How is it that you have agreed together to test the Spirit of the Lord?\"","Young men carried them out and buried them.","Great fear fell upon the entire church and all who heard."],"hint":"Husband and wife struck dead in Acts 5 for lying to the Holy Spirit about land money.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Ananias & Sapphira","Sapphira and Ananias","Ananias, Sapphira"],"stage":8,"stage_title":"The Scripture Trap","level_theme":"Deceptive Theological & Narrative Traps","difficulty":"easy","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l38-c4',
        'bible-riddles',
        38,
        4,
        'WHO AM I?
I was an unnamed man of God from Judah who came to Bethel by the word of the Lord, cried out against Jeroboam’s golden calf altar, and withered the king’s outstretched arm. God strictly commanded me: "You shall neither eat bread nor drink water nor return by the way that you came." However, an old prophet of Bethel pursued me on a donkey and lied, saying an angel had instructed him to bring me home to eat. I believed his lie and ate bread in his house; on my journey home, a lion met me on the road and killed me, leaving my body lying in the road beside the standing donkey and lion. Who am I (by my biblical title)?',
        '"Micaiah son of Imlah","Jehu son of Hanani","Ahijah the Shilonite","The Man of God from Judah"'::text[],
        'The Man of God from Judah',
