        'WHAT AM I?
God challenged Job in chapter 40 to behold me, an enormous land creature "which I made as I made you." I eat grass like an ox; my strength is in my loins and my power in the muscles of my belly; I move my tail stiff like a cedar; my bones are tubes of bronze, my limbs like bars of iron. I lie under the lotus plants in the covert of reeds, and even if a river becomes turbulent and rises to my mouth, I am confident. What creature am I?',
