        4,
        'FORENSIC MONOLOGUE:
"I was a foreign Philistine warrior from Gath who had arrived in Jerusalem with six hundred soldiers only yesterday. When David was fleeing into the wilderness from Absalom and urged me to return to my own country rather than wander with an exile, I swore a sacred oath by Yahweh: ‘As the Lord lives, and as my lord the king lives, wherever my lord the king shall be, whether for death or for life, there also will your servant be.’ David was so moved that he appointed me commander of one-third of his entire royal army in the decisive battle of the forest of Ephraim." Who am I?',
