        'TYPE THE NAME — MINI-BOSS RIDDLE:
FORENSIC MONOLOGUE:
"I was David’s close companion and counselor who met the weeping king on the crest of the Mount of Olives with my coat torn and dirt on my head. David told me that if I accompanied him, I would be a burden, but if I returned to Jerusalem, I could infiltrate Absalom’s court and defeat the brilliant counsel of Ahithophel. I feigned loyalty to Absalom, flatteringly defeated Ahithophel’s plan of an immediate night attack by recommending a vast national levy led by Absalom in person, and sent secret intelligence to David through the priests Zadok and Abiathar. When Ahithophel saw his advice was rejected, he went home and hanged himself." Who am I?',
