        'TYPE TWO ANSWERS:
In 2 Timothy 3:8, the Apostle Paul exposes false teachers in the last days by comparing them to two ancient Egyptian court sorcerers who opposed Moses before Pharaoh: "Just as [...] and [...] opposed Moses, so these men also oppose the truth, men corrupted in mind and disqualified regarding the faith." Remarkably, these two specific names appear nowhere in the Old Testament text itself! What are the names of these two Egyptian magicians preserved by Jewish tradition and canonized by Paul?',
