I was a colossal circular bronze water reservoir cast by master metalworker Hiram of Tyre for Solomon’s Temple. Measuring fifteen feet in diameter, seven and a half feet deep, and forty-five feet in circumference, with a brim carved like a lily blossom, I held over twelve thousand gallons of water for priestly ablutions. I rested upon the backs of twelve bronze oxen standing in groups of three facing north, west, south, and east, with all their hindquarters directed inward. What am I called in Scripture?',
