When Philip found me and announced, "We have found him of whom Moses in the Law and also the prophets wrote, Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph," I responded skeptically: "Can anything good come out of Nazareth?" When Jesus saw me approaching, He declared: "Behold, an Israelite indeed, in whom there is no deceit!" Astonished, I asked how He knew me, and He answered: "Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you." I immediately confessed: "Rabbi, you are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!" Who am I?',
