        'WHO AM I?
I am the Canaanite woman who married Er, the wicked firstborn son of Judah. When Er died under God’s judgment, Judah gave me to his second son Onan according to levirate duty, but Onan refused to father heirs and was also slain by the Lord. Denied the third son Shelah, I disguised myself as a veiled cult prostitute at the entrance to Enaim on the road to Timnah, where Judah took my pledge of his signet, cord, and staff. When sentenced to be burned for prostitution three months later, I sent out the items: "By the man to whom these belong, I am pregnant." Judah acknowledged: "She is more righteous than I." Who am I?',
        '"Rahab","Bathsheba","Ruth","Tamar"'::text[],
