        'THE BIBLICAL RELATIONSHIP RIDDLE:
In Matthew’s genealogy of Jesus (chapter 1), only five women are specifically mentioned by name or relationship. Four are Tamar, Rahab, Ruth, and Mary. The fifth woman is deliberately not mentioned by her personal name, but identified strictly through her tragic former marriage: "And David was the father of Solomon by [...]." Who was this fifth woman?',
