        45,
        4,
        'WHO AM I?
I was the tragic king of Judah, also known as Coniah and Jeconiah, who reigned for only three months and ten days before surrendering to Nebuchadnezzar in 597 BC and being carried captive to Babylon. In Jeremiah 22:30, God pronounced a terrifying bloodline curse upon me: "Write this man down as childless, a man who shall not succeed in his days, for none of his offspring shall succeed in sitting on the throne of David and ruling again in Judah." Because of this royal curse, Jesus could not be the biological son of Joseph (who descended from me in Matthew 1:11–12), but claimed the physical Davidic throne through Mary via David’s son Nathan! Who am I?',
