(
        'bible-riddles-l50-c2',
        'bible-riddles',
        50,
        2,
        'THE GRAND MASTER RIDDLE — 2 OF 5:
"In the opening chapter of Revelation, I appeared to the Apostle John in exile on the island of Patmos on the Lord’s Day. Clothed with a long robe and with a golden sash around my chest, my head and hairs were white like wool, white as snow; my eyes were like a flame of fire, my feet like burnished bronze refined in a furnace, my voice like the roar of many waters, and out of my mouth came a sharp two-edged sword. When John saw me, he fell at my feet as though dead. I laid my right hand on him, saying: ‘Fear not; I am the first and the last, and the living one. I died, and behold I am alive forevermore, and I have the keys of Death and Hades.’" What title did I take in this vision?',
        '"The Archangel Michael","The Ancient of Days","The Angel of the Covenant","The Son of Man"'::text[],
        'The Son of Man',
        'The glorified Christ revealed Himself to John on Patmos as the Son of Man holding the keys of Death and Hades.',
        'Revelation 1:12–18; Daniel 7:13',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Revelation 1:12–18.","Echoes Daniel 7:13–14.","Identified as \"one like a son of man.\""],"hint":"The glorified Christ who appeared to John on Patmos holding the keys of Death and Hades.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Son of Man","One like a son of man","The Glorified Christ"],"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","level_theme":"The Grand Master Final Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l50-c3',
        'bible-riddles',
        50,
        3,
        'THE GRAND MASTER RIDDLE — 3 OF 5:
"In Revelation 21–22, I am the holy city, the New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband. I have the glory of God, radiance like a most rare jewel, a great high wall with twelve gates guarded by twelve angels with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel inscribed, and twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb. My streets are pure gold transparent like glass, I have no temple for the Lord God the Almighty and the Lamb are my temple, and the river of the water of life flows from the throne down the middle of my street with the tree of life bearing twelve kinds of fruit." What am I designated as in Revelation 21:9?',
        '"The Garden of Eden","The Earthly Jerusalem","The Bride, the Wife of the Lamb","Solomon’s Temple"'::text[],
        'The Bride, the Wife of the Lamb',
        'The New Jerusalem is explicitly introduced in Revelation 21:9 as "the Bride, the wife of the Lamb," the radiant eternal dwelling of God with His people.',
        'Revelation 21:1–27; 22:1–5',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["The Bride, the wife of the Lamb.","The New Jerusalem / Heavenly City.","The eternal dwelling of God with redeemed humanity."],"hint":"The New Jerusalem described as a bride adorned for her husband.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Bride of Christ","The New Jerusalem","The Wife of the Lamb","New Jerusalem"],"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","level_theme":"The Grand Master Final Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
        'bible-riddles-l50-c4',
        'bible-riddles',
        50,
        4,
        'THE GRAND MASTER RIDDLE — 4 OF 5:
"In Revelation 19:11–16, heaven stands open and I appear riding upon a white horse. I am called Faithful and True, and in righteousness I judge and make war. My eyes are like a flame of fire, and on my head are many diadems; I am clothed in a robe dipped in blood, and the armies of heaven arrayed in fine linen, white and pure, follow me on white horses. From my mouth comes a sharp sword to strike down the nations, and I tread the winepress of the fury of the wrath of God the Almighty. On my robe and on my thigh I have a name written: ‘KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.’ What is the title given to me in verse 13 as the eternal revelation of God?"',
        '"The Word of God","The King of Glory","The Ancient of Days","The Prince of Peace"'::text[],
        'The Word of God',
        'The rider on the white horse in Revelation 19:13 is named "The Word of God," returning in triumph as King of Kings and Lord of Lords.',
        'Revelation 19:11–16; John 1:1, 14',
        '{"riddle_type":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","is_typed":false,"clues":["Revelation 19:13.","Echoes John 1:1 (\"In the beginning was the Word...\").","Designated: \"The Word of God.\""],"hint":"Title given to the conquering rider on the white horse in Revelation 19:13.","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["Word of God","Logos of God","The Logos"],"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","level_theme":"The Grand Master Final Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":30,"curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
(
