        'bible-riddles',
        50,
        5,
        'THE GRAND MASTER RIDDLE — 5 OF 5 (FINAL BOSS):
In the closing chapter of the entire Bible (Revelation 22:16), Jesus sends His angel to testify these things to the churches and proclaims His climactic twofold messianic title, uniting His eternal divine pre-existence as Creator with His human Davidic royalty, followed by His dawn-bringing promise: "I, Jesus, have sent my angel to testify to you these things for the churches. I am the root and the offspring of David, the [...]." What is this glorious three-word dawn title proclaimed by Jesus in Revelation 22:16?',
        '"Bright and Morning Star","Sun of Righteousness","Light of the World","Alpha and Omega"'::text[],
        'Bright and Morning Star',
        'Jesus proclaims Himself "the root and the offspring of David, the bright and morning star" in Revelation 22:16, concluding the canon of Holy Scripture.',
        'Revelation 22:16',
        '{"riddle_type":"Type the Name","is_typed":true,"clues":["Revelation 22:16.","Followed by: \"The Spirit and the Bride say, ‘Come.’\"","Symbolizes the eternal dawn that banishes darkness forever."],"hint":"Glorious dawn title of Jesus in Revelation 22:16: \"the bright and...\"","testament":"New Testament","acceptedAlternatives":["The Bright and Morning Star","Bright Morning Star","The Morning Star","Morning Star"],"stage":10,"stage_title":"The Ultimate Bible Riddle","level_theme":"The Grand Master Final Boss","difficulty":"master","timerSeconds":25,"curated":true}'::jsonb
