        'bible-chain-challenge',
        20,
        1,
        'DEEP SCRIPTURE STUDY: In 1 Samuel 4:3-11, Israel took the Ark of the Covenant from Shiloh into battle against the Philistines at Ebenezer/Aphek. When the Philistines captured the Ark, to which Philistine city and temple did they first bring it?',
        '"Ekron","Gaza","Gath","Ashdod (Temple of Dagon)"'::text[],
        'Ashdod (Temple of Dagon)',
        'Ark taken at Aphek → Brought to Ashdod into the temple of Dagon → Set by Dagon → Next morning Dagon fallen on his face → Next morning head and both hands cut off upon the threshold (1 Samuel 5:1-5).',
        '1 Samuel 5:1-5',
        '{"stage":4,"stage_title":"Places and Journeys","level_title":"Deep Scripture Study: The Ark’s Journey","chain_type":"name_to_event","chain_nodes":["Shiloh tabernacle","Captured at Aphek","Dagon’s hands cut off","?"],"is_typed":false,"difficulty":"Easy","timerSeconds":90,"points":100,"testament":"Old Testament","dossier":"1 Samuel 4–6 records the capture of the Ark by the Philistines and its terrifying judgment upon the five Philistine lords.","study_mode":true,"hint1":"The first of the five Philistine cities to receive the Ark.","hint2":"1 Samuel 5:1: \"And the Philistines took the ark of God, and brought it from Ebenezer unto Ashdod.\"","curated":true}'::jsonb
