(
        'bible-chain-challenge-l41-c1',
        'bible-chain-challenge',
        41,
        1,
        'Follow the Ethiopian rescuer chain: In Jeremiah 38, the princes of Judah cast prophet Jeremiah into the dungeon of Malchiah where he sank in the mire. Which royal Ethiopian eunuch obtained permission from King Zedekiah to rescue Jeremiah using thirty men and old cast clouts and rotten rags?',
        '"Pashur","Seraiah","Gedaliah","Ebed-melech"'::text[],
        'Ebed-melech',
        'Jeremiah in miry dungeon → Ebed-melech the Ethiopian appeals to King Zedekiah at the gate of Benjamin → Uses 30 men and old cords with rotten rags under armholes to draw Jeremiah up → God promises Ebed-melech his life for a prey because he put his trust in the LORD (Jeremiah 38:7-13; 39:15-18).',
        'Jeremiah 38:7-13; 39:15-18',
        '{"stage":9,"stage_title":"Expert Chain Challenge","level_title":"Obscure Old Testament Figures","chain_type":"character_chain","chain_nodes":["Miry dungeon of Malchiah","Old rags under armholes","Promise of life for a prey","?"],"is_typed":false,"difficulty":"Difficult","timerSeconds":75,"points":150,"testament":"Old Testament","hint1":"His name means \"servant of the king\".","hint2":"Jeremiah 38:7: \"Now when Ebed-melech the Ethiopian, one of the eunuchs which was in the king’s house, heard that they had put Jeremiah in the dungeon...\"","curated":true}'::jsonb
      ),
